window.FWN_GODLY_EMPRESS_DOCTOR_CHAPTERS=(window.FWN_GODLY_EMPRESS_DOCTOR_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":1401,"title":"Chapter 1401 - Sister-In-Law, That Hurts","paragraphs":["Seeing that Feng Wu wouldn’t let go of Mu the Sixth, Song Yichen rushed over and lashed out at Feng Wu. “Feng Wu, do you have a death wish?! Do you know who this is? He’s Young Lord Mu, the son of Lord Mu! How dare you disrespect him like this?!”","Members of the Song family were lower-ranking officials than those of the Mu family. To be more precise, Song Yichen’s family had to depend on the Mu family most of the time. Therefore, he had always shown Mu the Sixth great respect.","Behind him, apart from Shu Yunruo, all the other teenagers were also giving Feng Wu odd looks.","How arrogant did Feng Wu have to be to treat the son of a lord like that? Mu the Sixth could be very terrifying when he was angry!","But —","To their surprise, Mu the Sixth wasn’t mad. Instead, he smiled obsequiously at Feng Wu.","Pinching his ear, Feng Wu asked, “Why did you run away from me?”","Mu the Sixth said, “I didn’t. I really didn’t.”","Feng Wu twisted his ear. “You didn’t? You disappeared as soon as you saw me, didn’t you?!”","Mu the Sixth almost jumped to his feet. “My lady, please go easy on me... Ssss! That hurts!”","Feng Wu grunted. “So, you can still feel pain. I thought you’re immune to it. Where’s Feng Xun now? Speak!”","Seeing the way Feng Wu interacted with Mu the Sixth, the onlookers sucked in their breaths.","Holy shit —","Were they seeing things?","She was the neglected daughter of the Feng family, while he was the favorite son of a lord. However, Feng Wu showed no respect toward the young lord!","“Miss Feng, how can you do that? You —”","Song Yichen was still trying to speak up for Mu the Sixth, but as soon as he spoke, Feng Wu put more pressure on Mu the Sixth’s ear, and the latter stopped Song Yichen in vexation.","“Song Yichen! Shut the f**k up!”","Song Yichen was dumbfounded. He was speaking up for the young lord, but why was he the one getting yelled at?","“Brother Mu, this Feng Wu is such a shrew! Let me get rid of her for you.”","Song Yichen reached for Feng Wu’s shoulder as he spoke.","Mu the Sixth’s eyes flickered, and his pupils contracted. He then shouted, “Stop! How dare you try to touch her?!”","“Huh?” Song Yichen jumped and looked at Mu the Sixth in bewilderment.","Mu the Sixth was so vexed. He had mistaken Feng Wu for Feng Xun’s girlfriend at first, but as it turned out, the crown prince was the suitor... Anyone who tried to touch her would have their hands snapped off!","Meanwhile, Feng Wu had already let go of Mu the Sixth’s ear.","His left ear glowed red, which showed how hard Feng Wu had pinched it.","“Mu the Sixth, she’s just a common girl. How can you be so afraid of her?” Song Yichen tried to drive a wedge between the two people.","To his surprise, his “Brother Mu” raised a hand and slapped him!","Smack!","The crisp sound baffled everyone.","Mu the Sixth glared at Song Yichen. “I’m warning you. I can live with you disrespecting me, but if you dare say one harsh word about my sister-in-law, I’ll chop you into little pieces!”","W- What was that about... Song Yichen was befuddled.","Feng Wu flared up and kicked Mu the Sixth. “What are you talking about? I’m not your sister-in-law!”","Mu the Sixth was like a furious god when he yelled at Song Yichen, but when he turned back to Feng Wu, he behaved like a naughty monkey.","“Ouch! Sister-in-law, that hurts —”","Mu the Sixth whined, stumbled back, then turned to flee."]},{"number":1402,"title":"Chapter 1402 - Feng Xun’s Teasing","paragraphs":["Feng Wu was furious.","“Mu the Sixth! Stop right there!” Resting her hands on her waist, Feng Wu shouted after Mu the Sixth. “Take another step, I dare you!”","“Ahem —”","Mu the Sixth raised his hands over his head and turned around. “Fine, fine. I won’t run. Sister-in-law, don’t be mad.”","Feng Wu wanted to kick him. “I’m not your sister-in-law!”","“Ahem... alright, alright, Sister-in-law, you’re not my sister-in-law... I mean, you’re not my sister-in-law at all! It’s all my fault. Please don’t be mad, Sister-in-law. Brother Feng would kill me!”","Brother Feng had given him specific instructions, telling him that the crown prince was fond of Feng Wu and the girl wasn’t someone he should offend.","Seeing that the teenager wouldn’t stop talking nonsense, Feng Wu gave up trying to correct him and only asked, “Where’s Feng Xun? Take me to him.”","Feng Xun? Song Yichen and the others exchanged bewildered looks and wondered if there really was something going on between Feng Wu and Young Lord Feng.","If that was the case, Feng Wu was going to marry her way up the social ladder!","At that thought, many people eyed Feng Wu enviously and some were even overwhelmed with jealousy.","Song Yichen and the others looked at one another, feeling perplexed.","Young Lord Feng had indeed been present when Feng Wu took the Dragon’s Gate challenge the other day.","But they had thought that the young lord was there for the bet. Had he gone for Feng Wu?","Song Yichen and the others wouldn’t believe it. They couldn’t accept the fact that Feng Wu had befriended an influential man like Young Lord Feng.","Just then —","“Why, isn’t it little Feng Wu?”","The crowd heard a voice.","Feng Wu turned around to see none other than Feng Xun himself.","Feng Wu threw a dirty look at Feng Xun and retorted, “Oh my, isn’t it Young Lord Feng? To what do I owe this honor?”","Song Yichen was relieved; the two of them couldn’t be familiar with each other, or else they wouldn’t be talking to each other that way.","However, Feng Xun’s reply surprised everyone.","Feng Wu crossed her arms over her chest and sneered at Feng Xun in an arrogant way, while Feng Xun walked up to her with a smile. “Hey, are you mad at me?”","Feng Wu only rolled her eyes at him and wouldn’t speak.","Feng Xun poked Feng Wu in the arm. “Hey, little Feng Wu, have I upset you?”","Was Feng Wu mad at Feng Xun? Actually, she was mad at the system for making her give Jun Linyuan flowers in public. The task made Feng Wu feel so awkward.","Song Yichen and the others felt their hearts sink when they saw Feng Xun’s demeanor.","They had thought that Feng Xun had only shown up at the Dragon’s Gate as a happy onlooker, but as it turned out, he had been there to support Feng Wu!","They then recalled how Mu the Sixth had been addressing Feng Wu as his “sister-in-law”... Could it be...","At that thought, Song Yichen felt as though a bucket of cold water had been poured over his head.","“If Feng Wu tells Young Lord Feng that I picked on her...” Song Yichen was scared by that thought.","Luckily, Feng Wu was too busy to remember what he did.","Right now, she was glaring at Feng Xun and said, “Hey, I have a question for you.”","Feng Xun asked, “What?”","Feng Wu sounded awkward when she asked, “Where’s Jun Linyuan?”","Feng Xun’s eyes flickered. “Boss Jun, is it...” Looking down, he saw the immortal flower bouquet Feng Wu was holding and was thrilled!","He made himself look surprised when he said, “Little Feng Wu, what a fresh bunch of immortal flowers! There’s still dew on the petals!”"]},{"number":1403,"title":"Chapter 1403 - Are Her Flowers for His Royal Highness?","paragraphs":["Feng Wu rolled her eyes at him. “That’s hardly the point here!”","She had just bought the bouquet off some random passerby and couldn’t care less about the dew.","Feng Xun went on teasing her. “Wait, didn’t you refuse my invitation repeatedly yesterday? Why are you here now? Who are those flowers for?”","Seeing the teasing look in Feng Xun’s eyes, Feng Wu felt like smacking him on the head.","She glared at Feng Xun. “Just tell me where Jun Linyuan is.”","Although she still had quite a lot of time left, what if Jun Linyuan was difficult to find? Or what if something happened, and she was delayed again?”","“You’re looking for Boss Jun.” Rubbing his nose, Feng Xun looked at Feng Wu in amusement. “And are those flowers for him?”","Feng Wu kicked him. “Just tell me where he is!”","“So —” Feng Xun gave her a meaningful look. “You wouldn’t even consider coming here yesterday, but now, you’re giving Boss Jun flowers... Feng Wu, you’re playing hard to get, aren’t you?”","“Feng! Xun!” Feng Wu raised her fist.","“Please don’t hit me —” Feng Xun immediately surrendered. “If you’re so eager to see Boss Jun, of course I won’t stop you. Come, I’ll take you to him.”","Eager to see him... Feng Wu hated the way Feng Xun put it.","But what could she say? She had no choice but to follow him.","Feng Xun was being very naughty. He wouldn’t stop teasing Feng Wu as they walked, and he didn’t exactly try to keep his voice down.","Song Yichen and the others exchanged confused looks again.","Judging from their interaction, Feng Wu seemed to be on familiar terms with Feng Xun and the crown prince.","Was it possible that something was going on between Feng Wu and His Royal Highness? That would be such bad news for Song Yichen and his friends!","Song Yichen and Zhao Xingzhi looked at each other, and neither seemed too pleased.","Right now, everyone was following Feng Wu and Feng Xun.","But they were walking very fast, and only the teenagers from Initial were able to keep up with them.","“Look. Boss Jun is right over there.”","Feng Xun pointed at a teahouse ahead of them.","At the center of the grove stood a teahouse made of immortal flower wood. The burlywood seats and the immortal flower petals drifting down from the trees made for quite a refreshing scene.","The crown prince sat alone in the teahouse with his eyes half-closed. There was an indecipherable look on his face; no one could tell what he was thinking, nor did anyone dare to approach him.","Teenage girls were circling the teahouse at a distance.","They didn’t dare get any closer, but they didn’t want to leave either, so they decided to stay and wait in the distance.","Feng Xun gave Feng Wu a little push from behind. “Go ahead. Boss Jun is right there. Hurry up.”","Feng Wu’s face stiffened.","Feng Xun was right. Although she had been looking everywhere for Jun Linyuan, she lost her courage now that she had found him.","After all —","She was supposed to give Jun Linyuan these flowers on such a special day when everyone was watching, and Feng Wu knew perfectly well what that meant.","“Hey, little Feng Wu, are you going to back out now?” Feng Xun found his sister very amusing.","Just then —","A girl stepped out of the crowd with some flowers in her hands. She then pushed the door in the low fence open, summoned her courage, and walked into the teahouse.","From behind, her straight back reminded one of a warrior marching to her death.","“Is that Dugu Yamo?”","“As in Dugu Yamo from Empress Dugu’s family?”","“Is she going to give those flowers to His Royal Highness?”","“Her aunt is the empress, which makes her a kinsman of the emperor. Even if she can’t become the crown prince’s official wife, she’s good enough to be one of his consorts.”"]},{"number":1404,"title":"Chapter 1404 - What Choice Does Feng Wu Have?","paragraphs":["Feng Xun was surprised to see Dugu Yamo taking action. He then threw a dirty look at Feng Wu and said, “See? If you don’t hurry up, other people will give their flowers to Boss Jun.”","Feng Wu snapped, “So what if they do? Why should I care?”","“You dumb girl.” Feng Xun gently jabbed Feng Wu’s temple with a finger. “This festival is no joke. Only the first bouquet one receives has special meaning, and the ones after that don’t count. Understand?”","Special meaning?","Feng Wu shook her head. She didn’t need any special meaning. As long as she could complete her mission, she couldn’t care less if she was the first to give him flowers.","Therefore, she casually waved her hand. “Don’t worry. We shouldn’t ruin his moment. I’ll go after Dugu Yamo is done.”","Feng Wu already had a plan.","Since Dugu Yamo was going to be the first to give him the flowers, the girl would get all the attention. That way, Feng Wu was confident that no one would notice her. “Yes, that’s what I’m gonna do.”","Feng Xun stared at Feng Wu in bewilderment. “Aren’t you mad?”","Feng Wu looked perfectly innocent. “About what?”","Feng Xun said, “About this! You’re in love with Boss Jun, so you should feel jealous!”","Feng Wu rolled her eyes at him. “Since when am I in love with him? Nonsense.”","Feng Xun pointed at Feng Wu with a shaking finger. “You... you...”","She said she wouldn’t come, but she did.","And she came with a bunch of immortal flowers.","As if that wasn’t enough, she had been looking everywhere for His Royal Highness.","Everything she had done so far indicated that she was in love with Jun Linyuan, but...","“How can you still deny it? How can you? Little Feng Wu, you’re so unbelievable. No wonder Boss Jun is so mad.”","Hearing Feng Xun’s accusation, Feng Wu wanted to scream in frustration.","She cursed the system.","Just then —","“Master, Master, Master —”","The fairy spoke gingerly in Feng Wu’s head.","Feng Wu’s heart sank a little, and she suddenly had a very bad feeling.","Every time the fairy cringed and faltered, Feng Wu knew that something was about to go wrong.","“What is it?” She felt uneasy.","“Ahem... well...” Fearing that Feng Wu might want to hit her, the fairy recoiled and said timidly, “Actually, there’s a footnote in small font here. I missed it.”","“What footnote?”","“Well, it says that yours has to be the only bouquet of flowers.”","“What is the only bouquet?” Feng Wu was confused.","“Ahem... It means that the crown prince can only accept your bouquet of flowers today. If he takes flowers before or after you give him yours, you fail your mission.”","What?!","Feng Wu felt as though she had been struck by lightning and her ears buzzed.","If the fairy was in front of her now, she would squeeze that tiny body in her hand.","Feng Wu stared at the fairy with an indescribable look in her eyes.","The fairy had practically curled into a ball.","What choice did Feng Wu have?","She turned her attention away from the fairy and looked at Jun Linyuan and Dugu Yamo in the teahouse up ahead.","Right now, Dugu Yamo was standing in front of the crown prince. One could tell how nervous she was from her stiff back."]},{"number":1405,"title":"Chapter 1405 - She Was There First","paragraphs":["“Y- Your Royal Highness...” Dugu Yamo presented the light pink immortal flowers to Jun Linyuan with trembling hands. “P- Please accept these.”","Dugu Yamo was nervous and frustrated at herself.","She had worked on her lines the whole of last night, and had stayed up to memorize and rehearse her little speech. However, when the crown prince was actually in front of her, she was so nervous that she didn’t know where to put her own hands. All her lines escaped her, and her head went completely blank...","Dugu Yamo smiled bitterly.","Her father was the emperor’s brother-in-law, and she was respected like a real princess. She had more suitors than she could count, but she didn’t like any of them.","She had never expected that one day, she would stand in front of a teenager and wait for his verdict.","But he was Jun Linyuan, the dream of all the teenage girls in the empire.","Immediately, all eyes were on the crown prince.","“Is His Royal Highness going to accept it?”","“Dugu Yamo is pretty and smart, and she’s from an influential family. Maybe His Royal Highness really will...”","“Even Dugu Yamo was so nervous around His Royal Highness. I wonder if any girl can act naturally around him.”","“If His Royal Highness accepts Dugu Yamo, then...”","“Look! His Royal Highness is reaching out to her!”","It was true.","Jun Linyuan gave Feng Wu a sidelong glance.","But at that moment, Feng Wu was bantering with Feng Xun.","Other people might not be able to hear their conversation clearly, but Jun Linyuan could.","“She doesn’t like me, right? Heh.”","All warmth disappeared from his eyes and he gave off a terrifying energy.","He then snatched the flowers out of Dugu Yamo’s hands.","Wow —","Everyone cried out in surprise!","The crown prince had taken the flowers!","He... he had...","Even Dugu Yamo herself was dumbfounded and forgot how to react, not to mention the crowd.","“Is this really happening?” Dugu Yamo couldn’t believe it.","She had summoned her courage and stepped out because she wanted to try even though she knew that she was almost certain to fail.","“Y- Your Royal Highness...” She was so excited that she almost fainted.","The crowd was shocked as well!","“His Royal Highness accepted the flowers!”","“Holy crap!”","“Is His Royal Highness finally interested in girls now?”","“Is the Dugu family going to have a second empress?”","“No way. Dugu Yamo can’t possibly rise above Zuo Qingluan. She’ll be a consort at most.”","“What do you mean by ‘a consort at most’? That’s like a second wife to the crown prince! The crown prince!”","“The Dugu family is going to be so happy now.”","The servants of the Dugu family were indeed thrilled. They immediately headed back home so that they could tell their clansmen the good news at once!","In the crowd, Zuo Qingyu was frowning.","She had considered Dugu Yamo her good friend, but not only was the girl in love with the crown prince, she had done this!","Zuo Qingyu felt so betrayed and was furious that someone had stolen the man she loved.","Looking up, she saw Feng Wu and lashed out at her.","“Feng Wu, you look awful. Are you jealous?” Zuo Qingyu smiled."]},{"number":1406,"title":"Chapter 1406 - Amazing!","paragraphs":["Feng Wu wasn’t jealous, but she didn’t look too happy either.","She had been so sure that Jun Linyuan wouldn’t take the flowers.","Because she knew Jun Linyuan was an arrogant teenager who had very high standards. If he didn’t find Feng Wu good enough, why would he fall for someone as vulgar as Dugu Yamo?","Feng Wu was very confident on that point.","But!","To her surprise, the strict crown prince had very loose standards today.","Seeing the way Jun Linyuan casually played with the small bunch of flowers, Feng Wu couldn’t take it anymore.","What would she do if Jun Linyuan really accepted that bouquet? What about her mission, her broken star piece, and her beautiful master?","Feng Xun still wouldn’t stop talking. “See? You’re too late. That’s what happens when you play hard to get.”","Zuo Qingyu wasn’t helping either. She sneered at Feng Wu and said, “For a moment there, I thought His Royal Highness really had a thing for you. I see that I was mistaken. Feng Wu, you’re not much better than the rest.”","And a hubbub of other voices filled the air...","Everyone was still talking when Feng Wu shoved the door in the fence open and rushed inside with her immortal flowers.","Wow —","The crowd was thrilled when they saw Feng Wu charge toward the teahouse, looking like a lone warrior marching to her death.","Her movements created a stir!","To the onlookers, any change in the situation was exciting news, especially when it involved the crown prince’s love life.","“Feng Wu is going in! Look! She’s approaching the teahouse!”","“This is good! This is really good! Feng Wu is going to give her flowers, too!”","“Both girls are after the same man! That’s awesome! Who do you think His Royal Highness will choose?”","–","While the crowd was discussing among themselves, Song Yichen and the others exchanged bewildered looks.","Song Yichen also greatly admired Feng Wu.","“I didn’t know Feng Wu was so brave. She’s asking to get humiliated.”","Rubbing his chin, Zhao Xingzhi nodded. “That’s right. Dugu Yamo isn’t as pretty as Feng Wu, but she’s way more prominent in terms of her background. If I were His Royal Highness, I would choose the daughter of the Dugu family.”","“Poor Feng Wu. She’s going to be defeated and humiliated... Gosh, that’s so shameful. I’m too embarrassed to stay here as her fellow classmate...”","“It really is very humiliating. God, I feel too awkward to stay here. I can’t bring myself to see Feng Wu getting her face slapped. Let’s go, shall we?” Ning Yao, who was 6th, suggested.","“Of course not. How can we leave now?” Song Yichen refused without hesitation.","Who were they kidding?!","They had followed Feng Wu all the way here to see her get humiliated. Now that it was finally going to happen, how could they leave now?","Shu Yunruo glanced at Song Yichen.","He would bet his own life that Feng Wu wouldn’t be the one getting humiliated, for the crown prince had feelings for her.","Therefore, when Ning Yao turned to him, he said, “I’m not leaving. I want to see what happens next.”","He wanted to see Song Yichen and the others get their faces slapped.","“That’s the spirit.” Song Yichen had no idea what Shu Yunruo was thinking and patted the latter’s arm in satisfaction.","Meanwhile, the look on Zuo Qingyu’s face couldn’t be any more indescribable."]},{"number":1407,"title":"Chapter 1407 - Jun Linyuan the Unmanageable (1)","paragraphs":["Zuo Qingyu’s eyes widened as Feng Wu walked past her and went into the teahouse.","She couldn’t believe that Feng Wu had walked in just like that!","Wasn’t she afraid of the humiliation if he turned her down?","Somehow, when Dugu Yamo walked in with her flowers, Zuo Qingyu was enraged and felt betrayed.","But when Feng Wu walked in, Zuo Qingyu was worried, afraid, intimidated, and uneasy...","Was it because His Royal Highness treated Feng Wu differently? Zuo Qingyu clenched her fists.","Feng Wu had no idea of the kind of stir her action had caused.","She went straight up to Jun Linyuan and looked into his eyes. Her own eyes twinkled like stars.","Dugu Yamo was furious when she saw Feng Wu.","And she felt intimidated as well...","She was intimidated by Feng Wu’s beauty that could drive men crazy and her unpredictable behavior that could catch their interest.","At the same time.","The onlookers all held their breaths and watched.","They wondered how the two teenage girls would compete with each other.","And who would the crown prince choose?","What would the result be?","They were so curious!","They all watched with sparkling eyes and were eager for some gossip.","However —","To everyone’s surprise —","The competition ended in the most unusual way.","Feng Wu walked up to the crown prince, and acting as if no one else was around, she bent down and slowly drew closer to him. In the end, she was practically on top of him.","Wow —","The onlookers were utterly amazed.","“Isn’t His Royal Highness supposed to be a neat freak?”","“And I thought he wasn’t into girls.”","“I heard that he doesn’t allow girls to linger within 30 meters of him.”","But now —","Feng Wu was leaning in so close to Jun Linyuan that he could feel her breath on his lips.","She looked like she was going to kiss him!","The onlookers were so anxious!","They were overwhelmed with mixed feelings of anger, anxiety, agitation, and jealousy — something they had never felt before.","Song Yichen was dumbfounded. He stared at Feng Wu and pointed at her with a trembling finger. “T- This isn’t happening! Feng Wu is so bold! Why hasn’t His Royal Highness pushed her away?”","Zhao Xingzhi clenched his fists.","Zuo Qingyu was so frustrated that she wanted to smack her own head.","She regretted making the suggestion and cursed herself for provoking Feng Wu.","Zuo Qingyu went scarlet in the face and her voice dripped with jealousy. “She’s offering herself to His Royal Highness, so why shouldn’t he enjoy it?”","Someone next to her commented, “You can try it yourself and see if His Royal Highness will enjoy your company.”","“You —”","Infuriated, Zuo Qingyu turned around and wanted to hit the person. However, she saw that it was Mu the Sixth.","He stood there with his hands on his waist as he made a face.","And Feng Xun was standing next to him.","Zuo Qingyu could only grunt.","Their little episode didn’t attract much attention, because almost all eyes were on Feng Wu and Jun Linyuan.","Dugu Yamo was furious when she saw Feng Wu, but before she could do anything, Feng Wu had already rushed over and pressed herself against the crown prince."]},{"number":1408,"title":"Chapter 1408 - Jun Linyuan the Unmanageable (2)","paragraphs":["What was more...","To Dugu Yamo’s frustration, as Feng Wu moved closer, she snatched the flowers Dugu Yamo had given Jun Linyuan and threw them away.","The small bouquet flew through the air and fell to the ground with a small thump.","That abominable Feng Wu stuffed her own flowers into His Royal Highness’s hands!","Damn it!","Dugu Yamo’s eyes went bloodshot red, as though they were on fire!","Everyone saw what Feng Wu did.","And they were all stunned.","Feng Wu actually switched out Dugu Yamo’s flowers with her own, and she succeeded! His Royal Highness wasn’t mad at her!","They couldn’t understand this world anymore.","Ding —","Feng Wu heard a voice in her head.","“The fifth trial completed.”","The fairy’s voice had never sounded so pleasant.","Phew —","Feng Wu heaved a sigh of relief, and slowly relaxed.","She had been under a lot of pressure to take the initiative to approach Jun Linyuan, but to save her beautiful master, she had no other choice.","Now that the fifth trial was finally over and she had succeeded long before the deadline, Feng Wu felt very pleased.","However, one couldn’t say the same about the onlookers...","It was especially the case with Song Yichen and Zhao Xingzhi. They felt as if they had just been slapped in the face, and were completely baffled. It would take them a while to recover.","Zuo Qingyu was the most displeased of them all.","After her multiple confrontations with Feng Wu, Zuo Qingyu probably knew her better than even Chaoge did.","She clenched her fists in her sleeves.","Damn it!","If Dugu Yamo had succeeded in becoming the crown prince’s consort, Zuo Qingyu would still be mad, but she would have been able to accept it, because like every other girl, she wasn’t able to win his heart.","But Feng Wu was a different story!","Zuo Qingyu had to admit that Feng Wu was special to Jun Linyuan.","No one in the Zuo family would acknowledge it, but Zuo Qingyu knew that she couldn’t keep lying to herself.","She knew she couldn’t let things carry on like this, because it was obvious that the crown prince was attracted to Feng Wu.","Zuo Qingyu looked at Dugu Yamo.","“Dugu Yamo, you’re the only one I can count on now.”","Dugu Yamo wasn’t the type to swallow the humiliation. When the others weren’t looking, she had already run to her flowers and picked them up.","“Feng Wu, you’re not the only one who knows how to get close to His Royal Highness!”","Dugu Yamo quickly ran up to Jun Linyuan and shoved Feng Wu out of her way.","She moved as recklessly as a bull!","Feng Wu was still enjoying her success and failed to notice Dugu Yamo, so the latter actually managed to push her aside.","Before Feng Wu realized what was happening, Dugu Yamo had already approached the crown prince with her own flowers. “Your Royal Highness, here are my flowers...”","Wow!","Wow!","Wow!","The onlookers were thrilled.","“Here comes the fight!”","“Finally!”","“Come on!”","After much anticipation, the two girls were finally confronting each other!","What would happen next?","Would His Royal Highness accept Dugu Yamo’s flowers and cast Feng Wu aside?"]},{"number":1409,"title":"Chapter 1409 - Jun Linyuan the Unmanageable (3)","paragraphs":["Or would Feng Wu grab Dugu Yamo by the hair? Would they try to scratch each other’s eyeballs out?","OMG!","This was so exciting!","Zuo Qingyu’s heart raced and she looked thrilled.","Song Yichen and the others were eager to see what would happen next as well!","However, when everyone was so sure that a fight was going to start —","Thump!","They heard a loud bang.","Everyone watched as a figure was flung away from the crown prince.","There was a whoosh.","And she flew backward...","“That’s... Dugu Yamo...”","Some had hoped that it was Feng Wu who would be sent flying, but they couldn’t lie to themselves when they saw who it was.","Dugu Yamo had indeed been running toward the crown prince, but she was still an arm’s length away from him when she was pushed away by a strange force!","Thump!","The impact sent Dugu Yamo flying backward until she fell on her butt, looking utterly baffled.","She wasn’t the only one. The onlookers were just as astonished.","Everyone watched with their mouths agape.","The crown prince had risen to his feet. With his long legs and towering height, he cut quite an intimidating figure.","He looked down at Feng Wu with his dark, brooding eyes.","He had such well-defined features, and his profile was as perfect as a sculpture’s.","Right now, that extremely handsome face was moving closer and closer to Feng Wu.","His scent seemed to wrap itself around Feng Wu.","They were so close that they could feel each other’s hot breaths.","Lub dub — Lub dub —","Feng Wu could sense her heart racing.","This wasn’t part of the plan.","She didn’t know why this was happening, but she felt that things were getting out of hand.","Thus, she instinctively rejected the feeling.","Feng Wu bit her lower lip and stumbled back.","However, the crown prince kept his gaze fixed on Feng Wu.","As Feng Wu stepped back, he closed in.","With his eyes narrowed, Jun Linyuan looked as dangerous as a forest leopard.","Feng Wu turned to run, but Jun Linyuan caught her by her waist.","His grip stopped her from taking another step.","He stared at Feng Wu with his brooding eyes and waved the bouquet in front of her face.","Feng Wu said, “Uh...”","Jun Linyun’s eyes seemed to turn red, and his voice was quite intimidating. “Speak!”","An ice-cold energy seemed to come off the crown prince, and the pressure made Feng Wu’s heart skip a beat.","“What... do you want me to say?”","Feng Wu didn’t sound very confident.","“What does this mean?” Jun Linyuan showed her the flowers.","Feng Wu said, “Well... that...”","“Speak!”","Feng Wu mumbled something.","Jun Linyuan raised his eyebrows, and the energy coming off him became even more intimidating.","He pushed Feng Wu backward until she hit the table. He then raised her fine, pointy chin with one long finger.","The burlywood table was right behind Feng Wu, and Jun Linyuan had completely hemmed her in. She wasn’t going anywhere.","They were standing so close to each other, and their postures were so suggestive...","It was very hard not to be put in mind of other things!","Even Feng Wu couldn’t help but blush.","–","By then, all the onlookers were completely stupefied!"]},{"number":1410,"title":"Chapter 1410 - Jun Linyuan the Unmanageable (4)","paragraphs":["No...","This was so big!","The crown prince who was supposed to be uninterested in girls was touching Feng Wu’s face!","That move alone was enough to make one wonder.","Feng Xun rubbed his chin and his smiling eyes looked like two little crescent moons.","“Little Feng Wu, you dishonest girl! I’d like to see you deny your feelings this time!”","Feng Xun wouldn’t know what to do if things didn’t work out for them this time.","However, to everyone’s surprise, Feng Wu, the girl who was deemed to be the luckiest person in years —","“What the hell do you think you’re doing?!”","The moment the crown prince put his warm hand on her tender cheek, Feng Wu smacked his hand away.","OMG! She had smacked the crown prince’s hand!","How could she bring herself to do it?","He was the idol of all teenage girls in the empire, but Feng Wu had just smacked his hand away!","And she had used so much force!","They all heard the crisp sound.","And they were all astonished!","Had Feng Wu lost her mind? What was she thinking? Did she know what she was doing?!","Jun Linyuan frowned a little and had that majestic look on his face again.","He gave Feng Wu a sidelong glance and moved closer again.","WIth everyone watching, Feng Wu was very self-conscious, and she tried to push Jun Linyuan away. “You... get away from me! Now!”","She had no idea what was happening to her.","She was usually the level-headed type, but her heart was racing now, and she even panicked a little.","it wasn’t like her at all.","“Go? Go where?” Jun Linyuan wouldn’t let her move and pinned her arms behind her back.","The position forced Feng Wu to stand on tiptoe to keep her balance, and to everyone else, it looked like she was throwing herself at him.","“Hey, Jun Linyuan, that’s enough! You’ve gone too far!” Feng Wu yelled anxiously.","There were two people in this world that she couldn’t see through no matter what.","One was her beautiful master, and the other one was Jun Linyuan.","“I’ve gone too far?” The crown prince stressed each word.","They were so close that Feng Wu could see the ferocious look in his cold eyes.","His grip was so tight that it reminded Feng Wu of a clamp.","As Jun Linyuan uttered those words, Feng Wu felt his arms wrap tighter around her.","“Ssss... That hurts!” Feng Wu drew in her breath.","“So, is this only a joke to you?” There was something very dangerous about the look in Jun Linyuan’s eyes.","His husky voice reminded her of the calm before a storm.","“Well...” Feng Wu cringed and didn’t dare look into Jun Linyuan’s bloodshot eyes.","There was no warmth in them.","But there was rage, resentment, sarcasm, cruelty, and great sorrow. He looked like a wounded young cub, and she felt sorry for him.","Other people couldn’t see his eyes, but Dugu Yamo was close enough to notice the change in his emotions.","Oh god...","Dugu Yamo felt her head go blank...","She couldn’t believe that someone as unapproachable as the crown prince was capable of expressing human feelings.","And the person who made him change was her!","Feng Wu!!!","Dugu Yamo stiffened. She felt cold, and her head went blank. She could no longer think straight.","That was unbelievable!","She couldn’t believe it!","But it was happening."]},{"number":1411,"title":"Chapter 1411 - Jun Linyuan the Unmanageable (5)","paragraphs":["However, to Dugu Yamo’s further disbelief, when Jun Linyuan tried to express his feelings for Feng Wu, she smacked his hand away!","How dare she be so pretentious?!","Dugu Yamo really wanted to slap Feng Wu.","Feng Wu had no idea how Dugu Yamo felt, because all her attention was on Jun Linyuan now.","“That’s right. It really was a joke. What? Can’t Your Royal Highness take a silly joke? Hahaha, are you that petty?”","She then surprised Jun Linyuan by stepping on his foot forcibly. After that, she shoved him away and tried to flee the scene.","She was doing it again, running away as soon as she flirted with him! Jun Linyuan was infuriated.","He knew that the girl was so daring because he was so nice to her.","He stared at her and smirked.","The crowd was astonished.","Everyone saw how Feng Wu smacked His Royal Highness’s hand away, refused him, and even stepped on his foot.","Any other person would have been killed by now. Not only was Feng Wu still alive, His Royal Highness was smiling at her as well.","Had this world gone insane?!","“Damn! I was right!” Clenching her fists, Zuo Qingyu was overwhelmed with jealousy and hatred.","Song Yichen and his friends could practically feel their faces getting slapped.","They had come here to enjoy Feng Wu’s predicament, but instead...","Feng Xun was speechless.","He had thought that Boss Jun was a very pretentious man, but as it turned out, Feng Wu was worse. What a pair...","They were perfect for each other! They were so well-suited!","Feng Wu turned to run after she got free.","Of course she had to.","If she didn’t run now, who knew what Jun Linyuan would do next.","The man looked so dangerous and she was certain that he would take his revenge. What happened just then was the perfect proof.","But —","The system seemed to be working against Feng Wu. She had only taken a few steps when —","“My prettiest and smartest master!”","Feng Wu cursed under her breath as soon as she heard that cheap compliment.","“Save the flattery and cut to the chase,” Feng Wu said uneasily.","“Well... ahem...”","The fairy cleared her throat, recoiled, and spoke gingerly.","“I have your 6th trial here...”","Feng Wu glowered at the fairy.","“Well... It just suddenly arrived... I was surprised, too...”","Feng Wu shouted impatiently, “What is it?!”","“Well... It’s...” The fairy hesitated and stammered, and she still couldn’t form a coherent sentence after a while.","Feng Wu had a bad feeling.","If the task was easy, the fairy would have gladly told her.","Her hesitation indicated that it was going to be another difficult task.","“Just tell me.” Feng Wu wanted to roll her eyes.","She had gone through enough difficult tasks to no longer be affected.","“Well... Master, the 6th trial is...","“You have to take back the flowers which you gave to the crown prince earlier...”","“That’s all?” Feng Wu’s eyes lit up!","That wasn’t a difficult task at all. With her glib tongue, Feng Wu believed that she could easily take the flowers back."]},{"number":1412,"title":"Chapter 1412 - Jun Linyuan the Unmanageable (6)","paragraphs":["“No, no, no, my dear master... The key to this task is that His Royal Highness has to return the flowers voluntarily.”","Feng Wu cried out, “What?!”","The fairy nodded.","Feng Wu asked, “How much time do I have?”","The fairy said, “You have until the end of today.”","Feng Wu asked, “Can I do it tomorrow?”","The fairy said, “You have until the end of today.”","Feng Wu asked, “Are you sure?!”","The fairy said, “Very.”","Feng Wu rubbed her own forehead.","What kind of system was this? Why did it seem to specialize in making Feng Wu’s life miserable?","“Master? Master?” The fairy feared that it was too hard a blow to her young master.","She knew the saying, “To explode in silence, or die in it.”","And she was worried that her young master might explode...","But Feng Wu didn’t know what the fairy was thinking...","Taking a deep breath, Feng Wu adjusted her facial expression, slowly turned around, and stared at Jun Linyuan with her clear, bright eyes.","She then smiled at him.","Although she tried her best to beam at him...","Her smile still looked forced.","Meanwhile, the crown prince had crossed his arms in front of him and leaned back against a pillar as he casually studied Feng Wu.","With his great looks, his unhurried demeanor looked exceptionally attractive.","“Teehee —” Feng Wu smiled awkwardly.","This was so embarrassing...","Only a moment ago, she was trying to steer clear of Jun Linyuan, but now —","She needed his help again.","Despite her reluctance, Feng Wu still slowly approached him.","And the crowd...","They exhaled in unison.","“She’s turning around and going back.”","“Why do you think she’s doing that?”","“It’s obvious. She was trying to play hard to get and thought His Royal Highness would stop her, but he didn’t even say a word.”","“That’s right. Look, she’s going back to His Royal Highness because of that.”","“I don’t think that’s the case. His Royal Highness seems to really like her.”","“No, he doesn’t. She’s like a toy to him, that’s all. He’ll play with her when he feels like it and cast her aside when he doesn’t.”","–","Most of the people saying those things were girls.","They were jealous of Feng Wu, which affected their judgment. Naturally, they wouldn’t say anything nice about her.","Feng Wu heard them as well.","But the system had given her the lousy task, so what choice did she have? She was a victim as well!","Despite her torment, Feng Wu still had to keep smiling, which wasn’t easy at all.","“Y- Your Royal Highness...” Feng Wu inched forward until she reached him.","The crown prince raised his eyebrows and smirked.","His demeanor was so casual that he seemed to be enjoying a show.","Feng Wu felt like screaming. This was so humiliating!","However, she needed the broken star pieces and had to force herself to smile. “Your Royal Highness... Teehee...”","Jun Linyuan found the silly girl very amusing.","He was convinced that she was infatuated with him, but she just wouldn’t admit it. He wanted to see how much longer she could play hard to get.","“You’re back, again,” he said sarcastically.","“Ahem —” Feng Wu cleared her throat and nodded. She looked incredibly docile."]},{"number":1413,"title":"Chapter 1413 - Jun Linyuan the Unmanageable (7)","paragraphs":["“Little Feng Wu.” Jun Linyuan glanced at Feng Wu. “What on earth do you want?”","Feng Wu immediately answered, “I want your flowers.”","Everyone gave Feng Wu odd looks as soon as she said that.","“Oh my god!”","“Feng Wu really is the boldest girl I’ve ever seen...”","“Dugu Yamo only tried to give His Royal Highness her flowers, but Feng Wu wants his flowers instead!”","“Everyone knows what those flowers mean on a special day like this!”","“I heard that the royal family wants to arrange a marriage with the Zuo family, and Zuo Qingluan is the best candidate.”","“That’s right, I heard that too. Zuo Qingluan is the one with the True Phoenix Blood; Feng Wu is nothing in comparison.”","“Feng Wu is such a schemer!” Zuo Qingyu tried to exaggerate the situation. “She deliberately gave His Royal Highness those flowers, only to ask for them back later. That way, everyone will think that His Royal Highness gave her flowers. What a well-thought-out plan!”","Many people saw the light after they heard Zuo Qingyu’s interpretation and started criticizing Feng Wu.","Soon, the news of Feng Wu asking His Royal Highness for immortal flowers spread through the grove as if it had grown wings.","Gossip involving famous people like Jun Linyuan and Feng Wu traveled the fastest.","Couldn’t Feng Wu hear all the discussion? Of course she could.","Still, she had to force herself to defer to Jun Linyuan.","Jun Linyuan’s eyes flickered, and he gave Feng Wu a half-smile. “Are you asking for this bunch of flowers?”","He gave Feng Wu a teasing look and waved the flowers in his hand.","“Yes!” Feng Wu stared eagerly at the immortal flowers and reached out. “I’ve given it some thought and decided that I shouldn’t bother you. So, how about I take those flowers back?”","Feng Wu had formed a plan already.","She was about to snatch them and flee the scene. However —","The crown prince wasn’t that easy to fool.","“You won’t bother me?” Jun Linyuan’s pupils contracted.","She had flirted with him first, and now, she wanted to take it back. Who did she think he was?","A storm seemed to brew in his dark eyes.","“Yes, I’m sorry...” Feng Wu bit her lower lip and looked quite earnest.","She grabbed Dugu Yamo’s flowers and stuffed them into Jun Linyuan’s arms. “These are much nicer. Mine are already wilting, so I’ll take them from here.”","Something dangerous shone in Jun Linyuan’s eyes.","The look reminded one of dark clouds in the sky.","Feng Wu felt a tremendous pressure on her shoulders.","The chilly sensation made her tremble non-stop.","It was freezing...","His eyes were so frightening.","Feng Wu almost couldn’t look into his infuriated eyes.","“I thought... you didn’t like my flowers,” Feng Wu said gingerly.","Jun Linyuan smirked. The warmth in his eyes was gone, and they seemed to have turned into bottomless pits.","Frost seemed to cover his handsome face, and his black eyebrows reminded one of swords out of their scabbards.","“Well...” Feng Wu didn’t dare speak.","“Feng Wu, do you like me that much?” the crown prince asked unhurriedly.","What?"]},{"number":1414,"title":"Chapter 1414 - Jun Linyuan the Unmanageable (8)","paragraphs":["Feng Wu was dumbfounded and felt as if she had been struck by lightning. Looking up, she stared at Jun Linyuan in bewilderment, and her clear eyes were filled with innocence and confusion.","Jun Linyuan’s rosy lips curled into a half-smile, and he said, “If you don’t like me, why should I give you flowers?”","That was so true!","All the onlookers gave Feng Wu strange looks.","Feng Wu was speechless.","She now knew what “inexcusable” meant.","“Huh?” When the crown prince didn’t hear her answer, he raised his eyebrows and gave Feng Wu a goading look.","What could Feng Wu possibly say?","She tried to explain herself. “Well... It’s actually not like that...”","Jun Linyuan slowly approached her with a cold smile on his face and asked, “What is it, then?”","“Well... I...” Despite the smile on her face, Feng Wu was screaming inwardly.","How was she supposed to know what the system wanted her to do? She was as confused as everyone else!","“If it’s not like that, then explain yourself.”","The crown prince was usually uninterested in other people, but now, he was closing in with eyes that glinted coldly.","Feng Wu said, “I... I... I just don’t think these flowers are good enough for someone as elegant and graceful as you, so I want to take them back and give you something more suitable another day.”","“When will that be?” The crown prince stared at Feng Wu.","It was only a random excuse, and of course, she didn’t know when that would be.","Damn you, Jun Linyuan!","Feng Wu cursed inwardly. She wondered why this man wouldn’t leave her alone.","But she couldn’t lose her temper just yet and had to maintain that adorable sweet smile.","Grinding her teeth, Feng Wu smiled. “Your Royal Highness, are you really not going to give them to me?”","Jun Linyuan gave her a half-smile. “Little Feng Wu, are you really that in love with me?”","All Feng Wu had to say was yes and he would give her the flowers.","However, Feng Wu failed to recognize Jun Linyuan’s insinuation, and she waved her hands in denial.","“No, I’m not in love with you at all! Jun Linyuan, please believe me! I don’t have any feelings for you! Don’t believe the rumors!”","Jun Linyuan’s face immediately turned as dark as ink.","Around them, everyone became so quiet that they could hear their breathing.","The temperature seemed to drop.","Feng Wu eyed the flowers eagerly.","Although she still had a whole day ahead of her, if Jun Linyuan refused to give her the flowers, there was nothing she could do.","Moreover, what if Jun Linyuan decided to destroy the flowers?","Feng Wu had just jinxed herself.","The moment that idea popped into her head —","Jun Linyuan’s slender fingers wrapped around the flowers.","Shit!","Feng Wu’s pupils contracted.","Since the system had specified that she had to get those flowers back, she wouldn’t be able to accept any other flowers.","If Jun Linyuan destroyed them now, then her 6th trial would be... Feng Wu couldn’t bring herself to imagine her failure.","“Wait, wait —”","Feng Wu rushed over to him and wrapped her hands around Jun Linyuan’s wrist so tightly that she almost gave him bruises.","“Those are my flowers! You can’t destroy them!”","Feng Wu glowered at Jun Linyuan.","Jun Linyuan was baffled.","Had he misunderstood something?","If the girl cherished the flowers so much, how could she not be in love with him?","Was Feng Xun correct in saying that she was being dishonest and playing hard to get? Were her physical reactions more trustworthy than her words?"]},{"number":1415,"title":"Chapter 1415 - Jun Linyuan the Unmanageable (9)","paragraphs":["Feng Wu was very good at reading faces. Seeing the fleeting hesitation in Jun Linyuan’s eyes, she immediately pleaded with him.","“Please give me the flowers. Pretty please?”","Feng Wu’s voice had the natural sweetness of a child, which was accentuated when her tone softened further in making a request. Together with her big teary eyes and adorable expression, no man would be able to resist her.","Even Jun Linyuan’s heart skipped a beat seeing her like that.","However, he was more resistant than most people and soon returned to himself.","“No.” He turned her down outright.","Feng Wu almost stomped her foot in frustration.","This man was doing it on purpose!","He could live without these flowers, but to her, they were more important than her life!","“Are these flowers very important to you?” Jun Linyuan asked casually.","“Yes! They’re more important than my life!” Feng Wu nodded.","Feng Xun interjected, “Of course they are. They’re from Boss Jun, so they mean a lot more.”","Feng Wu wanted to kick Feng Xun.","Why wouldn’t this guy keep his mouth shut?! She didn’t want to marry the crown prince. She was here to save her beautiful master.","Jun Linyuan studied Feng Wu with his bright brooding eyes, and his gaze was so intense.","That look made Feng Wu’s heart skip a beat, and she found herself too scared to look up.","“ Thump — ” Feng Wu indeed kicked Feng Xun. “Just keep your mouth shut!”","Rubbing his leg where she had kicked him, Feng Xun looked at her with teary eyes. “I was only trying to speak your mind for you. If we do it your way, when will the two of you realize your mutual feelings?”","What feelings?!","Feng Wu raised her hand at Feng Xun again.","Feng Xun cried out and ran away, saying, “Fine, fine. I won’t say a word. Satisfied?”","Feng Wu accidentally met Jun Linyuan’s gaze, and the heat in his eyes almost burned her skin.","She involuntarily looked away.","She had to admit that Jun Linyuan was dangerously attractive.","If she wasn’t used to her beautiful master’s charm, she thought she might be infatuated with Jun Linyuan like all the other girls.","“Since these flowers are so important to you...” Flames seemed to burn in Jun Linyuan’s eyes as he looked down at Feng Wu.","Feng Wu’s eyes lit up.","She looked expectantly at Jun Linyuan and prayed that he would give them to her.","But —","Jun Linyuan changed his tone. “Of course, I can’t give them to you so carelessly.”","Feng Wu: !!!","She was smiling on the outside but cursing in her head.","Stomping her foot, she said, “Jun Linyuan, you —”","The crown prince misunderstood when Feng Wu said that the flowers were more important than her life; he thought it proved that Feng Wu had feelings for him.","He stopped being mad. Instead, he changed his mind and started teasing Feng Wu.","“If you want these flowers so badly...” The crown prince gave her a meaningful look. “I’m not saying you can’t have them.”","Feng Wu’s eyes lit up.","“Name your terms!” She thumped her own chest.","Eyes shining, Jun Linyuan smiled and said, “Be my personal maid.”","WHAT?!"]},{"number":1416,"title":"Chapter 1416 - Jun Linyuan the Unmanageable (10)","paragraphs":["Feng Wu glared at Jun Linyuan. “Can’t you propose something more reasonable?”","“Forget it, then.” The crown prince turned to walk away.","“Don’t go —” Feng Wu immediately ran after him and grabbed him by the sleeve. “Let’s talk it out. We’re in a teahouse, aren’t we? Let’s sit down and negotiate.”","Feng Wu was ready for a long talk.","She already felt a lot more relieved.","She still had hope as long as Jun Linyuan was willing to talk to her. Things would be a lot worse if he wouldn’t even name any terms.","Jun Linyuan glanced at Feng Wu.","She had proactively grabbed his sleeve before pressing on his shoulders so that he sat down in a chair.","She was determined to make him give her those flowers.","Not only did Feng Wu sit down after that, she also poured some tea for both of them, as though she was ready for a long conversation.","Her approach astonished a lot of people.","The teahouse was some distance away, so the crowd couldn’t hear their exact words.","But they could see their movements.","They saw with their own eyes Feng Wu sitting the crown prince down opposite her.","And they saw her pour him some tea, which he downed in one go.","They also saw Feng Wu and the crown prince ready to start talking.","More than jealousy, they felt envy.","Many people asked themselves if they would be able to act so unperturbed in front of the crown prince if they were in Feng Wu’s shoes.","The answer was —","No.","Their hearts would beat so fast as soon as they locked gazes with the crown prince, to say nothing of sitting down opposite him.","This Feng Wu was really bold.","Feng Wu had no idea what everyone else thought of her. Right now, her top priority was the 6th trial.","“I’m not saying I can’t become your personal maid.”","Feng Wu smiled at Jun Linyuan. “But only for a limited time. After all, I’m a student of Imperial College and I have my own studies to worry about, right?”","The crown prince gave Feng Wu a casual look and raised a finger.","“A day?” Feng Wu was elated.","Jun Linyuan gave Feng Wu a “you idiot” look and said, “A year.”","“A year?!” Feng Wu flared up and smacked her hands on the table. “No way! A year is out of the question! That’s preposterous! Jun Linyuan, you can’t be serious!”","Jun Linyuan was startled by her exasperation, but he still managed to keep his face very stern.","“What are your terms, then?”","“A day.” Feng Wu also raised a finger.","The crown prince even rolled his eyes at her.","He rose to his feet and turned to leave.","Feng Wu hastily stopped him.","“Hey, wait! Wait —” Feng Wu stopped him. “Don’t rush off. Let’s negotiate.”","“You think?” The crown prince glanced at Feng Wu.","The difference between a day and a year was a little too big.","“How about this? 10 days! That’s the best I can do!”","Feng Wu stared at Jun Linyuan and said, “That’s my bottom line and no more!”","“A month.” Jun Linyuan raised an eyebrow.","“15 days!”","“20.”","“16.”","“19.”","“17.”","“18.”","“Good, 18 days it is, then!” Feng Wu smacked the table and sealed the deal.","Just then —"]},{"number":1417,"title":"Chapter 1417 - Be My Little Maid (1)","paragraphs":["It was just serving Jun Linyuan, right? She would do anything to complete the 6th trial.","Jun Linyuan looked into Feng Wu’s eyes and was a little surprised by her prompt reply.","“Deal,” he replied.","“Flowers, give me my flowers.” Feng Wu eagerly reached out to him.","Did she want his flowers so badly?","The proud crown prince gave Feng Wu a half-smile.","Seeing the way the girl gingerly held the flowers and how much she seemed to like them, Jun Linyuan picked up some more from beside him and stuffed them into her hands. “Take them all.”","Feng Wu was speechless.","She only wanted her own bunch and wasn’t interested in more, okay?","However, she would still need Jun Linyuan’s help before she finished all 12 Trials of Love.","Therefore, she had to take the flowers and smile at him.","Jun Linyuan glanced at Feng Wu. “Happy now?”","Feng Wu was speechless.","She was forced to accept something she didn’t like and had to fake gratitude. What was worse, she had to endure all the sarcasm... It was awful.","Jun Linyuan rose to his feet and strolled off. He only took a few steps before he paused, turned his head, and glanced at Feng Wu.","“Let’s go.”","Feng Wu was dumbfounded.","She suddenly realized that she had agreed to be Jun Linyuan’s maid for 18 days, but —","“Is it starting now?” Feng Wu frowned.","“What do you think?” Jun Linyuan raised his eyebrows and turned to leave.","Since half the day was already over, Feng Wu found it a sweet deal. At that thought, she happily followed him.","The crowd watched as Feng Wu left with Jun Linyuan.","And the looks on their faces were very strange.","“So... she’s only going to be a maid.”","“I thought she would become a consort at least, but she’s only a maid.”","“The way she recklessly rushed up to the crown prince, what would His Royal Highness think of her? She should feel very lucky to be his maid.”","–","All the girls who had considered Feng Wu a great threat mocked her now.","Even Song Yichen and his friends felt conflicted.","Zhao Xingzhi smirked. “I thought His Royal Highness thought highly of Feng Wu, but after all the wrangling, she only became a maid. How preposterous!”","“Is it?” Shu Yunruo glanced at Zhao Xingzhi. “If you were given that chance, would you turn it down?”","“You —” Zhao Xingzhi stared at Shu Yunruo. “Watch your language!”","Zhao Xingzhi was 4th and Shu Yunruo was 5th. Whenever they had a conflict, Zhao Xingzhi would try to suppress Shu Yunruo with his higher ranking.","Shu Yunruo only found him ridiculous.","He was the heir of the Gongshu Family, and he would usually ignore someone like Zhao Xingzhi, but —","“Do you really think His Royal Highness only considers Feng Wu a maid?”","He gave Zhao Xingzhi and the others a half-smile. “Lying to yourselves is a foolish thing to do.”","After that, Shu Yunruo turned to leave.","Song Yichen and the others traded embarrassed looks. When they thought about it, they realized that if given the chance to stay close to His Royal Highness, they would take it, no matter in what capacity. They would be over the moon.","Feng Wu hence was indeed spectacular.","Feng Xun and Xuan Yi smiled at each other as they watched Feng Wu follow the arrogant crown prince."]},{"number":1418,"title":"Chapter 1418 - Be My Little Maid (2)","paragraphs":["Feng Xun tugged at Xuan Yi and asked, “Don’t you think Boss Jun has changed?”","“Has he?” Xuan Yi sounded confused.","Feng Xun said, “Yes! Haven’t you noticed? Boss Jun has been talking a lot more.”","Thinking about it, Xuan Yi realized that Feng Xun was right.","Feng Xun went on, “And haven’t you noticed that Boss Jun is a lot more expressive when he speaks?”","Xuan Yi was still trying to think how Jun Linyuan had changed, when Feng Xun gave him an example. “Before, Boss Jun would only say ‘move’ in that cold way of his, but just then, he told Feng Wu ‘let’s go.’ Can’t you tell the difference?”","“Yes, but that only happens when he’s around Feng Wu,” Xuan Yi said grumpily.","Feng Xun gave it some thought and realized that Xuan Yi was right.","Boss Jun was still as unapproachable and reticent as ever with other people, but he was a lot more considerate toward Feng Wu.","“Boss Jun couldn’t care less about Feng Wu’s life when we were in Northern Border City. Who could have known...” Feng Xun sounded amazed.","Meanwhile, Feng Wu was following behind Jun Linyuan.","She couldn’t tell if Jun Linyuan was doing it on purpose, but he was casually walking around the immortal flower grove with his hands behind his back.","With his impressive height, straight back, exquisite features, and excellent posture, he looked as imposing as a king.","Feng Wu stayed an arm’s length away from him the way a maid would.","But the air in the immortal flower grove was suggestive enough.","The sun was setting and the light was growing dim.","On the day of the Immortal Flower Festival, when the atmosphere felt right, couples might roll around in the bushes right there and then.","Therefore, Feng Wu felt embarrassed when she saw the rustling bushes on the side of the road.","However, Jun Linyuan seemed completely unaware and kept walking in that direction.","How awkward would it be if he ran into those people?","Feng Wu immediately quickened her steps and grabbed Jun Linyuan by his sleeve. She warned him, “We should leave. Now.”","The crown prince seemed to be lost in thought, and Feng Wu’s voice woke him up from his reverie. He then glanced at Feng Wu in bewilderment.","Feng Wu grew anxious when Jun Linyuan stopped walking, and she tried to pull him away. “Are you dumb or what? Don’t just stand there! Move!”","The crown prince was all about saving face, and no one had ever dared call him dumb. Thus, his rebellious side immediately flared up.","Instead of turning around, he kept moving forward.","“Hey! Stop right there!” Feng Wu was exasperated.","Even she knew what happened here in the bushes during the Immortal Flower Festival.","Unfortunately, the crown prince was walking too fast for Feng Wu to stop him.","It just so happened that the couple was too absorbed in what they were doing to notice the approaching footsteps.","Whoosh —","The tall bushes were brushed aside to reveal two entwined bodies.","By then, the young couple finally realized what was going on, and the girl shrieked.","Feng Wu arrived at that moment. She put two spiritual stones on the ground and dragged Jun Linyuan away.","The crown prince remained unperturbed and aloof, and one couldn’t see any change in his expression.","However, Feng Wu realized how stiff he had become when she dragged him off.","She complained after they were out of the bushes, “Your Royal Highness, did you do that on purpose?”","Jun Linyuan glared at Feng Wu with emotionless eyes. “Shut up!”"]},{"number":1419,"title":"Chapter 1419 - Be My Little Maid (3)","paragraphs":["The crown prince was very frightening when he was like this.","Feng Wu immediately quieted down. Fine. She would stop talking altogether.","However —","Feng Wu thought her head was going to explode when she saw the crown prince’s scarlet red earlobes.","Jun Linyuan wouldn’t be reacting this way if he was experienced.","Judging by the way he was reacting, could he be...","So, he was actually trying to cover up this embarrassment when he acted all nonchalant and unapproachable.","Feng Wu looked at Jun Linyuan involuntarily, but it just so happened that he was looking in her direction as well.","Their eyes met and they could almost see sparks in the air —","Feng Wu immediately looked away.","So did the crown prince.","The air seemed to freeze for a moment, and the embarrassment made them go stiff.","In the end, Feng Wu used to be a modern woman and was used to such things. Therefore, she soon returned to herself.","She then stole a glance at Jun Linyuan.","She realized that not only had Jun Linyuan’s fair earlobes turned red, but his eyes couldn’t stop darting around.","Driven by curiosity, Feng Wu tugged at his sleeve and whispered, “Jun Linyuan, don’t tell me you haven’t seen such things before.”","The crown prince immediately stiffened, and there was a vexed look on his taut, handsome face. He threw a cold glance at Feng Wu before looking away.","Oh my —","Feng Wu had been a secret agent in her previous life, and she was an expert at reading faces. Therefore —","“Jun Linyuan, are you a virgin?” Feng Wu didn’t know where she found the courage, but she just poked her nose into Jun Linyuan’s personal life.","Jun Linyuan stiffened and walked away without looking at Feng Wu.","Wow —","Feng Wu was thrilled.","She felt as though she had discovered a whole new world and couldn’t wait to hear more gossip.","“Hey, hey —”","Jun Linyuan walked very fast, and Feng Wu had to run after him. She looked up at him with sparkling eyes.","“Have you never seen such things before? Don’t you have a maid to warm your bed? Seriously? You’re the crown prince...”","He was walking so fast that Feng Wu could barely catch up. She was panting as she ran.","Feng Wu said grumpily, “Isn’t that normal? Why are you avoiding the question? You look so nervous.”","Suddenly, the crown prince stopped.","Feng Wu, who was still rushing forward, bumped into his back.","His back was so hard that Feng Wu thought she had broken her nose.","“Hm —”","That hurt.","She almost burst into tears.","“Do you know a lot about it?” There was a murderous look on his face as he looked down at her with his cold eyes.","All Feng Wu could feel was pain. Tears had welled up in her eyes as she stared at him innocently. “What?”","“Do you know a lot about such things?” The crown prince frowned and sounded very intimidating.","“Well...” Feng Wu was speechless.","What should she say?","Such things were quite common in modern society. Even if she hadn’t done it herself, she had still seen her fair share.","However, she then saw Jun Linyuan’s taut face and his clenched fists... The bulging purple veins were evidence of how furious he was.","“Who taught you those things?” The look on his face reminded her of a demon.","Feng Wu stammered, “Well... I — I only heard some things. I don’t really know much about it. I don’t! Trust me!”"]},{"number":1420,"title":"Chapter 1420 - Be My Little Maid (4)","paragraphs":["Feng Wu wanted to smack her own head.","Why did she have to be so nosy and ask after the teenager’s private life? Now, she became the one who was at a loss over what to say.","Jun Linyuan didn’t say anything, but he was looking in another direction.","A man was standing there, waiting for instructions.","It was none other than Feng himself.","Feng nodded, indicating that he had received the order.","Feng Wu was dumbfounded as the master and servant reached a tacit agreement; she had no idea what was going on.","But Jun Linyuan didn’t care if she understood or not. He picked her up and marched off.","“Hey, Jun Linyuan! What are you doing? I have legs. I can walk on my own. Let go of me —”","Of course, the crown prince wouldn’t let go of her. He wanted to pry her head open and find out what was inside.","The crown prince’s residence.","A lot of servants worked in the residence, and they all seemed to have been specially trained. Everyone walked swiftly and quietly without stopping for a second.","The crown prince liked things quiet, and he wanted the servants to stay out of sight.","Therefore, the wide and even paths of the residence were usually deserted.","News came from the tower building that His Royal Highness’s carriage was about to arrive.","Granny Gong immediately went out to greet him with hot towels.","The crown prince was a neat freak, and with all the dust outside, the first thing he always did when he arrived home was to clean his hands.","However, as Granny Gong laid out the hot water and towels, she saw the dark-faced crown prince quickly walk into the house with a person in his arms.","Jun Linyuan soon walked inside, leaving everyone behind.","The servant blinked in bewilderment as the crown prince walked away.","“Granny Gong?”","A maid next to Granny Gong spoke, and she sounded displeased. “I thought His Royal Highness always cleans his hands first before going inside. Why not today?”","The crown prince acted as if they didn’t exist.","Granny Gong glanced at the maid.","The empress dowager had sent over a few maids the other day and had left specific instructions that Bixi here should work as the crown prince’s chambermaid.","Of course, Granny Gong didn’t dare do that. She could only have Bixi stay close to her, so that she could see the crown prince often enough. Maybe she would get noticed one day that way.","But Granny Gong felt that the chances were very low.","She had to admit that Bixi was indeed very pretty.","But —","Granny Gong shook her head with a wry smile. She was only pretty, not stunning.","Compared with Feng Wu, Bixi was nothing.","Seeing the ambitious look on Bixi’s face, Granny Gong shook her head.","“Granny Gong, His Royal Highness hasn’t washed his hands yet. Let me bring these to him.”","After that, Bixi casually took the towels and had a younger maid pick up the hot water.","Granny Gong stared at her with a dark face. “Stop right there!”","“Granny Gong?” Bixi gave her an arrogant glance.","Before she came here, the empress dowager told her that she was a blessed girl. If she could give birth to a boy, she could become one of the crown prince’s senior concubines.","If she could become a senior concubine, there was a chance she could become an imperial consort in the future!","Granny Gong could sell the other maids however she wanted, but Bixi was someone the empress dowager had high hopes for.","Staring at her with cold eyes, Granny Gong told a younger maid to snatch the towels back.","“If you want to live, you’ll have to be a lot more obedient.”","After that —"]},{"number":1421,"title":"Chapter 1421 - Be My Little Maid (5)","paragraphs":["Granny Gong led the others away, leaving Bixi behind.","Bixi looked unconvinced.","She was confident that once the crown prince saw her, he would be attracted by her beauty.","Feng Wu had no idea that an ambitious girl had arrived at the crown prince’s residence.","Thump!","The crown prince casually threw Feng Wu onto the soft bed after he walked into his study.","Rubbing her arms, which were hurting from being carried around, Feng Wu glared at Jun Linyuan.","The crown prince closed the door behind him when he walked in and ignored Feng Wu after that.","Feng Wu simply found him ridiculous.","Why was Jun Linyuan doing this? She had only teased him over how innocent he was; did he have to be so angry?","Hmph! She decided that she would ignore him as well.","Instead of getting up, she slouched back on the soft bed and turned her back on Jun Linyuan.","Probably exhausted by the day’s events, Feng Wu gradually felt her eyelids grow heavy.","In the end, she fell asleep.","When she woke up, it was two hours later.","She sat up, holding the duvet and rubbing her sleepy eyes. The warm candlelight on the wall gradually reminded her of today’s events.","She recalled everything that had happened in the immortal flower grove today, the fact that Jun Linyuan had snatched her, and...","And she fell asleep when she was still mad at Jun Linyuan. How incredible!","Feng Wu patted her own head in frustration. She then turned her head and looked around.","She saw Jun Linyuan working at his table.","In the dim light, she saw his profile, with his chiseled jaw and deep-set features.","He wore a thin robe with a heavy cape over his shoulders, looking elegant and majestic.","He was reading a memorial to the throne.","Feng Wu knew that Jun Linyuan was raised as the future heir to the throne.","It was common knowledge that being the crown prince was the most difficult job in the world.","Because of their “tenure,” all emperors held complicated and conflicted feelings toward their crown princes.","An emperor would feel threatened if the crown prince was too active and became too popular among the officials.","But if the crown prince was too mediocre, the emperor would doubt if he was suitable for the job.","And it became even harder for the crown prince if the emperor lived to a very old age.","All crown princes hence trod on thin ice and lived difficult lives.","However, Jun Linyuan was quite comfortable in his role.","He had a short temper, could be arrogant or cruel at times, and would do whatever he wanted without any scruples.","Despite that, the officials thought highly of him, the commoners admired him, and even the emperor himself couldn’t do anything about his willfulness.","Feng Wu felt that compared with Jun Linyuan, Emperor Wu looked more like a wronged little wife, while his son was the great fiend.","Resting her chin on one hand, Feng Wu studied Jun Linyuan’s well-defined face with her curious, twinkling eyes.","The crown prince was reading a memorial to the throne.","Since he was the crown prince, he would receive copies of all the memorials to the throne.","He was a very fast reader, and it only took him a quick glance to memorize the content.","State affairs that would take Emperor Wu ten hours to sort through would only take Jun Linyuan one hour, and he was able to give advice afterward.","Handling state affairs was a walk in the park.","However, instead of quickly going through the memorial to the throne this time, he was stuck on a line and couldn’t turn a page."]},{"number":1422,"title":"Chapter 1422 - Be My Little Maid (6)","paragraphs":["Because Feng Wu was staring at him.","With his keen senses, he had been aware of Feng Wu’s gaze as soon as she woke up.","For some unknown reason, the girl kept staring at him, as if she was trying to solve a puzzle.","Under her gaze, the crown prince felt the temperature in his cheeks rise, and somehow, he was reminded of what he had seen in the bushes earlier.","But this time, the girl had Feng Wu’s face...","When he realized what was going on, Jun Linyuan felt like he had been struck by lightning.","What on earth was he thinking?","Thump!","Frustrated, Jun Linyuan smashed his fist on the table.","The impact sent all the memorials to the throne to the floor.","Feng Wu jumped at the noise as well.","“What’s wrong?” Before she knew it, Feng Wu had rushed over to Jun Linyuan’s side.","The memorials had fallen all over the floor, as if they were common letters.","But so many things were at stake in each and every one.","This was the political center of the empire, and the slightest change could have the greatest impact.","Feng Wu was even more confused when she saw how frustrated Jun Linyuan looked. “Jun Linyuan, you —”","However, the crown prince shoved Feng Wu to the side and marched out of the room. Before Feng Wu could say anything, Jun Linyuan was out of sight.","She was dumbfounded.","What on earth happened?","Feng Wu shook her head in resignation and couldn’t for the life of her think of an explanation, but she didn’t linger on the question.","She looked around and saw all the memorials scattered on the floor as if they were garbage. What a willful crown prince!","Crouching down, she picked up all the memorials, sorted them out, and put them back on the desk.","Just then —","There was a gentle tap on the door.","What?","Feng Wu was surprised.","She had been here at the crown prince’s residence many times, but she couldn’t recall anyone daring to disturb Jun Linyuan.","Certainly no one had dared knock on his door.","Feng Wu opened the door out of curiosity.","A beautiful young woman stood outside with a tray, which had a bowl on it. The content looked like...","Hm... was that white fungus soup with lotus seeds? Feng Wu remembered that Jun Linyuan hated sticky soup like this.","The girl wore the thinnest dress Feng Wu had ever seen. It consisted of a single layer of gauze, which did nothing to hide her curves.","“Your Royal...” Before Bixi could finish greeting the crown prince, she saw that the person in front of her was a girl.","While Feng Wu was looking her up and down, she was doing the same.","“You —” Bixi reacted first, and she was full of jealousy when she stared at Feng Wu.","She was so beautiful!","Her beauty was stunning, not to mention her fair skin was impeccable.","She was still young and hadn’t reached her potential, but her innocence reminded one of the spring sun, the morning dew, and the beauty of life.","Bixi was very displeased.","She glared at Feng Wu. “Who are you, and what are you doing here?! Aren’t all maids forbidden to come here to the study? How did you get in?!”","Bixi’s eyes lit up when she saw the memorials in Feng Wu’s hands, and she yelled, “Guards! Guards! There’s an assassin here! Come here!”","Security was the top priority in the crown prince’s residence, and there were guards everywhere.","Therefore, hearing Bixi’s cry —"]},{"number":1423,"title":"Chapter 1423 - Pretty Slave","paragraphs":["She glared at Feng Wu. “Who are you, and what are you doing here?! Aren’t all maids forbidden to come here to the study? How did you get in?!”","Bixi’s eyes lit up when she saw the memorials in Feng Wu’s hands, and she yelled, “Guards! Guards! There’s an assassin here! Come here!”","Security was the top priority in the crown prince’s residence, and there were guards everywhere.","Therefore, hearing Bixi’s cry —","Everyone was instantly alarmed.","And several people rushed toward the study.","Seeing them, Bixi shouted, “Come over here! Quickly! This woman broke into His Royal Highness’s study! She must be a mole! Catch her! No, kill her!”","All the secret guards around the study and posted throughout the residence were very loyal to Jun Linyuan.","They took orders from him and no one else.","To them, Feng Wu wasn’t an acquaintance, but she wasn’t a stranger either, as she had visited the residence a few times already.","Thus, the leader of the guards seemed slightly displeased when he saw that Feng Wu was the “assassin.”","Bixi said hastily, “Take her down! Now!”","However, the leader only cast a stern look at Bixi before walking away.","That look made Bixi shudder.","The next thing she knew, the leader was leaving.","“Hey, Lou Xuan! Why are you leaving? Shouldn’t you arrest her? Aren’t you afraid that His Royal Highness will punish you?!”","Bixi and Lou Xuan both grew up in the imperial palace, and their paths had crossed when they were little. While Bixi was sent away to learn how to please men, Lou Xuan went on to learn martial arts.","This was their first meeting after growing up.","Even though Bixi recognized him, Lou Xuan didn’t stop. He quickly led his men back to their positions.","“Hey —”","Infuriated, Bixi shouted after him.","The residence was very quiet after dark, so much so that one could hear leaves falling from the trees.","Bixi’s voice hence sounded very out of place.","Soon, Granny Gong arrived in a hurry.","“What’s going on here?!”","Her face was livid.","The crown prince’s residence ran smoothly under her supervision. All the servants did their jobs properly and no one made any unnecessary sounds.","This Bixi had been disobeying the rules just because she had been sent here from the imperial palace by the empress dowager herself, and Granny Gong had been enduring her behavior until now.","Seeing Granny Gong, Bixi quickly walked up to her and tried to take her arm.","However, Granny Gong drew her hand back and stared at Bixi.","“Granny Gong...” Bixi pursed her lips, pointed at Feng Wu, and whined, “This woman is a mole! She was tampering with His Royal Highness’s memorials! She’s after court secrets! We have to take her down before she escapes...”","Granny Gong stared at Bixi and found her an utter idiot.","However, Bixi had no idea how foolish her accusation was. Instead, she tried to make up more stories. “Granny Gong, I’m telling the truth. She was trying to steal the memorials! She really was...”","Granny Gong had had enough of her idiotic speech. “Do you know who she is?”","Bixi looked dumbfounded. The answer was obviously no.","“Who is she? Isn’t she some slave His Royal Highness brought back?” And this slave was too pretty to be real!"]},{"number":1424,"title":"Chapter 1424 - What if I Say No?","paragraphs":["Granny Gong was speechless.","A slave?","Granny Gong wanted to laugh out loud.","She was about to say something, when she realized a serious problem.","Last time when she was at court, the empress dowager had probed around, asking what the relationship between the crown prince and Feng Wu was like and if they were frequently in contact with each other. It was obvious that she didn’t like Feng Wu. Afterward, she gifted Jun Linyuan with a few teenage girls, like Bixi, who had been trained to please men.","Granny Gong remembered that the empress dowager used to give Jun Linyuan women before, but she stopped after he threw a tantrum.","But now, it was starting again...","Intuition told Granny Gong that she should keep the crown prince and Feng Wu’s relationship from Bixi, because Bixi had direct access to the empress dowager.","Moreover, Granny Gong had also learned that Bixi was from an influential family and had a well-connected father. Therefore...","At that thought, Granny Gong threw a dirty look at Bixi and said, “Get her out of here!”","Bixi’s eyes widened, and she stared at Granny Gong in disbelief.","“Granny Gong, are you serious? Get me out of here? You should arrest her and execute her!”","At Granny Gong’s command, some servants took Bixi by the arms, but she struggled violently.","She made all sorts of threats as she struggled.","“Granny Gong, why are you on her side? Are you on her payroll or what? You’re a team, aren’t you?!”","Granny Gong rubbed her forehead.","She couldn’t for the life of her figure out how someone as stupid as Bixi could have survived in court, let alone be selected by the empress dowager.","No matter how loudly she yelled, Granny Gong only ignored her.","“Miss Feng, sorry about the disturbance.” Granny Gong apologized to Feng Wu.","Feng Wu waved at Granny Gong as if the little incident didn’t bother her.","“By the way —” Granny Gong looked up and a pretty young maid walked over with a tray.","Granny Gong then smiled at Feng Wu. “Miss Feng, I need a little favor from you.”","Feng Wu glanced at the tray that was covered with a red cloth and was confused. “Granny Gong, what’s this about?”","Granny Gong smiled. “Her Majesty the empress dowager sent us this cooling soap as a gift, and His Royal Highness can really use it right now. So, Miss Feng, would you please take it inside?”","“Inside? Where?” Feng Wu seemed alarmed.","Granny Gong smiled. “The bath hall, of course.”","Feng Wu frowned. “Granny Gong, this is such a precious gift; don’t you think you should handle it yourself?”","Granny Gong smiled and said, “Miss Feng, since you’ll have to go inside anyway, why don’t you take it with you?”","Feng Wu stared at Granny Gong. “I’m going inside? Says who? That’s not going to happen!”","Granny Gong seemed confused. “But it’s His Royal Highness’s order.”","Feng Wu was speechless.","Jun Linyuan just wouldn’t let a day pass without making her life miserable.","Feng Wu said, “What did His Royal Highness say?”","Granny Gong smiled at Feng Wu. “His Royal Highness said that since you’re his personal maid now, you’ll have to do all the intimate things a personal maid is supposed to do.”","Feng Wu asked, “All the intimate things?”","Granny Gong nodded.","Feng Wu asked, “What if I say no?”","Granny Gong chuckled. “No one in this world has ever dared defy His Royal Highness, so Miss Wu, don’t act like a baby. Just hurry up.”","Act like a baby? Feng Wu rolled her eyes. When did she ever act like a baby?!","“What if I refuse?” Feng Wu gritted her teeth."]},{"number":1425,"title":"Chapter 1425 - Young Tigress","paragraphs":["Granny Gong was still smiling. “Miss Wu, I think you know what His Royal Highness is capable of.”","Feng Wu rested her hands on her waist and stuck out her chest. “I’m not afraid of him!”","Granny Gong smiled. “I know you’re not, but what about your family? By the way, I forgot to tell you —","“Miss Wu, while you’re with His Royal Highness, Young Master Qi will be staying with the imperial guards.”","Feng Wu narrowed her eyes in an intimidating way.","How dare Jun Linyuan touch her family?!","Feng Wu smiled coldly. She then snatched the tray from the maid and charged into the bath hall with the cooling soap.","Meanwhile, a pair of eyes stared at Feng Wu from a distance.","The look in those eyes was a mix of jealousy and cold hatred...","Thump!","Feng Wu kicked the door open and charged in.","Hot steam filled the room and the heat blew into her face.","Through the coiling steam, she saw Jun Linyuan sitting in the hot spring and leaning against the edge. She could see his fair chest and exquisite collarbones.","He raised his eyebrows when he heard the noise.","Feng Wu marched to his side and glared at him.","Jun Linyuan seemed to have anticipated her anger, so he was able to keep his expression completely unperturbed.","“How did you get in here?” He glanced casually at her.","Feng Wu found him ridiculous.","He had forced her to come here by taking Xiaoqi, but now, he was asking why she was here.","“You know perfectly well why I’m here!” Resting her hands on her waist, Feng Wu glowered.","The crown prince looked perfectly innocent when he raised his chin. “How am I supposed to know that?”","“Fine!” Feng Wu glared at him. “If you don’t need me here, I’m off!”","She then marched back toward the door.","However, just before she stepped out, the open door slammed shut with a loud bang.","Feng Wu had run so fast that she almost bumped her nose on the door. Luckily, she reacted in time and stopped herself with a hand.","Enraged, she turned around and glared at Jun Linyuan.","The crown prince looked as innocent as before and was even in the mood to play with the water.","Feng Wu was so angry that her brain almost stopped working. She ran up to Jun Linyuan and said angrily, “You did that on purpose!”","Jun Linyuan nodded lazily.","Feng Wu was furious.","“You actually nodded?!” Feng Wu pointed at Jun Linyuan. “You forced me to come here but won’t talk to me when I’m in the room, nor will you allow me to leave. Jun Linyuan, what on earth do you want?”","Only Jun Linyuan could make Feng Wu so angry.","Hearing Feng Wu’s question, he relaxed and gave Feng Wu an indifferent glance. “Yes.”","What was that supposed to mean?!","Feng Wu wanted to smack his head.","“Jun Linyuan, you’re threatening me with Xiaoqi’s safety. How dare you?!” The more Feng Wu thought about it, the angrier she got.","She was usually a very calm person, and no one ever saw her like this. She was always so composed and unperturbed.","But somehow, she always turned into a jumpy tigress whenever Jun Linyuan was around.","The crown prince was amused when he saw how agitated the girl was.","She always looked as if nothing could affect her, and no 13-year-old girl should look like that."]},{"number":1426,"title":"Chapter 1426 - I Can Keep My Word!","paragraphs":["Therefore, the crown prince felt very proud to be able to make her lose control.","“Come here.” Despite how he felt, his expression still remained arrogant and undisturbed.","“Hah!” Feng Wu smirked. “Explain yourself! Otherwise, I’ll never let this drop! What did you do to Xiaoqi? Tell me!”","Jun Linyuan smiled. “Little Feng Wu, whether he’ll get his ass kicked or enjoy some quality cultivation time will depend on how you behave in the next 18 days, got it?”","Feng Wu clenched her fists. Blue veins popped in the corner of her forehead and smoke practically rose out of her head.","How could someone be so abominable?!","“So, are you going to honor our deal or not?” Throwing his head back, the crown prince downed the wine in his amber glass and glanced at Feng Wu.","Feng Wu was about to answer, when the fairy spoke in her head.","“Master, Master, wait!”","“Hm?”","Feng Wu’s stomach lurched whenever the fairy spoke and she always got a bad feeling.","The fairy said in a frustrated voice, “Master, I have bad news!”","That made Feng Wu jump.","The fairy wailed, “The 6th trial has stopped moving forward!”","What?!","Feng Wu frowned. “What happened? Haven’t I finished that trial already?”","She remembered clearly that she had to give Jun Linyuan the flowers for the 5th trial and he had to give them back for the 6th. She had already taken those flowers, so why had it stopped moving forward?","She then heard the fairy’s voice.","“Master, the 6th trial is only 99.99% complete, and...”","“And what?”","“And it has been extended to 18 days!”","Feng Wu was speechless.","She realized what was going on. The duration of this trial had just been extended to 18 days because of her deal with Jun Linyuan.","That was to say, if she failed to work as Jun Linyuan’s personal maid for the next 18 days, she would fail the trial as well!","How could this happen?! Feng Wu looked frustrated and was sure that the system had something against her.","Why was it acting like a stepmother and treating her this way?!","Just then, she heard Jun Linyuan’s arrogant voice.","“If you don’t want the job, so many people can’t wait to take your place. Leave, then,” he said without hesitation.","Feng Wu looked at Jun Linyuan with teary eyes.","If the system was her stepmother, it was definitely Jun Linyuan’s loving biological mother!","“I... I... I can keep my word! I won’t be seen as an untrustworthy person!”","Feng Wu clenched her fists and opened her big black eyes very wide. She looked like she was going to cry.","The crown prince gave a small smile which quickly disappeared, but Feng Wu was too vexed to notice.","“Scrub my back,” the crown prince prompted her.","“Fine...” Feng Wu reluctantly inched toward him, fetched a clean towel, and was going to scrub his back.","But —","“Feng Wu, is that how you serve your master?” the crown prince said.","“What now?”","Jun Linyuan said, “Can’t you see five bath towels on the shelf?”","Feng Wu nodded. “I did see them. They’re all made from different fabrics and are in different sizes.”"]},{"number":1427,"title":"Chapter 1427 - I Want to Tell You —","paragraphs":["Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","“Didn’t Granny Gong teach you what to do? You use the phoenix towel for the first wash, the bath towel for the second, and for the third...”","“Gosh, you can’t possibly be serious!” Feng Wu cut him off. “Even as a girl, I only use a single wash cloth when I take a bath. Why do you use a different cloth for each wash? Don’t you find that redundant?”","The crown prince pouted a little.","That was how Granny Gong had taught his servants since he was little.","Feng Wu went on, “Plus, this first one is made of high-quality cloud satin, which is a tribute from the Botu tribe, and the second is a tribute from the Wuming tribe... Jun Linyuan, please don’t tell me that you wash your face with all these towels.”","Jun Linyuan bit his lower lip.","Feng Wu said, “These five pieces of cloth alone are worth tens of thousands of gold taels, and that’s as valuable as ten top-grade spiritual stones! Jun Linyuan, you’re so wasteful!”","Turning around, Jun Linyuan frowned when he saw Feng Wu putting the used towels back onto the shelf. “What are you doing?”","Feng Wu said, “Obviously I’m putting back the used ones so that Granny Gong can fetch them later and have them washed.”","“Wash them?”","The idea had never occurred to Jun Linyuan, and he gave Feng Wu a strange look. “What needs to be washed?”","“What needs to be washed?”","Feng Wu also gave Jun Linyuan a strange look. “These towels need to be cleaned before they can be used again, don’t they?”","The crown prince stared at Feng Wu as if he was looking at a mad person. He had to reassure himself that she wasn’t insane before he frowned and said, “Throw them away.”","“What?” Feng Wu’s eyes widened. She even stuck her fingers in her ears to clean them out.","“Am I hearing things?”","“I’m not going to repeat myself again. Throw them away!” The crown prince’s face darkened.","Feng Wu jumped to her feet. “Jun Linyuan, what’s wrong with you?! These are very expensive materials sent here by various tribes as tribute. You can’t buy them anywhere! You’re throwing them away after one use?!”","The crown prince said, “Yup.”","Feng Wu almost choked. “Do you know that these five pieces are worth at least ten top-grade spiritual stones?”","Jun Linyuan said proudly, “Yes.”","Feng Wu said, “Ten top-grade spiritual stones! People out there can bash each other’s head in for a mere low-grade spiritual stone, and you’re throwing away ten top-grade ones after each bath!”","The crown prince said confidently, “That’s because I’m the crown prince.”","So, that was how a crown prince was supposed to be treated.","Feng Wu didn’t know what to say.","She vented her sarcasm quietly. “Why should they bother fighting over a low-grade spiritual stone if they can just go digging in the trash can of the crown prince’s residence?”","The crown prince glanced at Feng Wu and said, “They’ll be burned. Nothing will get out.”","Feng Wu was speechless. It had to be done. Otherwise, it was possible that people would pay hundreds of top-grade spiritual stones for a bath towel that had been used by Jun Linyuan.","Some comparisons just couldn’t be made.","After Jun Linyuan’s retort, Feng Wu couldn’t be bothered to talk to him anymore. She lowered her head and focused on scrubbing his back.","Scars criss-crossed over Jun Linyuan’s fair skin. Some were from whips, some were left by swords, and some were from other weapons.","Feng Wu knew that there had to be a complicated story behind each one, but she also knew that the more she knew, the more danger she would be in. Therefore, she remained silent.","Instead —","Jun Linyuan casually asked, “Aren’t you curious?”","Still scrubbing his back with her head lowered, Feng Wu asked, “About what?”","“Aren’t you curious why a crown prince has so many scars on him?” Jun Linyuan seemed to be in the mood to chat again."]},{"number":1428,"title":"Chapter 1428 - Feng Wu, You’re So Annoying!","paragraphs":["However, Jun Linyuan had found the wrong person to talk to.","If Feng Wu wanted to get to know Jun Linyuan better and see into his soul, now would be the best chance. However —","Feng Wu dreaded the thought.","The last thing she wanted to do was to know Jun Linyuan better, because he was so terrifying. She had a premonition that if she got involved with him, he would trouble her for the rest of her life!","Hence, Feng Wu declined outright. “No, please say no more. I don’t want to hear it.”","The crown prince immediately stiffened.","He wouldn’t be so mad if Feng Wu had been a bit more tactful.","But she was so straightforward!","Feng Wu could sense his muscles stiffen under her palms.","Hot steam had been rising out of the pool and filling the air, but at that moment, it turned into frost and...","The bubbling hot spring started to freeze up!","Crack —","Ice spread out over the pool as Feng Wu watched.","She was alarmed by a sense of extreme danger.","Instinctively, she started moving backward.","However, she barely took a step before Jun Linyuan grabbed her hand.","Thump —","Poor Feng Wu. Jun Linyuan pulled her down into the pool before she could put up a fight.","It wouldn’t be so bad if the water was warm, but it had already frozen!","Crack!","Flung out, Feng Wu landed on her back with a thump, the impact from hitting the ice sending a sharp pain down her spine.","However, before she could return to her senses, Jun Linyuan had already grabbed her hand.","Feng Wu was still feeling dizzy when she was forced to meet Jun Linyuan’s furious eyes.","His eyes were bloodshot and had a murderous look in them.","And that wasn’t the most terrifying part. Right now, Jun Linyuan looked like a king of magical beasts who had lost his mind and was ready to charge out.","No one knew what such a destructive creature could do.","Feng Wu’s pupils contracted.","There was fear and reverence in her eyes, but more than that, there was confusion.","“J- Jun Linyuan... W- What are you doing?” Feng Wu’s voice trembled a little.","Jun Linyuan’s face was livid, and the bulging blue veins on the back of his hands looked like they were going to explode at any moment!","He was furious, but she still didn’t know why? The idea only made the crown prince angrier.","“Feng Wu, are you trying to give me a stroke?!","“Are you really so ignorant, or are you pretending to be innocent?!","“Do you have any idea how I...”","He stopped abruptly before he could finish the sentence.","He couldn’t say it now. The first one to express their feelings lost! He would never allow himself to be the loser!","Jun Linyuan lost control for a moment and tightened his grip.","“Ouch, that hurts...”","Feng Wu thought her bones were going to break and the pain brought tears to her eyes.","Jun Linyuan only came back to his senses a little when he saw Feng Wu’s tears.","He looked down and saw Feng Wu’s hand.","Her hands had always been so fair and impeccable, but now, there was a heavy bruise around her wrist.","Angry and frustrated, Jun Linyuan threw a dirty look at Feng Wu and finally let go of her hand.","Feng Wu was instinctively afraid of Jun Linyuan, and she immediately took a step back.","Jun Linyuan frowned and was displeased.","Why did she keep running away from him? Was he that frightening?","He yelled at Feng Wu, “Stop right there!”"]},{"number":1429,"title":"Chapter 1429 - Eavesdropping","paragraphs":["Feng Wu jumped out of the pool and ran toward the door at top speed!","She was running away?","Infuriated, Jun Linyuan jumped out of the pool as well.","Feng Wu was more level-headed in a critical moment like this, so when she ran for the door, she picked up both Jun Linyuan’s dirty and clean clothes.","Only after she rushed outside with all the clothes did Jun Linyuan realize that he was half-naked when he was almost at the door.","Exasperated, he bellowed, “Damn you! Get back here!”","Feng Wu only heaved a sigh of relief when she saw that Jun Linyuan had stopped inside. Still holding the clothes, she turned around and made a face. “I won’t! Catch me if you can!”","Jun Linyuan yelled, “Feng Wu, do you have a death wish?!”","Feng Wu said, “Come and get me.”","Jun Linyuan said, “What makes you think I won’t?!”","Feng Wu said, “What are you waiting for, then?”","Jun Linyuan was so furious that he almost laughed. Gritting his teeth, he said, “Little Feng Wu, I’m going to give you one last chance!”","Feng Wu grinned. “You can keep the chance! What can you possibly do to me?!”","What were Feng and Granny Gong doing when the young couple was bickering?","While the crown prince’s residence was very spacious, it was usually very quiet. Therefore, the slightest noise was very obvious.","How could Feng and Granny Gong not notice the quarrel between Feng Wu and Jun Linyuan?","They ran out of their rooms as soon as they heard it.","However, they stopped abruptly when they turned a corner, because they could clearly hear the two teenagers’ voices.","Sure enough, they heard the childish quarrel.","Feng and Granny Gong were both speechless.","They couldn’t begin to describe what they were feeling right now.","She was the new star of the imperial capital, someone who had risen again after her downfall, while he was the arrogant crown prince as well as a formidable warrior.","They were both very sensitive about their reputations when they were around other people, but now, they were fighting like two kids.","Feng cleared his throat. “Ahem. Deep down, His Royal Highness is still a child.”","Granny Gong rubbed her forehead. “His Royal Highness was never like this.”","Feng rubbed his chin and said calmly, “That’s because he had yet to meet the right opponent.”","Granny Gong agreed. It seemed that the crown prince only behaved this way when he was around Feng Wu.","But she was still worried. “Are you sure this is good for His Royal Highness?”","Feng glanced at Granny Gong. “Why not? His Royal Highness never smiled when he was little. By the time he turned three, he already looked like a 60-year-old. Too many people placed too many expectations on him when he was growing up, and he’s always been under more pressure than anyone can imagine. Isn’t it nice to have someone who can turn him into a child once again?”","Granny Gong still wanted to say something, but Feng cut her off. “Plus, cultivation is all about a balance between tension and relaxation. His Royal Highness has been under a lot of stress for so many years; a little relaxation may do him good.”","That immediately persuaded Granny Gong, and she nodded. “That’s true. If that’s the case, Miss Feng Wu has done us a great favor!”","While Feng and Granny Gong were enjoying the show, someone else was standing in a corner a hundred meters away.","Bixi wasn’t allowed to go near the hot spring and had to eavesdrop from afar."]},{"number":1430,"title":"Chapter 1430 - No! I Won’t Give Them to You! Hmph!","paragraphs":["Seeing the way Feng Wu and Jun Linyuan bickered and how agitated the crown prince was, Bixi clenched her fists in jealousy.","Other people might think that Jun Linyuan and Feng Wu were quarreling, but Bixi had been learning such things since she was little, and she knew better.","With His Royal Highness’s temperament, if he didn’t like a person, all he needed to do was flip a sleeve, and they would be annihilated. There was no need to quarrel.","Therefore, if a girl could bring out the crown prince’s childish side, she had to be very special to him!","Her Majesty the empress dowager had to know about this!","At that thought, Bixi quietly retreated.","Meanwhile, Feng Wu had no idea that someone else had seen her little confrontation with Jun Linyuan. She was too busy driving Jun Linyuan crazy.","“Nope! I’m not giving them back to you! Hmph!” Feng Wu said proudly.","“Show yourselves already! Are you waiting for an invitation?!”","Jun Linyuan yelled at a corner.","Feng Wu turned around to see Feng and Granny Gong step out of their hiding place.","Feng Wu wept inwardly...","At her current cultivation level, she indeed wasn’t capable enough to detect them...","Feng and Granny Gong looked straight ahead when they walked past Feng Wu, but Granny Gong still took the clothes away from her.","Jun Linyuan gave Feng Wu a threatening look. “Just wait and see!”","“You big baby!” Feng Wu stuck out her tongue at him before jumping onto the wall and trying to dash off.","However —","This was the crown prince’s residence.","With the crown prince’s permission, Feng Wu could go wherever she wanted.","But if he wouldn’t give that permission —","“Ouch —”","Feng Wu jumped onto the wall, only to see a dark shadow moving quickly toward her. Before she knew it, she fell down and hit the ground with a loud thump.","The fully dressed crown prince strolled to her side.","Crouching down, he studied her with a complacent look in his twinkling eyes. The next second, he caught Feng Wu’s chin with his slender, fair fingers.","Feng Wu glared at him. “Jun Linyuan, you had help! That’s not fair!”","Jun Linyuan only smirked. “Is that so?”","Thinking that she had turned things around, Feng Wu nodded repeatedly. “Yes!”","Jun Linyuan said, “So what?”","Feng Wu was dumbfounded. “Huh?”","Jun Linyuan said, “This is the crown prince’s residence, and they’re all my people. So what if I had help?”","Feng Wu stammered, “You, you...”","Jun Linyuan snorted and rose to his feet. “Tidy her up. She looks like a dirty little beggar now.”","He promptly turned to leave after that, as if Feng Wu was just a discarded doll...","If Granny Gong and Feng didn’t know that Jun Linyuan had feelings for Feng Wu, they really would think that he didn’t like her.","“Tell her that she’s cooking dinner tonight!” Jun Linyuan had Granny Gong pass on his command instead.","Obviously, he was still mad at her for what she did earlier.","“Is it Your Royal Highness’s dinner, or...” Granny Gong asked.","Jun Linyuan gave Granny Gong a sidelong glance. “The entire residence, obviously! No one is allowed to help her!”","He walked away after that.","Granny Gong frowned. Cooking dinner for the entire crown prince’s residence was a lot of work. Things were getting complicated.","At that thought, Granny Gong gave Feng Wu a sympathetic glance. “Miss Wu...”","Feng Wu waved her off. “Granny Gong, just tell me, how many people are there in the residence?”"]},{"number":1431,"title":"Chapter 1431 - I’m Jun Linyuan’s Least Favorite Person","paragraphs":["Feng Wu looked at Granny Gong. “Granny Gong, please tell me how many people there are in the residence.”","Granny Gong looked at Feng Wu sympathetically. “In total? 3,000.”","Feng Wu drew in her breath. “That many?”","Granny Gong smiled wryly. “That’s already fewer than before. A lot more people used to work here, but His Royal Highness didn’t like all the noise, so he let a lot of them go. Miss Wu, as you know, His Royal Highness is the heir to the throne and our future emperor. There are bound to be a lot of servants here.”","Feng Wu rubbed her forehead. She had just disrespected the future emperor; she should count herself very lucky to still be alive.","She had to cook for 3,000 people now.","“There are requirements for the meals here, right?” Feng Wu asked.","Granny Gong gave her a sympathetic look. “Yes. His Royal Highness’s dinner consists of thirty dishes, and dinner for the stewards consists of ten, and after that...”","Feng Wu listened in astonishment.","Forget the stewards and servants, Jun Linyuan’s dinner alone would be a lot of work. It was unbelievable!","Feng Wu asked Granny Gong, “And when do you usually have dinner?”","Granny Gong gave her another sympathetic look. “You only have two hours left.”","Feng Wu almost fainted.","Granny Gong nodded. “Yes, Miss Wu, you’ll have to prepare tens of thousands of dishes in two hours...”","This mission was impossible!","There were over a hundred chefs and assistants in the kitchen here.","Feng Wu pulled a long face. “Jun Linyuan gave me an impossible job!”","Granny Gong and the maids around her all nodded.","That was more than impossible. He was purposely making her life miserable.","Feng Wu lowered her head in frustration.","Granny Gong said sympathetically, “Miss Wu, how about you talk to His Royal Highness? He’s always been nice to you. I’m sure he’ll change his mind if you ask for his help.”","Feng Wu stared at Granny Gong in resignation and spoke in an exaggerated tone. “He’s always been nice to me? Granny Gong, you must be mistaken! He’s the worst! Otherwise, he wouldn’t be giving me trouble and making me angry all the time!”","Granny Gong was speechless.","She felt a little conflicted, because she couldn’t tell Feng Wu that the crown prince had a strange habit of picking on the person he liked.","Seeing that Granny Gong was speechless, Feng Wu was satisfied. “I’m right, aren’t I? I’m Jun Linyuan’s least favorite person!”","Granny Gong was speechless.","If one person in a relationship was silly, it was still manageable, but if both had no idea what was going on, what else was there to be done? Granny Gong was so worried.","Granny Gong heaved a sigh and changed the subject. “Miss Wu, what are you going to do?”","The others all looked worried as well.","Feng Wu rubbed her chin and fell into thought.","There were so many people in the crown prince’s residence, and since it involved their dinner and no one was told to keep the news a secret, the entire household soon heard about it.","Every servant in the crown prince’s residence was talking about it.","“Wait, Miss Wu is going to cook dinner for us? I can’t wait.”","“Why? She can’t possibly finish it.”","“Why do you say that?”","“Why do you think? We need tens of thousands of dishes, and no one is allowed to help her. She can’t possibly finish them all even if she has three pairs of hands!”","“You’re right. So... is His Royal Highness punishing Miss Wu?”","“Does His Royal Highness not like Miss Wu anymore?”"]},{"number":1432,"title":"Chapter 1432 - Jun Linyuan’s Unspoken Feelings","paragraphs":["“So, has Miss Wu fallen out of favor?”","–","Someone listening quietly in the crowd smiled in satisfaction.","It was none other than Zhen Xia, the senior maid.","She had been laying low these days and trying not to be noticed. In fact, she worked for Zuo Qingluan and would tell the latter everything that was going on in the crown prince’s residence.","“Feng Wu, I didn’t expect you to fall out of favor so quickly. There I was, feeling so threatened by you. Heh.”","Zhen Xia smirked and left.","And she wasn’t the only maid in the crown prince’s residence to think like that; the other women secretly rejoiced and couldn’t wait to see Feng Wu embarrass herself.","In the study.","Jun Linyuan sat on the couch next to the window and read some memorials to the throne.","Feng walked in and stood quietly by his side","Jun Linyuan hadn’t turned a page since Feng came back and was waiting for Feng to tell him what was going outside.","However...","Feng stood there without uttering a word, which baffled Jun Linyuan.","Frustrated, he threw the memorial away and rose to his feet.","After pacing for a moment, he couldn’t help but turn around and stare at Feng. However, he feigned an indifferent tone when he asked, “Did you just come back?”","Feng said, “Yes, Your Royal Highness.”","Jun Linyuan asked, “How’s that stupid girl doing? Has she finished cooking?”","Feng could see that Jun Linyuan was trying to hide his concern and he chose his words carefully.","After some thought, Feng gave him a wry smile. “Your Royal Highness, the task is really difficult. There are 3,000 people in this residence, and she’ll have to cook at least 10,000 dishes. Moreover, your food requires a careful combination of spiritual essence, and it’s less than two hours to the start of dinner... No mortal man would be able to achieve that in time.”","Jun Linyuan was a little dumbfounded when he heard that.","Rubbing his sculpted chin, he said, “I didn’t know it was going to be that difficult.”","Feng smiled in resignation. “It really is. The job is usually done by hundreds of cooks over a few hours, but you ordered Miss Wu to finish it all by herself in two hours. That was... Your Royal Highness, isn’t that a bit too much?”","Jun Linyuan was one of the smartest people in the empire, so when he could think straight again, he immediately realized how difficult the task was.","It took time to cook.","However, as arrogant as he was, he would never admit his fault.","Despite his concern, he smirked. “She has to take responsibility for what she did! I’ve already given her a light punishment! Hmph!”","Feng shook his head. The crown prince could be very stubborn.","He then asked casually, “Your Royal Highness, what did Miss Wu do to make you so angry?”","Jun Linyuan didn’t know what to say.","He couldn’t tell Feng that it was because Feng Wu had refused to listen when he wanted to talk. Feng would laugh at him if he told the truth; Jun Linyuan wouldn’t stand for such humiliation!","Jun Linyuan immediately went scarlet in the face and bellowed, “Are you curious?”","Feng knew his young master too well. He immediately realized that Jun Linyuan was angry from shame.","So he waved his hands repeatedly. “No, no, no. I’m not curious at all. I’ll go check on Miss Feng Wu.”","As he backed away, he gave Jun Linyuan an enquiring look.","“Just go!” Jun Linyuan thought."]},{"number":1433,"title":"Chapter 1433 - The Impossible","paragraphs":["However, Feng didn’t leave. Instead, he gave the crown prince a searching look. “Your Royal Highness, may I go?”","Jun Linyuan wanted to kick him. Of course he could go! What was he waiting for?","“Your Royal Highness, I’ll be on my way, then?” Feng asked deliberately.","Jun Linyuan almost exploded.","He said, “Yes, if you want to!”","Feng said, “Well, I don’t think I want to go all that much...”","Jun Linyuan said, “Out!”","–","In the kitchen.","Granny Gong looked at Feng Wu sympathetically, because the task was so difficult.","As time went by, Feng Wu didn’t seem worried at all. Granny Gong, on the other hand, was on edge.","If Feng Wu starved everyone in the residence tonight, she would leave such a bad impression on the others.","“Miss Wu...” Granny Gong tried to make Feng Wu see how serious the situation was. “The servants may be inferior in status, but each of them has their own role, and you’ll probably need their help in the future. But if today...”","While Granny Gong chattered away, Feng Wu was racking her brain.","All the cooks had been ordered to leave the kitchen. Looking around, Feng Wu saw rows upon rows of stoves and pans. There had to be hundreds of them.","Since His Royal Highness had said that no one was to help Feng Wu, no one dared to. She even had to wash and chop the vegetables herself.","Feng Wu knew that she would never be able to fulfill the original requirement, so she had to find another way.","She touched here and there as she walked around, and her eyes lit up when she saw a bag of flour.","“If I make some noodles...”","Granny Gong immediately rejected the idea. “Don’t! His Royal Highness hates noodles and won’t let them touch his lips!”","Feng Wu frowned. “Why is he so difficult?”","Granny Gong smiled wryly.","“He has to eat rice, then?” Feng Wu asked.","Granny Gong nodded. “His Royal Highness will be displeased if there’s no rice, and when that happens, all of us will be in trouble.”","Feng Wu said, “If he has to eat rice... hm... wait a minute!”","Feng Wu’s eyes lit up, as if she had discovered a new world!","Granny Gong looked at Feng Wu in bewilderment and wondered why she was so happy.","Granny Gong asked, “Miss Wu, do you know what to do now?”","Feng Wu nodded happily. “I do. It won’t be a problem! I promise I’ll give you perfect results.”","Granny Gong was about to ask some more, when Feng Wu pushed her toward the door. “Just wait for my good news!”","Once Granny Gong was outside, Feng Wu closed the door behind her.","Granny Gong was dumbfounded.","Feng arrived at that moment and asked Granny Gong for an update. “How’s Miss Wu doing?”","Granny Gong smiled bitterly. “I don’t know how to answer that question.”","Feng asked, “Why?”","Granny Gong said, “Miss Wu said she knew what to do and chased us all out, but she didn’t tell us what she was going to do.”","Would she really know what to do? She was supposed to cook for 3,000 people without any help.","Everyone was convinced that Feng Wu was bragging.","Feng had come here on a mission, so he pushed the door open and walked in. Otherwise, the crown prince would be mad at him.","Feng Wu was busy working when Feng walked in.","Feng Wu turned out to be really good with her knife, and she was chopping vegetables."]},{"number":1434,"title":"Chapter 1434 - Back in Northern Border City...","paragraphs":["“Miss Wu, what are you preparing?” Feng asked.","Feng Wu heard Feng, but she gave him an instruction without looking up. “Mr. Feng, you’re right on time. Quick, boil some water for me.”","Feng was dumbfounded.","Everywhere he went, he was a revered figure. Even those who worked in the imperial palace treated him with respect, and Zuo Qingluan herself had to address him respectfully. But now, Feng Wu had just told him to boil some water.","Seeing that Feng wasn’t moving, Feng Wu urged, “Mr. Feng, hurry up. My hands are full here.”","Feng smiled wryly and found Feng Wu very interesting.","He did as he was told. Sitting down behind the biggest stove, he moved a finger slightly, and a flame jumped out from his fingertip to ignite the firewood.","If anyone else saw Feng, the steward who was superior to even a lord, doing such a petty task, they would probably pass out from astonishment.","Feng chatted with Feng Wu as he worked. “Miss Wu, I heard that you’ve come up with an idea.”","Feng Wu hesitated and said, “I don’t know if it’s an idea, but I do know what dish to cook.”","Dish? Feng was shocked. “You mean, only one dish?”","Feng said matter-of-factly, “That’s right. I’m going to serve some rice with meat and vegetables on top: fish-flavored sliced pork over rice. How does that sound?”","Feng didn’t know what to think, because he didn’t quite understand it.","“Rice served with meat and vegetables?” Feng repeated.","“Yes.” Feng Wu chatted with him as she busied herself with cooking. “Basically, you pour the mixture over the rice.”","“Is that even edible?” Feng was very doubtful.","“Of course it is. Mr. Feng, that sweet and sour taste mixed with a pinch of hot chilli is going to wake your taste buds up!” Feng Wu said happily, because she had high expectations for the dish.","However, Feng rejected the idea immediately. “No, no, no. That dish won’t do.”","Feng Wu was confused. “Why not?”","Feng smiled wryly. “His Royal Highness hates spicy food, and he’ll never touch anything that’s slightly spicy. Miss Wu, you should cook something else, because this dish is never going to work.”","However, Feng Wu remembered something.","That didn’t seem right...","Back when they were in Northern Border City, Jun Linyuan had indeed refused to eat at first, but then... He might have elegant movements, but he ate as much as everyone else.","“Your crown prince doesn’t eat spicy food, you said?” Feng Wu asked.","Feng nodded solemnly. “That’s right. He never touches anything spicy, because it’ll give him an allergic reaction. So, Miss Wu...”","“Teehee.” Feng Wu chuckled. “Mr. Feng, who are you kidding? Your master was so happy with my spicy dishes that he practically licked the plates clean. Allergic to spicy food? You’ll have to try harder if you want me to believe that.”","Feng gave Feng Wu a strange look. “His Royal Highness really ate it?”","Feng Wu said, “That’s right. He didn’t just eat it, he ate a lot of it. He practically gulped up everything that was left on the plates.”","Feng asked, “When did that happen?”","Feng Wu said, “When he was in Northern Border City.”","Feng rubbed his forehead. That was why the crown prince had lost a lot of weight when he came back.","“Is this fish-flavored sliced pork only slightly spicy?” Seeing that Feng Wu wouldn’t change her mind, Feng asked another question."]},{"number":1435,"title":"Chapter 1435 - Your Royal Highness, What Would You Like to Know?","paragraphs":["Feng Wu waved her hands. “It’s mostly sour and sweet, so please don’t worry. Plus, I’ve chopped up all the ingredients already and I don’t want to waste them. Otherwise, I can cook something else.”","“There’s one more thing...” Feng smiled bitterly.","Feng Wu paused. “What is it?”","Feng said, “His Royal Highness doesn’t eat fish. To be more precise, he hates fish.”","Feng Wu was dumbfounded.","Feng smiled wryly. “Therefore, Miss Wu, please cook something else, because this dish really is going to offend His Royal Highness.”","Feng Wu chuckled when she heard that. “You’re mistaken. There’s no fish in this fish-flavored sliced pork.”","Feng was dumbfounded.","Feng Wu said, “There’s a story behind it — quite a long one, actually, but since we don’t have anything better to do at the moment, I’ll tell you about it.”","Hence, Feng Wu told him how fish-flavored sliced pork was created.","Once upon a time, there was a family who loved eating fish, and they were quite particular about the flavors in their fish dishes as well. Hence, they created a special recipe for fish.","One day, the wife chopped too many ingredients. She didn’t want to waste them, so she used them in another stir-fry, but wasn’t sure if it would taste good. She was still worrying about it, when her husband came back.","The husband was amazed by how delicious the dish was, and the recipe became known as “fish-flavored stir-fry.”","“Therefore, there’s no fish in fish-flavored sliced pork.” Feng Wu grinned at Feng.","The main ingredient in fish-flavored sliced pork was lean pork, which was cooked with wood ear and dried slices of tender bamboo shoots, and used condiments like oil, salt, soy sauce, vinegar, and cooking wine, as well as chopped scallion and garlic.","When all was said and done, Feng Wu was a cultivator, and she was great with her knife.","Each piece of pork was chopped into 6cm-long slices of the same thickness. She then seasoned the pork with salt and cooking wine before coating the shreds evenly in starch.","Leaving the pork to sit for a while, Feng Wu shredded the wood ear and bamboo shoots and quick-boiled them in the pot.","Meanwhile, she fetched a big pot and made some fish-flavored sauce with soy sauce, sugar, and other condiments.","When Feng Wu looked up again, she realized that Feng had left.","He needed to report to the crown prince.","He knew his young master too well. Right now, the crown prince had to be waiting anxiously for him to go back, but he wouldn’t let it show. Indeed, Feng walked into the study to find it filled with a cold, murderous energy.","“I thought you would never come back!” The crown prince’s face was livid.","Feng was baffled, because he had only been gone for a little while.","“Speak!” Jun Linyuan wanted to kick Feng.","“Ahem —” Feng coughed into his hand. “Your Royal Highness, what would you like to know?”","Of course Jun Linyuan wanted to know what was going on with Feng Wu, but he was too proud to say so. Instead, he only stared at Feng.","“Ahem —”","The look in Jun Linyuan’s eyes was so fierce that Feng didn’t dare tease him, so he slowly said, “Miss Wu seems to have run into some difficulty.”","“What difficulty?!” Jun Linyuan immediately asked.","Feng looked at Jun Linyuan and said grumpily, “There’s simply too much work. It’s impossible for her to finish. I think Miss Wu is going to faint from exhaustion.”","Jun Linyuan puffed out his cheeks.","After stealing a glance at the crown prince, Feng mumbled, “Well, I think she should be considered to have succeeded as long as everyone is fed tonight.”"]},{"number":1436,"title":"Chapter 1436 - Lovely Spiritual Pets","paragraphs":["Feng was trying to make some excuse for Feng Wu.","But Jun Linyuan frowned. By now, he had also realized how difficult the task was.","He said angrily, “What’s Granny Gong doing? Why didn’t she help her?!”","Feng smiled wryly. “Your Royal Highness, Granny Gong isn’t to be blamed. You gave the order yourself that no one was allowed to help her. We all heard it.”","Jun Linyuan was rendered speechless.","Feng said, “Your Royal Highness, would you like to check on her?”","Jun Linyuan didn’t know what to say.","Feng said, “Or, would you like to withdraw your order?”","Jun Linyuan threw a dirty look at Feng and said proudly, “Withdraw my order? In her dreams!”","A lot of people had gathered around the kitchen and were discussing among themselves.","Feng Wu was bustling around when Granny Gong walked in.","She was so concerned that she had to come in and have a look.","As soon as she entered, she saw that Feng Wu was chatting with Feng as she worked, so Granny Gong asked, “Miss Wu, are you sure you don’t need any help?”","Feng Wu tossed the sliced pork into the oil in the wok on medium heat. As she stir-fried the meat, she said, “Jun Linyuan said no help was allowed. He’ll be angry if he knows you tried to help me.”","Granny Gong sighed in resignation.","“Is that the only dish you’re going to make?” Seeing the red sauce, Granny Gong frowned, because she knew that His Royal Highness didn’t like spicy food.","Feng Wu nodded. “One dish is more than enough.”","It wasn’t just any fish-flavored sliced pork, because Feng Wu had added liquid spiritual essence to it.","The liquid was the product of the formation core in Grand Secretary Fang’s manor.","Feng Wu had set up a special pond there which produced one drop of liquid every day and which could be used to enhance physical strength.","The rapid progress which her family members had been making was also a result of this liquid.","Feng Wu had added one drop before she scooped the fish-flavored sliced pork out of her wok. Nothing changed at first, but as time went by, an aroma filled the air.","“Hey, what’s that smell?” Granny Gong found the aroma very appetizing.","Feng Wu wasn’t going to tell her about the liquid, so she only smiled and said, “I guess this fish-flavored sliced pork just smells so nice.”","The food in the crown prince’s residence was supposed to be specially tailored with spiritual essence. Although she had only made one dish, it contained as much spiritual essence as all the dishes combined, if not more.","Feng Wu was an amazing cook to begin with. With the help of the liquid, when the delicious smell spread out of the kitchen through the closed door —","“Hey, what’s that smell?”","“That’s wonderful...”","“How can it smell so nice? My stomach is growling.”","–","No one in the crown prince’s residence was allowed to help Feng Wu. Luckily, she still had her two spiritual pets, Little Phoenix and the tiger cub.","Feng Wu asked Granny Gong, “What’s the rule here? Do you usually eat in your own quarters or is there a big dining hall?”","Feng Wu noticed that there was a huge empty space right next to the kitchen, and tables and benches had been arranged in neat rows. It looked like a place where people went to eat.","Granny Gong said, “His Royal Highness doesn’t like the residence to smell like food, so almost all the servants eat here.”","“That’ll be much easier, then.”","Feng Wu then gave instructions to the cub and Little Phoenix, telling them to set out the plates."]},{"number":1437,"title":"Chapter 1437 - Amazing! (1)","paragraphs":["The two pets were very efficient for their tiny sizes.","They each held a stack of white plates and set one down at each seat. Feng Wu walked behind them and filled the plate with rice.","There was one standard spoonful of rice on each plate.","And it wasn’t ordinary rice.","Because Feng Wu had run out of time, she had to cook the rice with her own fire attribute, and she had applied quite a few different techniques.","This was the first time Feng Wu had tried to cook with her own fire, so when the rice was out of the pot —","Wow!","Even Feng Wu herself was amazed.","“That smells so nice —” Granny Gong gave Feng Wu a strange look.","She had also tried cooking with the fire attribute before, but everyone knew that because the rice cooked so fast, it was very hard to get much fragrance out of it.","But now...","This rice smelled so nice!","The long tables were lined with big white porcelain plates, and Feng Wu put rice on each of them as she walked down the tables.","After making sure that all the plates had rice on them, she started ladling the fish-flavored sliced pork over the rice.","The rice was plump, white, and chewy, and it already smelled delicious on its own. Now that the fish-flavored sliced pork with the liquid spiritual essence was added...","The fragrance became even more intense.","Strangely, however, after the meat touched the rice, the aroma grew fainter and fainter until it dissipated in the air.","The fish-flavored sliced pork over rice didn’t look any different from any ordinary dish.","Granny Gong was amazed and gave Feng Wu a strange look. “Miss Wu, that’s...”","Feng Wu shrugged. “I don’t know what happened either.”","Right now, a lot of people had gathered around.","Apart from the crown prince, everyone else in the residence ate all three meals here in the big dining hall.","It was dinner time now, and people were queuing outside.","“I heard that Miss Feng Wu was the cook today.”","“That’s right. I didn’t have any hope in her, but it smelled so amazing just now.”","“I’m so curious. I can’t wait to see the food she prepared for us.”","However, when the door opened and the servants filed in, many of them were astonished.","“W- What’s this?”","“If I’m not mistaken, that’s a side dish poured over rice.”","“That’s it?”","“It can’t be. This just has to be the first dish.”","–","They were still talking among themselves when Feng Wu and Granny Gong came out.","The servants immediately rose to their feet.","Granny Gong waved at them and said mildly, “Everyone, take a seat. This is your dinner tonight. Enjoy.”","“Granny Gong, are you serious? This thing is our dinner?”","Someone cried out.","Granny Gong corrected them in a grumpy tone, “This is called fish-flavored sliced pork over rice.”","“Granny Gong, I know we have a different pay grade and a different meal standard, but even so, you can’t just give us a spoonful of rice with this tiny amount of meat. She didn’t even make us any soup!”","“That’s right. Granny Gong, you can’t be serious.”","“Miss Wu, we’re on the night shift; we won’t have the strength to work if you starve us.”","It was obvious that these few people who were speaking out didn’t like Feng Wu."]},{"number":1438,"title":"Chapter 1438 - Amazing! (2)","paragraphs":["It wasn’t easily to tell who was behind them, but it was definitely an organized protest.","Their words were highly disruptive, and the calmer servants grew agitated as well.","“Granny Gong, are we supposed to eat this?”","“Miss Wu, you’re treating us like beggars.”","“If Miss Wu ends up running the residence one day, are we going to be starved all the time?”","–","They believed that the rules wouldn’t apply to them if their number was big enough, so everyone spoke at the same time, though no one dared to step out.","But Feng Wu still heard every single word.","Granny Gong’s face darkened when she saw Feng Wu frown.","However —","Just then, they heard footsteps outside.","The sound was quite special, and couldn’t belong to just any ordinary person, so everyone turned to look.","It was none other than Jun Linyuan himself!","He seemed to start a gust of wind when he walked in.","Dark clouds seemed to gather overhead after he arrived, and the oppressive energy made everyone uneasy.","Immediately, everyone stopped talking. They all lowered their heads and avoided Jun Linyuan’s sharp gaze.","The crown prince looked around the room before his gaze fell on the dinner table.","There —","There was only one plate in front of each seat.","Jun Linyuan frowned and glanced at Granny Gong.","Granny Gong immediately explained, “Your Royal Highness, Miss Wu only had time to make one dish, so she made fish-flavored sliced pork over rice instead.”","She was a little embarrassed.","Dinner was the most important meal for the crown prince, and even the simplest dinner would contain thirty dishes, but now...","There was only one dish poured over rice, and the dish was spicy, which His Royal Highness hated. Granny Gong thought that Jun Linyuan would be furious.","And she wasn’t the only one who expected that.","Because this thing was so offensive!","Not only did she only make one dish, it was also a chilli red color. The crown prince hated spicy food!","Something cold glinted in Zhen Xia’s eyes.","Bixi smiled a little.","Everyone was waiting for Jun Linyuan’s tantrum when —","To their surprise, the crown prince frowned at first and indeed looked like he was going to lose his temper.","Yes, he was about to shout at Feng Wu...","Everyone’s heart rates picked up, but Jun Linyuan turned around and glared at the crowd.","“You should consider yourself lucky to even have food on the table! Who gave you the right to be so picky? Even I haven’t said anything yet!”","Jun Linyuan was furious.","He was angry because these servants didn’t have the right to be picky.","Little Feng Wu made the dish herself, and they should feel grateful to even be able to taste it. Who gave them the right to be so choosy?","“Finish everything on your plate, down to the last grain of rice!” The crown prince glared at the crowd. “Do that, or wait to be punished!”","That serious?!","Everyone exchanged looks, and all of them couldn’t believe their ears.","However, the crown prince wasn’t reasonable when he was angry. He sat down and beckoned Feng Wu over. “Give me a plate!”","Feng Wu was speechless."]},{"number":1439,"title":"Chapter 1439 - Amazing! (3)","paragraphs":["Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","Jun Linyuan acted as though she was some waitress.","However, since he had helped her, Feng Wu decided to let him be. She quickly fetched a plate of fish-flavored sliced pork over rice and set it down in front of Jun Linyuan.","Seeing the food, Jun Linyuan gave Feng Wu a resigned look and smirked. “Feng Wu, you sure know how to choose the easy way out.”","Feng Wu said, “What did I do?”","The crown prince almost rolled his eyes. “Can’t you tell?”","Feng Wu said, “This type of food is very filling; what’s wrong with it? You didn’t say I had to make a certain number of dishes.","“Moreover!” Feng Wu glared at Jun Linyuan. “Do you know how difficult it was to make this fish-flavored sliced pork? I had to create a separate essence-gathering formation just to get the spiritual essence in the food perfect.”","Jun Linyuan pursed his lips. “You’re such a braggart.”","No one else believed her either.","She had set up a formation just to cook a dish?","To be more precise, her cooking needed a formation? That was preposterous!","No one would believe Feng Wu.","Feng Wu didn’t know what to say. “Just try it, and you’ll see.”","The fish-flavored sliced pork and rice combined so that their fragrances covered each other, which was why the dish didn’t have much of a smell.","But in fact, it really was very tasty.","However, since Jun Linyuan wouldn’t touch it, the others didn’t dare to eat either.","Feng Wu thus sat down next to Jun Linyuan and looked at him with her big bright eyes.","“Your Royal Highness, just try it —”","Jun Linyuan almost rolled his eyes.","It was a spicy dish!","He could tell from the smell!","Everyone around him knew that he didn’t touch anything spicy, so if he ate it now, he would be so humiliated!","Hence, Jun Linyuan threw down the chopsticks he had just picked up.","Feng Wu stared at Jun Linyuan in bewilderment. What did he do that for?","“Jun Linyuan —”","“What the hell is this? Is it human food?!” Jun Linyuan glared at Feng Wu.","Feng Wu was speechless.","She wanted to lose it, but she knew better than to yell at Jun Linyuan. She couldn’t afford to be mad at him...","The man was all about saving face. If she got mad at him in front of all these people, the consequences would be unimaginable.","This man wouldn’t be forced!","Hence, Feng Wu tugged at Jun Linyuan’s sleeve and spoke in a low voice that only he could hear. “Jun Linyuan, Your Royal Highness, please try it. I almost cut my finger off when I made the dish. Please try it —”","She sounded so pitiful...","It had to be said that Feng Wu finally understood Jun Linyuan a little better.","The crown prince enjoyed it a lot when she held his arm and pleaded with him.","“Ahem —”","Jun Linyuan looked up and threw a dirty look at Feng Wu. “Behave yourself. Everyone’s watching.”","He brushed Feng Wu’s arm off as he spoke.","Feng Wu was speechless.","What a...","The others all gave Feng Wu strange looks, especially Zhen Xia, whose smirk had grown even more wider.","“That Feng Wu is throwing herself into the crown prince’s arms. Does she have no shame at all?”"]},{"number":1440,"title":"Chapter 1440","paragraphs":["Zhen Xia clearly wasn’t the only one who thought that way. A lot of people agreed with her.","They all thought that the crown prince would keep telling Feng Wu off before he walked away...","To their surprise, Jun Linyuan only casually chided her, then —","He picked up the chopsticks and glared at Feng Wu. “Don’t you have any spoons?”","Feng Wu’s eyes snapped open!","“Yes, of course I do. Here’s a spoon.” Feng Wu immediately brought him a porcelain spoon.","She had prepared special tableware for Jun Linyuan, but he was sitting in the dining hall and there wasn’t enough room to spread out the entire set of tableware.","Immediately, everyone stared at Jun Linyuan in disbelief.","Oh god, His Royal Highness was eating it!","He really was!","“I thought His Royal Highness didn’t eat spicy food?”","“And I thought he couldn’t even stand the smell of it.”","“Isn’t His Royal Highness very picky about his food?”","“Isn’t he...”","None of them could believe that the respectable Jun Linyuan would eat such simple food, not to mention that it was a spicy dish, his least favorite taste.","To their surprise, Jun Linyuan ate it...","He frowned when he took the first bite, and looked like he was going to flare up the next moment.","Everyone held their breaths, fearing that he might direct his anger at them.","However —","They waited and waited, but nothing happened.","The crown prince then ate another spoonful.","And the crowd was speechless.","Everyone’s eyes widened!","How was that even possible?!","They were already very surprised when the crown prince didn’t lose his temper, but he had taken another bite! Exactly how considerate was he?","They thought that Jun Linyuan would stop after two bites and put down the spoon. However —","The crown prince wouldn’t stop eating!","Everyone was speechless.","They were so shocked that they didn’t know how to express their feelings.","“His Royal Highness is still eating, so maybe it’s actually quite nice.”","“What are you thinking? It’s just some rice with a little bit of meat and vegetables. How can it be tasty? I’ll chop my own head off if that thing tastes good.”","“You have a point. Miss Feng had to cook for 3,000 people, so taste would be her last concern. It’s already very amazing that she could cook a meal at all.”","“Since His Royal Highness is eating it, let’s show Miss Feng some respect as well.”","They had to admit that His Royal Highness was being very nice to Feng Wu. Despite the big frown on his face, he was still trying to support her.","Zhen Xia and the others exchanged looks, and all of them frowned.","How could His Royal Highness stand such food? That was so infuriating!","Many servants felt just as indignant.","Chang San used to have three deputies, and after he left, one of them known as Hou Si was promoted.","Like Feng Xun, Hou Si was quite a lively man. A plate of food was right in front of him at the moment, so he rolled up his sleeves and chuckled. “Since His Royal Highness has started, I’m going to have my dinner as well. Let me try Miss Wu’s great cooking.”","Hou Si believed that he had to take his young master’s side.","If His Royal Highness was on Miss Feng Wu’s side, he should be as well.","No matter how horrible the food tasted, he had to say that it was delicious."]},{"number":1441,"title":"Chapter 1441","paragraphs":["Hence, Hou Si picked up a spoonful of food, closed his eyes and stuffed it into his mouth.","As soon as the food entered his mouth...","Dense spiritual essence filled his mouth, waking up all his taste buds!","Holy shit!","Hou Si was astonished!","How could anything be so delicious?!","When he swallowed the food, the satisfying sensation was indescribable.","After standing there in astonishment for three seconds, Hou Si finally returned to his senses. He opened his eyes and gave Jun Linyuan an accusing look.","The crown prince was such a good actor!","Hou Si had thought that the crown prince was forcing himself to eat because he was trying to help Feng Wu save some dignity, but the truth was —","It was so delicious!","After tasting the dish, Hou Si resumed eating and wolfed down the food on the plate.","It wasn’t just because it was delicious!","Hou Si had the distinct feeling that this food was going to benefit his cultivation greatly!","The others were amazed by the way Hou Si ate.","There was a reason it was Hou Si who took over Chang San’s position. The man was such a great actor!","Two brothers known as Luo Bai and Luo Hei looked at each other in bewilderment. They were both Hou Si’s subordinates.","“Captain, isn’t that a bit over the top? Is that thing really so tasty?” Luo Bai, the livelier one, asked.","Luo Hei also stared at Hou Si.","Hou Si immediately shook his head. “No, it’s not tasty at all.”","The others saw the light.","They were right.","Hou Si glanced at Luo Bai before shifting his gaze to the plate in Luo Bai’s hands. “It’s not worth eating. I’m sure you don’t want it.”","Surprised, Luo Bai nodded in bewilderment.","The next second, Hou Si snatched the plate out of his hands.","What?","Before everyone else realized what was happening, Hou Si had eaten Luo Bai’s portion.","He then reached out to Luo Hei, asking, “You don’t want this, right? Don’t let it go to waste...”","Luo Hei wasn’t stupid; he found it very strange that Hou Si wouldn’t stop eating when he said the food wasn’t good at tall.","Hence, Luo Hei scooped up some and put it into his mouth.","Hou Si’s face immediately darkened.","The next second —","Luo Hei’s face darkened as well!","Without another word, he raised the plate and poured everything into his mouth.","Thump —","Hou Si was exasperated. “Since when are you so fast?!”","Hou Si was the captain of the guards, and Luo Bai and Luo Hei were his capable assistants. Naturally, the others paid a lot of attention to them.","They saw how vexed Hou Si was.","Because of that, they looked at one another in bewilderment. Then...","Hou Si, Luo Bai, and Luo Hei involuntarily looked around at the other servants, and the look in their eyes gave them the creeps!","Just then —","Rumble —","A fluctuation of spiritual essence spread out from Hou Si...","Even Hou Si himself was astonished!","He had made a breakthrough!","Everyone gave him strange looks.","Hou Si was quite capable already, and it was very difficult for someone at his level to make a breakthrough.","He had been stuck in this bottleneck for a very long time...","He had thought that it would be years before he made another breakthrough.","Therefore, this one was such a big surprise!"]},{"number":1442,"title":"Chapter 1442","paragraphs":["“I made a breakthrough?” Hou Si mumbled and looked completely baffled.","“I really have?","“How?","“Am I dreaming?”","Not only couldn’t Hou Si understand it, neither could the others!","“What did Hou Si do? Why did he suddenly make a breakthrough?”","“That’s right. I’ve never seen anymore make a breakthrough during a meal.”","“Captain Hou, how did that happen?” Luo Bai was baffled.","Just then, Luo Hei realized what happened. Without another word, he turned around and stared at the person behind him. “You don’t want this, do you?”","Hou Si revealed the secret, ruining Luo Hei’s plan. “There’s pure spiritual essence in this dish, which will benefit your cultivation greatly...”","He didn’t need to say more. Everyone had seen Captain Hou make a breakthrough because of the dish!","At that thought, they all grew excited!","The next second, almost everyone started wolfing down the food.","The taste wasn’t the most important thing anymore. There was spiritual essence in it, and that was all they cared about!","The spiritual essence exploded on their tongues when the food was in their mouths, and finally, those who didn’t believe in Feng Wu were convinced.","Captain Hou was right!","Rumble —","Either Feng Wu’s liquid spiritual essence was very potent, or a lot of people were in the bottleneck stage. With some buzzing sounds, five people made breakthroughs in a row!","Everyone was speechless.","One person could be considered a coincidence, but there were at least five cases now. Coincidence couldn’t explain them all!","“Oh god —”","“That’s amazing —”","“Is it really because of the food?”","“The food... the food... Miss Feng Wu made the dish with her own hands...”","Immediately, all eyes were on Feng Wu!","Feng Wu was shocked as well.","She knew she was an excellent cook and was aware of the liquid spiritual essence she put in the food, but she didn’t expect it to be so potent!","Five people had made breakthroughs, which sounded just a little too scary.","“Miss Feng!” Luo Bai was the first to react, and he had never felt so regretful in his life.","“Miss Feng! Do you still have some food left?” Luo Bai was so frustrated, because his captain had eaten his own!","Otherwise, he might have made a breakthrough as well!","Feng Wu said, “Well... that...”","His gaze was so intense that Feng Wu felt a little abashed. She could only give him a wry smile and said, “I only made one portion for each person, and there’s nothing left. Sorry about that —”","Luo Hei rushed over and knocked Luo Bai out of the way. He stood in front of Feng Wu and asked excitedly, “Miss Feng Wu, what about the wok you used?”","The wok? Feng Wu was confused. Did they want to wash it for her?","She turned around and pointed at the giant iron wok on the stove.","It was big enough to cook food for 3,000 people.","Feng Wu pointed at the giant wok.","The next second!","Two shadows flitted across the courtyard, and before she realized it, Luo Bai and Luo Hei had dashed off!","“My wok!”","“No, it’s my wok!”"]},{"number":1443,"title":"Chapter 1443","paragraphs":["“Luo Hei! You’ve eaten your portion already! Why are you trying to take this from me?!”","“Luo Bai! You were dumb enough to let the captain fool you, I had nothing to do with that!”","“I don’t care. I’m your older brother! You have to respect me!”","“I’m the younger brother, so you should indulge me!”","Luo Bai and Luo Hei were two brothers whom Jun Linyuan had picked up from the side of the road. They were at the most noisy age.","To Feng Wu’s surprise, the twins ended up burying their heads in the wok and started licking the sauce inside.","The look on Feng Wu’s face...","She looked like she had seen a ghost!","However, Feng Wu was the only one who looked so astonished, because the rest of the members of the residence all eyed the twins with envy.","Even Hou Si swallowed and took a few steps forward. However, his dignity as captain prevailed, and he stopped moving closer.","Before long, the twins had licked the wok so clean that it seemed like it had been washed, the inside bright enough to reflect light.","Feng Wu’s eyes widened.","She couldn’t understand this world anymore.","Meanwhile, Zhen Xia frowned and said in a low voice, “Even if the food was full of spiritual essence, should they lower themselves like that? The Luo Brothers are going too far.”","Those around her shook their heads as well. “That’s right. That’s so humiliating! He may not even make a breakthrough!”","Rumble —","To everyone’s surprise, Luo Bai, who had been licking the wok like a dog, made a breakthrough the next second!","Feng Wu was speechless.","Zhen Xia didn’t know what to say.","Nor did everyone else.","Luo Bai was so excited that he was almost in tears. “I — I... Oh god! Oh my god!”","He had made a breakthrough!","He couldn’t believe it!","Luo Bai was so excited that he was almost in tears.","Everyone was astonished.","Their gazes shifted from Luo Bai to Feng Wu, and they all looked at her in disbelief.","Even Zhen Xia, who wouldn’t believe it at first, had to admit that Feng Wu’s food could indeed help with cultivation.","Even Jun Linyuan was giving Feng Wu a strange look.","It was a mix of pride and resignation...","He then rose to his feet and walked away.","A hush fell over the room.","He halted after a few steps and looked at Feng Wu over his shoulder.","Although he didn’t say anything, his sharp gaze was more than enough to deliver the message.","What choice did Feng Wu have? She could only follow him out.","Jun Linyuan went straight to his bedchamber.","Feng Wu stood outside and hesitated.","Wasn’t it a bit inappropriate for her to go in?","She was still hesitating, when some pretty teenage girls walked toward her in two rows. They moved elegantly, and their curves were so soft that they seemed boneless.","Each of them held a red tray in their hands, and some had lukewarm water on it.","Feng Wu moved aside to let them pass.","The girls gave Feng Wu warm and friendly smiles when they spotted her.","Feng Wu rubbed her chin. Because of her beauty, very few girls had been friendly to her when she was growing up."]},{"number":1444,"title":"Chapter 1444","paragraphs":["Through the open door, Feng Wu saw the girls put down their things in the room before they quietly came back out.","They smiled at Feng Wu again on their way out, and they were very sweet smiles.","However, it gave Feng Wu the creeps. What was going on?","“Come in.”","She heard Jun Linyuan’s cold voice.","Feng Wu’s stomach lurched. Something felt off, but it was impossible to resist Jun Linyuan’s pressure.","However, she put up one last struggle.","Jun Linyuan snorted in the room. “I thought you agreed to work as my humble servant. Are you going to go back on your word?”","Feng Wu was speechless.","What other choice did she have? She could only inch toward Jun Linyuan, moving as slowly as she could manage.","The crown prince looked at the way she lowered her head and was very amused.","Did she think the work would disappear if she stalled for time? The longer she put it off, the worse it would be.","“Come over here.” Jun Linyuan patted the stool by his bed and gestured at Feng Wu to come closer.","Feng Wu pouted and stared at him.","Jun Linyuan ignored her and lay down on the bed, resting his head on his hands.","Looking from the basins of hot water to Jun Linyuan’s casual demeanor, Feng Wu was dumbfounded. “This is...”","The crown prince glanced at Feng Wu and asked, “What do you think?”","Feng Wu said, “Please don’t tell me that I have to wash your hair for you.”","The crown prince nodded.","Feng Wu said, “Jun Linyuan, are you a three-year-old? Can’t you wash your hair on your own? Why do you need other people to wash it for you?”","Jun Linyuan’s face darkened.","Feng Wu said, “Plus, so many pretty young maids were here just then, why didn’t you ask them? Why me? No, I’m not doing it!”","The crown prince gave her a half-smile and asked, “Are you disobeying my order now?”","Feng Wu said, “Hmph! Yes, I am! So what?!”","Jun Linyuan gave her a cold glance. “Leave, then.”","Outside, Feng was speechless.","Your Royal Highness, you have to talk nicely to girls. Can’t you be a little softer? You’ll never win Miss Feng Wu’s heart like this!","Feng Wu was baffled.","She had expected Jun Linyuan to be mad, but never thought that he would kick her out.","Feng Wu was speechless.","She stood there and didn’t know what to do.","She couldn’t leave, because the 6th trial had been extended to 18 days, and it was only 99.99% complete at the moment. If she walked away now, she would fail!","Therefore, she couldn’t leave!","Gritting her teeth, Feng Wu stomped her foot and wanted to smack her own head.","Why did she have to be so stubborn? She had to live with the consequences now.","What choice did she have? For her broken star pieces, she had to stay.","In the end, Feng Wu had to rub her forehead to get rid of the frown, and she inched back toward Jun Linyuan.","Sitting down on the stool, she was about to untie Jun Linyuan’s hair, when he sat up.","Feng Wu was confused. “What are you doing?”","The crown prince gave her an arrogant glance and said indifferently, “I don’t deserve your service. You can go now!”","Jun Linyuan then pointed at the door, telling Feng Wu to get out.","Feng Wu was speechless.","“If you don’t want to serve me, just leave!” the crown prince said proudly.","Feng Wu was speechless.","She wanted to go. She wished she could leave now and never come back!"]},{"number":1445,"title":"Chapter 1445","paragraphs":["Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","The last thing she wanted was to become his little maid!","But she didn’t have a choice!","She had to wake her beautiful master up, and that task was more important than her life.","Therefore, Feng Wu took a deep breath to calm down.","She had tried the gentle approach, but Jun Linyuan was still so arrogant, so she had to change her method.","Putting on a serious look, Feng Wu glared at Jun Linyuan and pushed him back down. “Hey! That’s enough! Sit yourself down!”","Jun Linyuan glared at Feng Wu and wondered why she dared to yell at him.","However, before he could react, Feng Wu had forced him to sit down.","And the crown prince let her.","The way Feng Wu washed his hair was quite rough, because she needed to get it done as soon as possible.","However...","“Feng Wu! Be gentle!","“Feng Wu! Do you even know how to serve others?","“Feng Wu, you...”","–","The crown prince who was known for being reticent and aloof was yelling like an angry young lion now.","Outside, Feng and Granny Gong exchanged looks and shook their heads.","Miss Wu was amazing. The crown prince only behaved like a normal teenager around her.","Inside, Feng Wu finally finished washing Jun Linyuan’s long black hair.","Jun Linyuan had ordered her around the entire time.","He was as difficult as always. He had no fewer rules for washing his hair than when he took a bath.","At his request, Feng Wu rinsed his hair as many as nine times, and she was exhausted.","Luckily, it was finally over.","Feng Wu fetched a thick towel, wrapped it around Jun Linyuan’s black hair, and heaved a sigh.","Serving Jun Linyuan was so draining. She would rather go through hell nine times than follow his orders.","Hearing the sounds inside, someone outside soon opened the door.","The maids from earlier filed in again, and within minutes, they tidied everything up and left the room when Feng Wu was still feeling baffled.","Feng Wu was about to go out, when she heard Jun Linyuan snort. “Where are you going?”","She looked back at Jun Linyuan in bewilderment. “I thought we’re done here.”","Jun Linyuan smirked. “Leave, then.”","Feng Wu was speechless.","She knew it couldn’t be that easy.","Jun Linyuan had asked her to wash his hair repeatedly and to give him a head massage. It had taken Feng Wu over an hour to do everything.","“What do you want now?” Feng Wu sounded very impatient.","The crown prince was very sensitive, and he immediately detected her impatience.","He snorted and looked away.","His attitude was very obvious.","Feng Wu was speechless.","“Jun Linyuan, are you asking me to dry your hair now?” Feng Wu asked grumpily.","Jun Linyuan rolled his eyes and gave Feng Wu an accusing look.","Feng Wu rubbed her own forehead.","She was so baffled. “Your Royal Highness! You’re a very capable cultivator with the fire attribute. Activate your spiritual essence and your hair will dry instantly!”","Why did he have to dry his hair with a towel? That was so..."]},{"number":1446,"title":"Chapter 1446","paragraphs":["The crown prince immediately flushed.","He glared at Feng Wu and said, “So, you’re going to leave before your work is done?!”","Feng Wu felt so helpless.","“You can solve that problem by simply moving a finger, so why do you have to order me around? Do I look like an easy target?”","Jun Linyuan glared at Feng Wu. “Go, then! Now!”","Feng Wu was speechless.","She wanted to smack her own head again.","She had only just warned herself not to get mad at Jun Linyuan, but she had forgotten again! She still had the 6th trial!","Feng Wu took a deep breath and forced herself to calm down.","She raised both hands over her head.","“Fine, fine. Drying your hair, is it? No problem.” She knew that if they continued quarreling, she would have to charm Jun Linyuan again later. So, why bother?","Seeing that Feng Wu didn’t even want to quarrel with him, Jun Linyuan felt even more frustrated.","But he also knew that he had pushed Feng Wu to the brink of losing her temper.","Feng Wu walked up to him and ripped off the thick towel wrapped around his head. She was quite rough about it.","Jun Linyuan frowned involuntarily.","The room felt a little stuffy.","After that, Feng Wu’s hands started to emit warm energy, and it was getting stronger.","She was going to dry Jun Linyuan’s hair with her fire energy.","That way, she could do it in less than a minute.","But just then —","She heard Jun Linyuan’s cold voice.","“Is that how you’re going to deal with my hair?”","Feng Wu stopped rubbing and looked at Jun Linyuan in bewilderment. “What are you talking about? This is the quickest way!”","However, once his hair was dry, he would run out of excuses to keep her here...","He looked at Feng Wu and said, “It’ll damage my hair!”","Feng Wu almost choked on her own breath.","Damage his hair?","“I didn’t know a man like you would care about the quality of your health. Jun Linyuan, you’re so full of surprises!” Feng Wu chuckled.","The crown prince looked abashed, and he glared at Feng Wu. “Leave, then!”","“Please don’t say that ”","Feng Wu waved her hands. “I’m not going anywhere until my work is done here. I have to make sure that you’re all comfortable.”","After that, she fetched a thick towel to rub Jun Linyuan’s hair.","“Did I force you to stay?” the crown prince asked grumpily.","Feng Wu said, “No, of course you didn’t. How is that possible? I love this job.”","The crown prince snorted.","However, Jun Linyuan had a lot of requests even when his hair was being dried. There was a different towel for each round...","Feng Wu had to go back and forth and do as she was told.","Luckily, she was getting better at controlling her anger, and she was able to get through this by reciting the vajracchedika sutra in her head.","However...","The scripture made her feel more and more sleepy. In the end, she could barely keep her eyes open.","“Hey —” Thinking that Feng Wu was being lazy, Jun Linyuan poked her little head.","However, Feng Wu slid down and fell toward Jun Linyuan.","When he realized what had happened, Feng Wu was already snoring a little.","“She’s asleep?” The crown prince was amazed.","What he didn’t know was —"]},{"number":1447,"title":"Chapter 1447 - What Did You Do to Me?","paragraphs":["Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","Feng Wu had been working for him since that morning and was exhausted. It was only natural that she felt sleepy.","“You’re such a careless girl, falling asleep like this.” Jun Linyuan wanted to jab a finger into Feng Wu’s head, but when his hand touched her, it caressed her softly.","Jun Linyuan already had well-defined features, and the dim moonlight coming in from the window only accentuated them.","Raising his straight black eyebrows, Jun Linyuan stared at Feng Wu with his glittering eyes, completely absorbed.","Despite his usual domineering and majestic self, he was looking at her with such gentle eyes that he seemed to be as calm as the wind and the moon.","Feng Wu liked to move around in her sleep. She rolled toward Jun Linyuan.","With a thump, Feng Wu was in Jun Linyuan’s arms.","The crown prince’s eyes widened and he stiffened when he felt Feng Wu in his arms...","Talk about walking into one’s own trap. He had an example right in front of him.","Hmph!","Jun Linyuan thought, “You may deny your feelings all the time, but your body is very honest.”","No one could stay calm when they had a soft body in their arms, not to mention that she was the girl he liked.","Seeing the girl’s stunning face, the crown prince lowered his head toward her.","Jun Linyuan’s mouth touched Feng Wu’s soft lips, and he was so happy when —","Ding —","Feng Wu’s clear, black eyes snapped open.","They were still so close, and their lips were touching. When their eyes met, they were both shocked.","Caught red-handed, the crown prince was astonished, and his head went blank.","The next second!","He involuntarily pushed Feng Wu away.","Crash —","Poor Feng Wu. Before she knew what was going on, she was spinning in the air, and then fell to the floor.","The crown prince blushed in embarrassment when he heard the crisp sound.","Feng Wu had been sleeping, but the fall woke her up.","She landed on her butt. Although there was no real damage, it still hurt a lot, and tears welled up in her eyes.","Feng Wu stared at Jun Linyuan in vexation and bewilderment. “What are you doing?!”","The crown prince was speechless.","Pursing his lips, he tightened his jaw and looked at Feng Wu rather guiltily.","Rubbing her back, Feng Wu slowly got to her feet and looked down at Jun Linyuan, who was sitting in bed. She then accused him, “Jun Linyuan, you kissed me without my permission, and you kicked me!”","The second accusation didn’t bother him, but he would never admit to the first.","If he admitted it, he would be admitting that he was secretly in love with Feng Wu. That would never happen!","The crown prince fought back. Glancing at Feng Wu, he crossed his arms and said slowly, “Feng Wu, don’t pretend to be innocent. Don’t you know what you did?”","Feng Wu’s stomach lurched.","“W- What did I do?!”","The crown prince snorted. “Don’t you remember?”","Baffled, Feng Wu scratched her head and started thinking.","She remembered how Jun Linyuan had been ordering her around, telling her to wash his hair and towel-dry it. She became sleepy as she rubbed... And she didn’t remember anything after that."]},{"number":1448,"title":"Chapter 1448","paragraphs":["Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","“Just tell me! What on earth did I do?!” Feng Wu was a little flustered, because she couldn’t recall anything.","Jun Linyuan gave Feng Wu an arrogant glance.","Seeing how righteous he looked, Feng Wu felt even more guilty. “Hey! Just tell me!”","Jun Linyuan grunted. “So, you’re going to deny it after everything you did.”","What?!","Feng Wu’s eyes widened. “After what I did? What on earth did I do?”","“Heh.” The crown prince snorted. “You’re supposed to work as my maid, but you’ve been drooling all over me!”","Talk about throwing the blame on other people. The crown prince was trying very hard to prove that he wasn’t in love with Feng Wu.","Feng Wu was furious, and she glared at Jun Linyuan. “Impossible! I would never drool over you! Even if I did, it would be over...” My beautiful master!","The crown prince didn’t notice the last bit of her claim and went on grumbling, “That’s not even the worst bit. You then caught me off-guard, climbed into my bed, and wouldn’t let go of me. And... and you know the rest!”","That was a very serious accusation!","Feng Wu could stand the previous one, but this second part set her off.","Her face went scarlet red, and she could barely form a coherent sentence. “I... I... I climbed into your bed?! Impossible!”","The crown prince casually glanced at her. “If you hadn’t, why did you fall off?”","Feng Wu said, “Well... Anyway, the climbing into bed part never happened!”","The crown prince said, “It did!”","Feng Wu said, “No, I didn’t do that!”","The crown prince said, “Yes, you did.”","Feng Wu said, “No, no, no!”","Jun Linyuan snorted and glanced at Feng Wu. He then said sarcastically, “Little Feng Wu, what did you do today? Why are you so desperate tonight?”","Feng Wu clenched her fists in frustration.","She couldn’t help but recall what happened earlier today.","Today was the Immortal Flower Festival, and a lot of very suggestive things happened in the grove.","Jun Linyuan glanced at Feng Wu, crossed his hands behind his back, and asked in a solemn tone, “Aren’t you too young to think about such things? You shouldn’t surrender to your desires.”","Feng Wu: !!!","She now knew what it meant to “give a dog a bad name and hang him.” She almost had a stroke!","She could neither retort nor fight him, and the frustration made her tremble from head to toe.","Seeing how defeated Feng Wu was, the crown prince was over the moon.","That’s what you get for laughing at me earlier today! It’s never too late to take revenge.","As smart as Feng Wu was, Jun Linyuan was the only one who could irritate her like this.","Frustrated, she clenched her fists and ran out the door.","“Hey! Feng Wu! Stop!”","Realizing that he had stepped out of line, he called after her.","But Feng Wu ignored him.","The door was yanked open and then slammed shut.","Running out after Feng Wu, Jun Linyuan almost smashed his nose into the door.","“Ahem —”","Feng and Granny Gong had been standing outside the door the entire time, so they heard everything.","The crown prince looked embarrassed when he saw them at first, but the proud teenager immediately glared at them!"]},{"number":1449,"title":"Chapter 1449 - Doesn’t She Know Shame?!","paragraphs":["Granny Gong was too timid to speak.","But not Feng. He could speak freely even in front of Emperor Wu.","“Ahem, Your Royal Highness —”","Feng said patiently, “When a girl is mad, the sooner you try to appease her, the easier it will be. It’ll be very difficult to make her happy if you leave it for too long...”","Jun Linyuan had wanted to find Feng Wu, but he realized what he was doing when he heard Feng.","“Me, appease her? Feng, you must be out of your mind!”","He then shut the door from inside.","Feng was speechless.","Granny Gong heaved a sigh. “I’ll go talk nicely to Miss Wu.”","Her young master had made the mess, but she had to clean up after him.","Feng nodded in resignation.","Feng Wu dashed off in frustration. She ran all the way out of the crown prince’s residence and back to the Feng manor.","She bumped into a person outside Fallen Star Yard.","“Watch where you’re going!” the person cried out. After recognizing Feng Wu, she immediately shut up.","It was none other than Feng Liu herself, and Dugu Mengxi was with her.","Although she had lost her baby, she and Lady Wang had somehow managed to make Dugu Mengxi care even more for Feng Liu, and they were preparing for an engagement reception.","Feng Liu was furious when she saw Feng Wu.","Dugu Mengxi didn’t like Feng Wu either, both from what happened before and because of the humiliation which Dugu Yamo had gone through today.","Feng Wu ignored them and walked straight in.","“Feng Wu! Stop right there!” As the favorite son of the Dugu family, Dugu Mengxi had never been ignored like this.","Feng Wu had a fierce energy about her when she was in a bad mood, so she turned around and stared at Dugu Mengxi with her cold gaze.","Dugu Mengxi was a spoiled young heir, and that murderous look was more than he could take. His stomach lurched, and he felt a chill run down his spine.","“Feng Wu! How dare you! Are you trying to hurt Young Master Dugu?!”","Feng Liu had dealt with Feng Wu quite a few times, so she wasn’t as intimidated.","Feng Wu’s gaze swept over them before she turned around to go inside.","Just then, the door to Fallen Star Yard opened, and Granny Zhao appeared in the doorway.","Seeing that the door was open, Feng Liu knew that her voice could easily be heard inside, so she snorted and said, “Feng Wu, after what you’ve done, how dare you come back?! Do you know how much shame you’ve brought to our clan?!”","Granny Zhao was about to chase Feng Liu away, but she frowned when she heard those words.","Uncle Qiu, Qiuling, and Chaoge were all there, and the beautiful lady was doing some needlework in the yard as well. It had been so peaceful and quiet in Fallen Star Yard before Feng Liu disrupted the atmosphere.","Feng Liu stared at Feng Wu and smirked. “What? After doing such a humiliating thing, are you going to leave just like that?”","There were a lot of people in Fallen Star Yard, and everyone went out and glared at Feng Liu.","The short-tempered Chaoge rushed over to Feng Liu and picked her up by the collar. “What was that? Do you want to get your ass kicked?!”","Feng Liu smirked. “Get my ass kicked? Hahaha, why don’t you ask Feng Wu what she did? Does she have no shame at all?!”"]},{"number":1450,"title":"Chapter 1450","paragraphs":["Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","Chaoge raised a fist, but Feng Wu shook her head.","“What did I do? What do you mean?” Feng Wu decided to stop ignoring Feng Liu. She walked up to her and gestured at Chaoge to put her down.","Once released, Feng Liu started mocking Feng Wu again. “What did you do? Hah! Feng Wu, the entire capital city has heard of it! Stop pretending!”","Feng Wu said calmly, “Speak or go away.”","Seeing her elaborate speech received with nonchalance, Feng Liu was furious.","She smirked. “You can quit pretending already! You’re just a despicable maid now! How dare you act pretentiously in front of me!”","A despicable maid? Granny Zhao and the others were all surprised. What was that supposed to mean?","Feng Liu snorted. “You don’t know? Feng Wu has been turned into His Royal Highness’s personal maid! Personal... heh...”","Chaoge paled and grabbed Feng Wu by the arm. “Xiao Wu, is that true?”","Feng Wu was already mad because of what Jun Linyuan had done, and hearing Feng Liu’s slander, she almost had flames coming out of her eyes.","She stared at Feng Liu with a cold look in her eyes and didn’t say a word.","Thinking that Feng Wu was intimidated, Feng Liu rejoiced, and her tone was even more sarcastic. “Of course it’s true. So many people in the immortal flower grove heard it! The crown prince only said it in passing, but Feng Wu couldn’t wait to say yes. Do you know what people outside are saying now?","“When I went to the Dugu family today,” Feng Liu spoke in a serious tone, “they asked me about it, and wondered why a daughter of the Feng clan would want to become a bed-warming maid. Do you know how embarrassed I was when Aunt Dugu asked me that? I was so humiliated!","“Feng Wu! Can you think about other people when you do something like this in the future? Fine, we all know you’re in love with His Royal Highness and can’t wait to get into his bed, but please don’t just think about yourself the next time you’re infatuated. I’m your cousin, and your humiliation becomes mine! If your reputation is ruined, so is mine! I can’t believe this! If the Dugu family calls off the engagement, it’ll be all your fault!”","Feng Liu had so many grudges against Feng Wu. Now that she finally had a chance, she would make sure to let it all out.","Since she was deliberately trying to make a scene, instead of trying to control the damage, she yelled very loudly.","Soon, more people had gathered around.","Not only the members of Fallen Star Yard, even Feng Yanfeng and Lady Wang showed up.","Feng Liu was even more pleased when she saw the crowd.","She stared at Feng Wu and said sarcastically, “Feng Wu, you’re a shame to our clan! If you still have the least bit of shame, you should cut ties with the Feng clan!”","“What’s wrong?” Feng Yanfeng frowned.","“Father!” Feng Liu walked up to her parents as soon as she saw them and told them all about Feng Wu’s job as Jun Linyuan’s personal maid. She also stressed that Feng Wu was there to warm his bed.","“Warm his bed?!” Lady Wang looked astonished, and she stared at Feng Liu in disbelief. “You can’t make up stories like that!”","“I’m not! All the people in the immortal flower grove heard it! I’m not making up any stories! Feng Wu, tell us. Did you or did you not agree to become the crown prince’s personal maid?”"]},{"number":1451,"title":"Chapter 1451 - Is It True?","paragraphs":["Instantly, all eyes were on Feng Wu.","As Feng Liu’s mother, Lady Wang certainly knew what Feng Liu meant.","Feng Liu had suffered so much defeat at Feng Wu’s hands. Now that she finally had the upper hand, Lady Wang had to back her up.","Hence, Lady Wang faked an astonished face and smacked Feng Liu on the head. “Watch your language! That’s your sister!”","Feng Liu smirked. “If she really thinks of herself as my sister, she should leave this clan! Otherwise, she’ll only bring us shame!”","Lady Wang gritted her teeth and cast a stern look at Feng Liu. “How can you say such things about Feng Wu? Your sister isn’t like that!”","As she spoke, she smiled at Feng Wu. “Xiao Wu, do tell us. Xiao Liu wasn’t telling the truth, was she? Surely you wouldn’t bring such shame to our family like that.”","What a question... One could tell how much she hated Feng Wu.","Feng Wu didn’t know how to describe her feelings right now.","Had it not been for the mission, she would never have become Jun Linyuan’s maid.","Despite her frustration, she kept her face unperturbed. She then glanced at Lady Wang and said indifferently, “Jun Linyuan’s maid? That’s me.”","WHAT?!","Lady Wang stared at Feng Wu with unblinking eyes. “What did you say? You’re really warming his bed now?!”","Feng Wu smirked. “My lady, what’s that look on your face? Do you think Feng Liu can get this job even if she wants it?”","Wow —","Lady Wang sucked in her breath.","“You...” Lady Wang didn’t expect to hear such a bold claim.","“Aren’t you ashamed?!” Lady Wang went scarlet red in the face.","Feng Wu smirked. “Ashamed? Other people can’t get this opportunity even if they beg for it. Shouldn’t I be honored? What’s shameful about it?”","“You...” Lady Wang was so furious that she pointed a shaking finger at Feng Wu.","Feng Liu stared at Feng Wu in astonishment as well.","She had tried to attack Feng Wu with that piece of news, but Feng Wu didn’t care at all. Not only that, she was actually proud of it.","Feng Liu didn’t know what to say...","She felt as if she had thrown a punch with all her strength, only for her fist to hit cotton.","The beautiful lady took Feng Wu’s hand and looked very concerned. It broke one’s heart to see her like that.","“You! You’re shameless!” Lady Wang pointed at Feng Wu’s nose.","However, Feng Yanfeng smacked her hand away.","“Ahem —”","Crossing his hands behind his back, Feng Yanfeng looked at Feng Wu with an expressionless face. He suddenly cleared his throat and gestured at Feng Wu to walk to the side with him.","He stared at Feng Wu once they were alone.","Feng Wu frowned. “Uncle, if there’s nothing else, I’m going back inside.”","“Stop.” Feng Yanfeng stopped her.","Feng Wu looked over her shoulder.","Feng Yanfeng probably felt that it was an embarrassing question for him to ask as well, but he couldn’t resist the possible gains. In the end, he cleared his throat and asked, “Is Feng Liu telling the truth?”","Feng Wu looked at him in bewilderment.","It only made Feng Yanfeng even more embarrassed, but he still snorted and asked, “Is it true, the thing between you and His Royal Highness?”","Feng Wu said casually, “If by the thing, you mean me becoming his personal maid —”"]},{"number":1452,"title":"Chapter 1452","paragraphs":["Feng Yanfeng looked Feng Wu up and down, and had to admit in the end that Feng Wu was a lot prettier than Feng Liu. No wonder even His Royal Highness was...","“Ahem...” Feng Yanfeng cleared his throat. “Actually, it’s not a bad thing.”","Feng Wu only gave him an indifferent glance, because she already knew what her uncle was getting at.","Indeed, the next thing Feng Yanfeng said was, “Since His Royal Highness is into you now, you should take the chance to make him care for you!”","Feng Wu looked at him with expressionless eyes.","Feng Yanfeng thought that Feng Wu was going to listen to him, so he said patiently, “You have to know how prestigious His Royal Highness is! He’s the crown prince! You know how many girls are around him all the time!","“Yes, that’s right. You’re pretty, and His Royal Highness likes you, but can you be sure that His Royal Highness will always like you?”","Feng Wu frowned when she heard that.","Feng Yanfeng couldn’t sense her annoyance at all and went on trying to persuade her. “Xiao Wu, you have to listen to me. This is a chance you can’t miss. Feng Wu —”","Feng Wu stared at Feng Yanfeng.","Feng Yanfeng looked around, leaned closer to Feng Wu, and whispered, “Xiao Wu, while you still have the chance, you have to...”","Feng Wu frowned, “What did you say?”","Feng Yanfeng said, “You have to get pregnant with the crown prince’s baby!”","Feng Wu looked at Feng Yanfeng and found him a complete idiot. How could this man be a senior member of her own family?","Feng Yanfeng stared at Feng Wu and stressed each word. “The crown prince doesn’t have any children now. If you give him a son, do you know what will happen?","“He’ll dote on you, and you’ll become the royal family’s favorite! The Feng clan will rise because of you!","“Little Feng Wu, the entire Feng clan is counting on you!","“Even if you don’t want it yourself, you have to do it for the clan! Do you understand?!”","In the end, Feng Yanfeng was so excited that he was shaking Feng Wu by her shoulders.","Feng Wu gave him a “you idiot” look.","Seeing how unperturbed Feng Wu was, Feng Yanfeng gradually became disappointed.","After a final glance at Feng Yanfeng, Feng Wu turned to leave.","Feng Yanfeng’s face darkened. “Feng Wu!”","Feng Wu didn’t even look back. She only said, “Moron!”","Moron?!","Feng Yanfeng was astonished.","He was the minister of the Ministry of Official Personnel, the head of the Feng clan, and Feng Wu’s uncle. But she had just called him a moron!","“Hey, you stupid...”","But before he could go on, Feng Wu turned her head and sneered at him. “Uncle, are you urging me to...”","“Ahem —”","Feng Yanfeng coughed loudly to stop Feng Wu from telling other people.","After all, as her uncle, he would be ridiculed if other people learned that he had urged his niece to sleep with a man, even if that man was Jun Linyuan...","Although Feng Wu didn’t finish the sentence, they all knew what she meant.","Fearing that Feng Wu might expose her father, Feng Liu immediately tried to change the subject. “Feng Wu, how can you be so proud when you haven’t even been on a winter hunt yet?!”","Feng Wu rolled her eyes at Feng Liu.","Feng Liu smirked. “You don’t know what that is, do you?”"]},{"number":1453,"title":"Chapter 1453","paragraphs":["Feng Wu decided to let the idiot go on.","Feng Liu gloated. “Hah, of course you don’t know what it is, because you’re not qualified to go! You can’t even be there! That’s so funny!”","Chaoge was so mad that she wanted to hit Feng Liu.","After her initial rage, Feng Wu had calmed down by now. She stopped Chaoge and let Feng Liu continue her performance.","“Are you done?” Feng Wu looked at her.","“Feng Wu, you don’t know what to say now, do you? Hahaha —” Feng Liu laughed in satisfaction.","Feng Wu then slammed the door shut.","Feng Liu and the others were shut out.","“Hey! Feng Wu! Open the door! How dare you shut me out?!” Feng Liu kicked the door in frustration.","However, the door wouldn’t budge no matter how hard she kicked.","Suddenly, a hush fell over the crowd...","Feng Liu turned around and almost jumped in fright, because an old woman was standing behind the crowd.","And that old woman was staring at her with a very grim look in her eyes.","“G- Granny Gong...” Feng Liu felt a chill run up her legs.","Granny Gong was only a chief maid when she was in the crown prince’s residence, but when she came outside...","All the noble ladies of the empire had to address her politely and show her no less respect than they showed Lady Northern Feng.","Therefore, when Granny Gong stood outside Fallen Star Yard with a grim face, Lady Wang tugged at Feng Liu’s sleeve to shut her up.","“Hm...”","Feng Liu swallowed. “Granny Gong...”","Granny Gong slowly walked up to Feng Liu, and suddenly smiled at her.","Feng Liu was elated.","Had she left a good impression on Granny Gong?","Oh god, if she could earn Granny Gong’s favor, her life would be so much easier!","Feng Liu was thrilled, but —","There was a crisp sound, and Feng Liu was slapped in the face by none other than Granny Gong herself.","“Granny Gong, you...”","Feng Liu was astonished and felt wronged.","The smile had vanished from Granny Gong’s face, and her eyes were colder than ice.","She stared at Feng Liu with her sharp gaze.","“Do you want to go on the winter hunt very much?”","Feng Liu said, “Granny Gong, actually...”","“You don’t have to bother preparing for it now!” Granny Gong said haughtily.","Feng Liu stared at Granny Gong in surprise.","Lady Wang realized what had happened, so she ran up to Granny Gong and tried to explain. “Granny Gong, Liu didn’t mean that. Actually...”","“No one in the Feng clan except for Feng Wu is allowed to go hunting this time!”","After that announcement, Granny Gong gave them an arrogant glance and said, “Now, get out of here.”","Feng Liu still tried to explain, but Lady Wang tugged at her to stop her.","After politely bidding Granny Gong farewell, Lady Wang took Feng Liu away.","Feng Liu wouldn’t accept it.","“Mother, what are you worried about? She’s just a nanny, and the chief maid of the crown prince’s residence at most. Why does she think she can control our clan...”","Smack!","Lady Wang slapped Feng Liu before she could finish.","“Shut up now, or you’ll incriminate the entire Feng clan!” Lady Wang had never been so mad at Feng Liu before."]},{"number":1454,"title":"Chapter 1454","paragraphs":["Feng Yanfeng had seen Granny Gong, but he thought he was too important to beg her, so he only gave her a nod and was ready to leave.","But Granny Gong stopped him in a cold voice.","“Master Feng —” Her voice wasn’t loud, but there was something very majestic in it.","She was only an elderly maid in the crown prince’s residence and was far more inferior to Feng Yanfeng, the minister of the Ministry of Official Personnel.","But somehow, Feng Yanfeng felt intimidated by her.","Granny Gong stared at Feng Yanfeng with her sharp gaze. “Master Feng, you’re short-sighted!”","Feng Yanfeng was utterly baffled and looked at Granny Gong in confusion.","Granny Gong snorted.","To her, Feng Yanfeng was an idiot.","If he had a little more faith in Feng Wu, he would be able to see the crown prince’s feelings for her and wouldn’t think Feng Wu was a mere bed-warming maid.","Feng Yanfeng was about to ask, when Granny Gong cut him off in her indifferent voice.","“Master Feng, think it over. If you’re perceptive enough, you may be able to grab this great opportunity.” That was all the hint Granny Gong would give him.","“Great opportunity?” Feng Yanfeng was dumbfounded.","“Yes, a chance to make the Feng clan rise again.” Granny Gong stared at the front gate of Fallen Star Yard.","“To make the Feng clan rise again?!” Feng Yanfeng was thrilled. “Can the Feng clan become one of the nine major clans again?”","Granny Gong glanced at Feng Yanfeng. “The nine major clans? You can rise higher than that.”","Feng Yanfeng was elated.","He wanted to ask more questions, but Granny Gong was done reminding him. “Master Feng, think it through.”","After that, Granny Gong walked past Feng Yanfeng and went into Fallen Star Yard.","She thought that Feng Yanfeng should understand, because she had made it so obvious.","However, Feng Yanfeng was still dumbfounded after Granny Gong went inside.","A great opportunity to make the Feng clan great again? What could it be?","Could it be Feng Wu? But even if Feng Wu actually climbed into Jun Linyuan’s bed and gave him a child, it wouldn’t be enough to make the Feng clan rise.","Could it be —","Feng Yanfeng’s eyes lit up.","Could it be that Feng Wu’s child would inherit Jun Linyuan’s great talent, and the Feng clan would rise because of that genius baby?","Yes, that had to be it.","Feng Yanfeng successfully persuaded himself and got very excited. He couldn’t wait to see Feng Wu pregnant and give birth.","“Father, you’ve seen it. Feng Wu was so mean to me.” Feng Liu took Feng Yanfeng’s hand and complained.","Feng Yanfeng had recognized Feng Wu’s importance now, so he would never let Feng Liu hurt her.","“Keep this in mind: No more conflict with Feng Wu!” Feng Yanfeng glared at Feng Liu. “Any conflicts in the future, and you’ll be held responsible!”","“Father —” Feng Liu was dumbfounded.","She couldn’t understand the sudden change in her father’s attitude. What on earth happened? Feng Liu couldn’t figure it out, but Feng Yanfeng wouldn’t tell her either.","Granny Gong walked into Fallen Star Yard and asked Feng Wu directly, “Miss Wu, do you need me to take care of Miss Feng Liu and the others for you?”","Take care of? How? Feng Wu stared at Granny Gong in amazement.","Granny Gong smiled at Feng Wu and said matter-of-factly, “If Miss Wu wants, I can make her disappear.”","Feng Wu waved her hands. “It’s not that serious.”"]},{"number":1455,"title":"Chapter 1455","paragraphs":["Granny Gong said, “Then I’ll make sure she can’t participate in the winter hunt. If we don’t teach her a lesson, His Royal Highness will punish me when he hears about it.”","Feng Wu’s eyebrows knitted tightly when Jun Linyuan’s name was mentioned, and she immediately cut Granny Gong off. “Please don’t bring up that name anymore!”","Despite Feng Liu’s insult and Feng Yanfeng’s reprimand, Feng Wu hadn’t really been affected. However –","As soon as Granny Gong mentioned Jun Linyuan, Feng Wu flared up.","Granny Gong wanted to say something, but hesitated. Her poor young master just didn’t know how to express his feelings...","“Miss Wu, His Royal Highness is just a little childish sometimes. In fact, he’s very nice to you...”","Very nice? Feng Wu couldn’t believe her ears.","If Jun Linyuan was nice to her, then no one in this world could be considered mean!","Granny Gong could guess from Feng Wu’s silence what she was thinking, so she cleared her throat and said, “Ahem, actually, you’re very special to His Royal Highness...”","Feng Wu glanced at Granny Gong in resignation. “Very special indeed, but I’d rather not be.”","Granny Gong said, “Miss Wu, actually...”","The crown prince really liked little Feng Wu, but he was just too proud, which was why he always behaved like a bully.","She told Feng Wu that.","Feng Wu rolled her eyes. “Granny Gong, do you believe that?”","Granny Gong was speechless.","She knew that so much misunderstanding had accumulated by now that no explanation would be enough, so she decided to leave it to her young master to solve the problem.","She heaved a sigh and said, “Miss Wu, I think you should say goodbye to your family for the evening.”","Feng Wu kept her cold gaze on Granny Gong without saying a word.","Despite her reluctance, Granny Gong still looked at Feng Wu and said solemnly, “Miss Wu, I think it’s time you said goodbye.”","She made it very clear that Feng Wu had to go back with her tonight.","Feng Wu pointed a trembling finger at Granny Gong and remained silent.","Chaoge ran up to Feng Wu, put herself between the two people, and glared at Granny Gong. “You evil old woman! If you’re trying to take Xiao Wu away, you’ll have to kill me first!”","The others gathered around them as well.","Qiuling pleaded with her eyes.","The beautiful lady was in tears.","Granny Gong was speechless.","She was only taking Feng Wu to the crown prince’s residence. Why did they look like she was going to decapitate Feng Wu?","Granny Gong ignored them all. She only stared at Feng Wu and said a name.","Feng Xiaoqi.","Feng Wu frowned. “Granny Gong, are you threatening me now?”","Granny Gong raised an eyebrow. “Miss Wu, I think you know the answer. His Royal Highness is the only one who can do that.”","Jun Linyuan...","Feng Wu frowned. She had to admit that Jun Linyuan could actually do that.","“Where’s Xiaoqi?” Feng Wu asked Chaoge.","Chaoge had been about to tell Feng Wu about it and she immediately said, “He left with some men who were supposed to be from the imperial guards. Xiao Wu, let’s go get Xiaoqi now!”","So, it was indeed the imperial guards...","Feng Wu stared at Granny Gong with a dangerous look in her eyes.","Granny Gong remained unperturbed and spoke to Feng Wu in a low voice that only she could hear.","The look on Feng Wu’s face changed immediately.","She stared at Granny Gong. “Are you threatening me now?”"]},{"number":1456,"title":"Chapter 1456","paragraphs":["Granny Gong said, “You think too highly of me.”","Feng Wu snorted, walked out the door, and headed for the Fang manor next door.","Grand Secretary Fang was a highly capable man and Xiaoqi’s teacher. Why would he let the imperial guards take Xiaoqi away?","However, when she got there, Steward Fang told her that Grand Secretary Fang was out visiting a friend.","“Out visiting a friend? What a coincidence.” Feng Wu frowned.","Steward Fang bowed. “Yes, the old master received an invitation from Old Master Zeng and immediately set out.”","“Did he say when he’ll be back?” Feng Wu narrowed her eyes.","Steward Fang shook his head with a wry smile.","Feng Wu went back to Fallen Star Yard and only asked Granny Gong in an indifferent voice, “Does Jun Linyuan know Old Master Zeng?”","Granny Gong replied in an unperturbed tone, “The old master taught His Royal Highness scriptures for a year before. He retired and went back to his hometown after His Royal Highness mastered everything.”","So, Old Master Zeng’s invitation must’ve been designed by Jun Linyuan to lure Grand Secretary Fang away!","“Damn you, Jun Linyuan!”","What lengths would he go to, just to keep her around him?","Feng Wu was speechless.","Granny Gong looked at Feng Wu. “Miss Wu, stalling may not do Young Master Qi any good.”","Of course Feng Wu knew that, but she still couldn’t get over the fact that she was being threatened.","“Xiao Wu, did the crown prince really hit you?” the beautiful lady asked between broken sobs.","Feng Wu’s eyes widened. “Did Jun Linyuan hit me?”","Where did that rumor come from?!","The beautiful lady caressed Feng Wu’s face with her soft hands and said nervously, “Good. There’s no scar...”","Feng Wu was speechless.","She took her mother’s hand and frowned. “Mom, who told you that?”","Since the beautiful lady remained at Fallen Star Yard all the time, rumors outside shouldn’t be able to reach her, not to mention that it was utter nonsense.","Qiuling immediately complained, “It’s all because of Miss Liu. When Young Master Qi was taken away, she came here and spouted all sorts of rumors. We chased her off, but my lady obviously heard her.”","“That’s right. They took Xiaoqi away. Xiao Wu, your brother was kidnapped —” The beautiful lady sobbed and looked so perplexed. “Where did your brother go?”","Feng Wu gave her mother a sympathetic look.","She had no idea what the beautiful lady had gone through, but she had always lived in a confused state like this. To her, the world revolved around Feng Wu and Xiaoqi. Now that Xiaoqi was missing, she was bound to feel anxious.","“Mom, don’t worry. I’ll bring Xiaoqi back.” Feng Wu sighed inwardly.","Granny Gong was right. It would be very unwise of her to argue with Jun Linyuan right now.","Since she couldn’t do that, she had to change her approach. She didn’t like the idea, but what choice did she have?","“Let’s go.” Feng Wu glanced at Granny Gong and walked out of the courtyard.","Granny Gong heaved a sigh.","She was genuinely worried that the young couple would fall out again. By now, because of Bixi, the empress dowager had noticed Feng Wu again.","Granny Gong felt a headache coming on when she thought about that old lady.","Feng Wu and Granny Gong left the Feng manor and went back to the crown prince’s residence.","However —"]},{"number":1457,"title":"Chapter 1457","paragraphs":["Chapter 1457: Untitled","Soon, news leaked out of the Feng clan.","It was said that Feng Wu ran back home after Jun Linyuan hit her, but Granny Gong came after her and took her back to the residence.","Jun Linyuan was such a high-profile name.","And Feng Wu drew a lot of attention.","Everyone was so curious about their story that in less than two hours, the news spread to every corner of the imperial capital.","Even the empress dowager heard it.","“What? Junjun beat Feng Wu up?”","The empress dowager didn’t like Feng Wu in the first place. After what she heard from Bixi, she disliked Feng Wu even more.","Therefore, she was secretly delighted when she heard the news.","“If that’s the case, let her stay in the crown prince’s residence to recover from her injuries. Eliminate her name from the list of participants for the winter hunt!” The empress dowager didn’t want to see Feng Wu’s face.","Lady Northern Feng was about to speak, but the old lady cast a stern look at her. “Don’t say a word! Don’t mention her name again in front of me. Otherwise, I won’t like you anymore!”","Lady Northern Feng was rendered speechless.","What could she do about the willful old lady?","All news got around eventually, not to mention a decree from the empress dowager herself.","Therefore, before Feng Wu and Granny Gong got back to the crown prince’s residence, the news of Feng Wu being scolded by the empress dowager and her name being removed from the list had already gotten around.","It spread so fast that someone had to be behind it.","And the two of them came back too late to hear the news until the following day —","The winter hunt was a big deal for the royal family, but with so many servants around, things were quickly prepared and packed.","Early next morning —","Feng Wu had yet to wake up when she felt something cold on the tip of her nose.","She opened her eyes to find the domineering crown prince sitting by her bed.","Feng Wu smacked his hand away and glared at him. “Jun Linyuan, what are you doing?!”","“Hmph!”","The proud crown prince felt rather humiliated by her reaction.","After what Feng said the night before, Jun Linyuan seemed to realize that what he had done to Feng Wu was wrong. Right now, he was here to mend things.","But Feng Wu’s rejection immediately set him off.","Feng Wu had no idea that she had offended Jun Linyuan, and she glared at him. “Even a crown prince shouldn’t just walk into a girl’s room! I have my own dignity!”","Jun Linyuan smirked and said the first thing that came into his mind. “Heh. You’re a bed-warming maid. What dignity do you have?”","Feng Wu almost exploded when she heard that.","Her eyes went bloodshot red, and she yelled, “Jun Linyuan! What did you say?!”","Outside, Feng really wanted to smack the crown prince on the head.","He didn’t know what else he could do.","The crown prince was an incredibly smart man, and other people would willingly follow his lead. But when Feng Wu was involved, he simply stopped thinking. What was wrong with him?!","Seeing that the young couple was going to start a row again, Feng immediately intervened. “Your Royal Highness, you still need to sign a lot of memorials to the throne.”","Hearing that, Jun Linyuan threw an angry glance at Feng Wu. “You’re impossible! Reflect on yourself!”","He stormed off after that."]},{"number":1458,"title":"Chapter 1458 - Untitled","paragraphs":["Seeing Jun Linyuan leave, Feng Wu was so frustrated, but she didn’t know where to vent.","She realized that she was such a wuss around Jun Linyuan.","Feng tried to explain to Feng Wu, “Actually, His Royal Highness was here to...”","“To piss me off, is it?” Feng Wu stared at Feng.","Feng was speechless.","“What are you still doing there?!” Jun Linyuan yelled outside.","Feng was speechless.","With their temperaments, he wondered when the two of them would reconcile. Feng himself almost felt like crying.","With no other choice, he could only give Feng Wu a long look. “Miss Feng, please get up. We’re leaving for the winter hunt in an hour.”","After Feng left, the more Feng Wu thought about it, the more displeased she became.","The winter hunt was the last thing she wanted to do right now.","However, Jun Linyuan still had Xiaoqi, and she had agreed to be his maid for 18 days, so she had to go.","Suppressing her frustration, Feng Wu struggled to her feet.","Being as pretty as she was, she didn’t need to do much. After quickly washing up and getting dressed, she pushed the door open.","“So, Miss Feng is awake.”","Feng Wu pushed the door open to see a pretty girl leaning against the wall and looking at her in a triumphant way.","This was... Feng Wu frowned.","Because she recognized the person. It was none other than Bixi, the girl who had confronted her before.","Feng Wu wasn’t in the mood to talk, so she gave her a nod and was going to walk past her.","However —","“Little maid, where are you going?” Bixi uncrossed her arms and said to Feng Wu with a smile.","Her tone was quite provoking.","Moreover —","Who was she to call her a maid? Who did she think she was? Feng Wu was already grumpy from having to get up, and with the row with Jun Linyuan, she was very angry when Bixi just showed up like this. So, she wasn’t going to play nice.","“To the winter hunt.” Feng Wu stared at Bixi.","“The winter hunt? Hahaha! Are you saying you’re going?” Bixi gave her an “you’re insane” look.","Feng Wu ignored her and continued walking.","“You haven’t heard?” Bixi shouted behind Feng Wu.","She didn’t try to keep her voice down, so she had already caused a scene. Slowly, people began to gather.","Zhen Xia and a few young maids were standing a short distance away.","Zhen Xia was on Zuo Qingluan’s payroll, so she was naturally hostile toward Feng Wu.","She was thrilled to see Bixi criticizing Feng Wu.","Seeing that Feng Wu was leaving, Bixi said in a sarcastic voice, “Don’t you know? You’re not qualified to go to this year’s winter hunt.”","What? Feng Wu frowned and stared at Bixi.","Bixi looked like she had just seen an idiot. “You seem surprised. But didn’t you know? Only four maids can go, and you’re new here. Why would you think you get to go?”","Feng Wu was a little baffled.","Crossing her hands behind her back, Bixi raised her chin and gloated. “Moreover, the empress dowager gave a decree. You, Feng Wu, have been disqualified from going.”","Disqualified? Feng Wu frowned. “Are you sure?”","Seeing the way Feng Wu frowned, Bixi thought that Feng Wu was unhappy, which pleased her immensely. “It’s an order from the empress dowager, so of course it’s true. Feng Wu, don’t tell me you just presumed you could go. How do you feel now? I bet you’re so mad! Hahaha —”"]},{"number":1459,"title":"Chapter 1459 - Royal Progress (1)","paragraphs":["Feng Wu was speechless.","She had never wanted to go to the event in the first place. Hearing this good news, she felt like throwing a party to celebrate.","“Are you sure I’m not qualified to go?” Feng Wu looked at Bixi with her brooding eyes.","Bixi snorted. “Feng Wu, I see that you really want to go hunting. Too bad, you’re not allowed to. Hahaha —”","The idea of Feng Wu not being able to go made Bixi feel utterly satisfied.","But Feng Wu —","As soon as she heard that she wasn’t qualified, she was over the moon!","Without another word, she turned around and headed back.","She moved so fast that the others didn’t have time to react.","When Bixi realized what had happened, Feng Wu was already several hundred meters away.","Dumbfounded, Bixi watched as Feng Wu walked away. She then turned to Zhen Xia with a confused look on her face.","“S- She left, just like that?” Bixi stared at Zhen Xia and mumbled.","Zhen Xia was too smart to get involved in the conflict between Bixi and Feng Wu, so she gave Bixi a little bow and left with her young maids.","Bixi was speechless.","By then, the crown prince had already gotten into his carriage. However, he was so angry at the moment that no one dared to get any closer.","Even Feng couldn’t start a normal conversation with him.","“Why aren’t we moving?” the crown prince asked impatiently.","“That girl is so grumpy. I can’t even make fun of her now.” The more he thought about it, the angrier he became.","“Your Royal Highness, some people are still not here yet, especially Feng...”","However, the crown prince cut him off with a wave of his hand. “If they’re not here yet, they’re not going!”","He was so angry that he didn’t understand what Feng was saying.","Feng was speechless, for he knew that his young master didn’t hear him clearly, so he raised his voice and said, “Your Royal Highness, Miss Feng Wu hasn’t arrived yet...”","Something clicked in Jun Linyuan’s head.","No one could disturb him like that — not even the emperor or the empress dowager. However, whenever Feng Wu’s name popped up, it meant something special.","However —","He still cared about his pride more.","“How dare she not show up? Good. That’s interesting! So interesting!” Jun Linyuan smirked. “Let her stay behind, then! Let’s go!”","After that, Jun Linyuan gave a wave, and they were on their way.","Bixi was one of the maids who was allowed to tag along.","She wasn’t on the list at first, but since she worked for the empress dowager, all it took was a word from the old lady, and she was given permission.","She was a little fidgety after confronting Feng Wu today, fearing that the crown prince would punish her later.","However —","Bixi was thrilled when she heard what Jun Linyuan said.","“Feng Wu, there I was, thinking you mean something to His Royal Highness. But as it turns out, you’re nothing special!”","Bixi wasn’t worried anymore.","The winter hunt always took place in the Selna Grassland.","That grassland was where the Selna Tribe lived. They were one of the fiercer tribes in the empire, and known as “the tribe on horseback.”","The tribesmen were known for their towering heights and sturdiness. They were born with great strength and were innately amazing soldiers."]},{"number":1460,"title":"Chapter 1460 - Royal Progress (2)","paragraphs":["Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","Therefore, even Emperor Wu, the ruler of the continent, had to be on friendly terms with the tribe.","The winter hunt was when Emperor Wu paid a friendly visit to the chief of the tribe, and more went on behind the scenes than any ordinary person could comprehend.","That was why Emperor Wu would have a large entourage every single time.","At Dingwu Gate.","Emperor Wu brought more than 20 officials with him this time, all of whom were his closest confidants.","And they all came with their own families as well, who had carriage after carriage of luggage. Right now, the square outside Dingwu Gate was packed.","Luckily, the families all had their allotted spots, so it wasn’t very messy.","There was a hubbub of voices as soon as Emperor Wu showed up.","“Your Majesty —”","Emperor Wu’s steward smiled wryly and spoke in a low voice when the emperor was about to give the order to set out.","“His Royal Highness isn’t here yet...”","“What?!”","Emperor Wu’s face immediately darkened.","For this trip, he had not only brought Empress Dugu, but quite a few concubines as well. However, Empress Dugu was the only one sharing a carriage with the emperor.","Hearing the steward’s words, Empress Dugu thought that her chance had arrived, so she slowly said, “His Royal Highness is really arrogant. Your Majesty has to wait for him now.”","Emperor Wu was already unhappy, and Empress Dugu’s deliberate words only aggravated the situation. He was visibly in a bad mood.","The chief steward smiled bitterly inwardly. “Her Majesty is still so selfish. She’s all about making her own son the crown prince instead.” However —","The chief steward was completely on Jun Linyuan’s side, even if the young man had never been particularly nice to him.","“Jun Linyuan is getting bolder and bolder!” Emperor Wu smacked the table.","“Your Majesty, we calculated the best time to set out. If we’re delayed because of His Royal Highness, it won’t be a good sign... What are we going to do?” Empress Dugu feigned a worried tone.","Emperor Wu snorted. “If he doesn’t want to come, then don’t! Tell everyone we’re leaving now!”","Emperor Wu had two stewards with him. The chief steward, Zhao Ruhai, was 100% Jun Linyuan’s supporter.","The other steward was Bai the eunuch, who had served Emperor Wu when the latter had still been the crown prince. After all these years, they had quite a close relationship.","However, Bai was on Empress Dugu’s side, so he didn’t like Jun Linyuan.","The chief steward and Bai left the imperial carriage, and Bai looked pleased.","He glanced at the chief steward and smirked. “How can His Royal Highness make His Majesty wait? That’s too arrogant.”","The chief steward almost rolled his eyes. “I’m sure His Royal Highness has his own reasons.”","Bai asked, “Does he? I wonder who is important enough to make His Majesty wait.”","His voice might be low, but Emperor Wu heard everything.","“That’s unacceptable!”","Emperor Wu was very serious about his dignity, and he wouldn’t be challenged. Now that Bai had said that, his impression of Jun Linyuan immediately worsened.","What was Jun Linyuan doing now?","Halfway to the square, the crown prince couldn’t stand it anymore.","He had been thinking about Feng Wu the entire time."]},{"number":1461,"title":"Chapter 1461 - Royal Progress (3)","paragraphs":["Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","In the end, Jun Linyuan felt a throbbing pain in his head.","What was the point of going if little Feng Wu didn’t go?","Jun Linyuan suddenly realized a frightening fact.","Before he knew it, Feng Wu had become so important to him.","Without Feng Wu, everything was so dull.","He sat there dazed for a very long time when he realized that shocking fact. When he returned to himself —","“Feng!” He told the carriage to stop.","Phew —","Feng sighed in relief.","He knew it. The two of them couldn’t stay mad at each other for long, but he had thought that Feng Wu would be the first to give in. As it turned out —","The first to surrender was obviously the one who was more in love.","“I left something behind at the house. Go fetch it for me,” Jun Linyuan told Feng.","Feng cleared his throat.","Left something behind? My dear crown prince, don’t you have a storage ring, where you store all the important files?","That excuse was simply too lame and stupid!","However, Feng wasn’t going to expose his young master, so he put on his most innocent smile and asked, “Your Royal Highness, what did you leave behind?”","Jun Linyuan asked, “You don’t know?”","Feng played dumb. “I don’t. Your Royal Highness, please enlighten me.”","Jun Linyuan’s carriage was in the center and drew the most attention.","Therefore, when they saw Jun Linyuan in the carriage staring at Feng outside in vexation —","They all knew that something was going on.","“Turn back!”","Jun Linyuan threw a dirty look at Feng and told everyone to turn around.","Since he was the crown prince, he was traveling with the whole shebang. It was practically an army.","Everyone was dumbfounded.","“Go back?”","Everyone looked at one another in bewilderment, because they didn’t know why they had to turn around.","Hadn’t Feng said it earlier? Their delay would slow down the entire team.","What on earth happened? They exchanged confused looks.","Jun Linyuan didn’t let anyone question him. Looking at his dark face, no one dared to ask.","“Your Royal Highness, time is running out. If we go back now, His Majesty may...” Granny Gong tried to warn Jun Linyuan, but —","He wouldn’t be Jun Linyuan if he listened.","He only threw Granny Gong a resentful and displeased look.","Resentful and displeased? Granny Gong felt perplexed.","She could understand if His Royal Highness was unhappy, but why the resentment?","Feng nudged her with his elbow and mouthed Feng Wu’s name.","Granny Gong was usually a smart person, but that didn’t mean that was always the case. Like right now, she didn’t know how Feng Wu had anything to do with this.","“Miss Wu still isn’t here.”","Seeing that Jun Linyuan was getting more and more furious, and that the air felt like it was going to freeze, Feng lowered his voice and enlightened Granny Gong when Jun Linyuan wasn’t looking.","Granny Gong’s eyes widened. “Miss Wu isn’t here? Why? She’s on the entourage list!”"]},{"number":1462,"title":"Chapter 1462 - Why Is His Royal Highness Late? (1)","paragraphs":["Feng said grumpily, “Feng Wu really isn’t here!”","Everyone immediately started talking and arguing.","“So, His Royal Highness really wants to go back because Feng Wu isn’t here?”","“So, His Royal Highness really cares about Feng Wu, doesn’t he?”","“So, His Royal Highness...”","–","Granny Gong was dumbfounded.","“Miss Wu isn’t in the entourage? How can that be? Miss Wu should be here...” Granny Gong searched everywhere, but when she couldn’t find Feng Wu, she panicked.","She had come up with the name list for the crown prince’s residence, so she knew better than anyone else where Feng Wu should be.","“Her Majesty the empress dowager specifically gave the order that Feng Wu’s name shouldn’t be on the list,” someone said in a low voice.","The empress dowager’s order?","Immediately, all eyes were on Bixi.","Bixi was from the palace, and she had been out last night.","“I...” Knowing that she couldn’t pretend that she was innocent, Bixi stepped out and spoke in a low voice. “Her Majesty did summon me last night... and she asked me about Feng Wu... But I’m not to be blamed. Her Majesty doesn’t like Feng Wu to begin with.”","Granny Gong’s face darkened.","So, it was indeed because of Bixi!","“Are you an idiot?!” Infuriated, Granny Gong smacked Bixi on the forehead!","Bixi was dumbfounded.","Even those around her stared at Granny Gong in disbelief.","Bixi had been sent here by the empress dowager, who had explicitly told everyone that Bixi was going to be the crown prince’s concubine.","But now, Granny Gong had just hit her in front of so many people!","Bixi was dumbfounded and stared at Granny Gong in disbelief. “You hit me? You’re just an old maid! How dare you hit me?!”","Granny Gong took a deep breath. It was really tiresome to deal with such a stupid woman.","Bixi had no idea what Granny Gong was thinking and went on yelling at her. “You hit me because of Feng Wu?! She’s a nobody! How dare you hit me because of her!","“That’s right! Feng Wu wanted to come this morning, but I stopped her! I laughed at her and told her she wasn’t qualified! So what? What can you possibly do to me?!” Bixi raised her chin and looked very smug.","She believed that she was going to be an imperial concubine one day!","However, before she could go on, a fair, slender and strong hand wrapped itself around her thin, porcelain neck.","Oh, no...","Bixi felt suffocated and couldn’t breathe. She was then lifted up until her feet left the ground.","“Your Royal Highness —”","Feng had looked away for a moment, and the next thing he knew, Jun Linyuan had picked Bixi up by the neck.","“Your Royal Highness, don’t —”","Granny Gong said hastily.","Bixi had such a special status that she couldn’t be handled roughly. Otherwise, Granny Gong wouldn’t have put up with her for so long.","However —","Crack —","They heard the crisp sound of bones breaking.","Everyone’s eyes widened.","They watched as Jun Linyuan snapped Bixi’s thin, white neck.","Just like that, the pretty girl was dead."]},{"number":1463,"title":"Chapter 1463 - Why Is His Royal Highness Late? (2)","paragraphs":["All around them —","There was only silence.","No one dared to breathe loudly or make a sound...","That was so terrifying...","Chills ran up their legs and spines, and they felt cold to the bone.","They had always known that the crown prince was a heartless man who could kill easily. But recently —","It had been a while since the servants at the residence saw the crown prince lose his temper. They even thought that they were beginning to see something human in him. So...","Many people involuntarily thought that the crown prince had become more approachable. As it turned out, he was still that heartless crown prince.","“Your Royal Highness —”","Immediately, everyone dropped to their knees, lowered their heads, and didn’t dare to meet Jun Linyuan’s eyes.","The crown prince looked around with his cold, murderous eyes.","His eyes seemed to see through everything.","The crowd shook from head to toe. They didn’t dare meet his gaze and had to control their breathing so that they wouldn’t make a sound.","“Let’s go!”","Jun Linyuan snorted, tossed Bixi aside, and marched off.","The others felt chilled to the bone...","The crown prince’s residence.","Feng Wu had slept in that morning and was enjoying the moment.","She was having a sweet dream, when she felt a cold, intense gaze on her. The person never looked away.","Feng Wu was so sensitive that she couldn’t ignore such an intense gaze.","Involuntarily, she opened her eyes.","“Jun Linyuan?!” Feng Wu rubbed her sleepy eyes and yawned.","Jun Linyuan gave her a half-smile.","Crossing his arms, Jun Linyuan strolled over to the bed and stopped in front of Feng Wu.","“You’re awake?” The crown prince pinched Feng Wu’s plump cheeks with his slender fingers.","“Hm —”","Jun Linyuan’s fingers were as cold as ever, and his touch immediately woke Feng Wu up. She shuddered and smacked his hands away.","“Didn’t you go to the winter hunt? Why are you back?” Feng Wu was surprised.","The crown prince smirked. “To look for you.”","“To look for me?” Feng Wu pointed a finger at herself. “Haven’t you heard? Her Majesty the empress dowager specifically gave the order that I’m not allowed to go.”","Jun Linyuan gave her an indifferent glance. “Why do I feel that you look very happy?”","“I’m not!” Feng Wu wasn’t a fool, so of course she wasn’t going to admit it. She immediately said, “I’m not qualified to go? Aww, I’m so sad. I’m such a pitiful girl...”","Jun Linyuan stared at Feng Wu like he was looking at an idiot.","Under his gaze, Feng Wu couldn’t keep pretending, so she cleared her throat to give herself a way out.","“Hey, Jun Linyuan, are you also not going to the winter hunt?” Feng Wu really didn’t want to go.","The wind was the harshest on the Senal Grassland during this season, and it wouldn’t be a comfortable journey. But because of that, the beasts which came out at this time were fierce magical beasts, making it the perfect season for a hunt.","“Let’s go.” Jun Linyuan wrapped his right hand around Feng Wu’s little hand and dragged her toward the door.","“Hey, where are you taking me?” Feng Wu suddenly had a bad feeling.","“The winter hunt.” The crown prince’s answer was very succinct.","Feng Wu said, “Hey, I’m not going.”","The crown prince grunted. “Didn’t you just call yourself a sad, pitiful girl?”"]},{"number":1464,"title":"Chapter 1464 - Why Is His Royal Highness Late? (3)","paragraphs":["Feng Wu buried her face in her hands. “But I’m not qualified to go. Her Majesty the empress dowager gave the order to exclude me from the entourage!”","The crown prince looked at Feng Wu as if she was an idiot. “Are you stupid?”","Feng Wu was dumbfounded.","The crown prince said, “That order is meaningless to me.”","Feng Wu said, “Ahem, that’s an imperial decree.”","Jun Linyuan said, “To other people.”","He was always the one who would be treated differently.","Feng Wu shook her head. What more could she say?","Most of the crown prince’s entourage had left for Dingwu Gate, led by Granny Gong.","When they arrived, the others were ready to set off.","The chief steward had been keeping an eye on the surroundings, and was finally relieved when he saw the people of the crown prince’s residence.","“His Royal Highness is finally here!” The chief steward heaved a sigh of relief.","Bai frowned.","He hadn’t expected Jun Linyuan to arrive in time, and had thought that he could use the opportunity to trash the crown prince. What a waste of an opportunity... Bai was disappointed.","“I see that His Royal Highness decided to show up at the last minute,” Bai said sarcastically.","The chief steward glanced at Bai. “Master Bai, I advise you not to step out of line. His Royal Highness’s position isn’t easily shaken.”","Bai snorted and wouldn’t comment.","A stepmother could turn a real father into a stepfather as well. His Majesty doted on Empress Dugu right now, and of course, he loved their son, the second prince. Was the crown prince’s position that stable? Bai didn’t think so.","The chief steward was about to tell Emperor Wu that the crown prince was here, when Granny Gong gave him a wry smile.","She then told him that the crown prince wasn’t in the carriage.","“What?!” The chief steward panicked.","“How can His Royal Highness not be here?!” The chief steward stared at Granny Gong in disbelief. “Granny Gong, this isn’t the time to make jokes like that!”","Bai gave Granny Gong a strange look as well.","Granny Gong smiled bitterly. She knew what the situation was like right now, but what could she do about the willful prince?","Just then, they heard Emperor Wu’s voice from the carriage nearby.","“What’s with the noise?”","Bai immediately seized the opportunity to step forward and answer loudly, “Your Majesty, the crown prince’s entourage is here.”","The chief steward and Granny Gong frowned as they stared at Bai.","Bai had put it in such an ambiguous way that he had deliberately made the emperor think that the crown prince had arrived.","Emperor Wu was still mad, and he smirked when he heard that. “Tell that unruly son of mine to get over here!”","Granny Gong knew that she couldn’t let things go on like this, so she stepped forward, bowed to the imperial carriage, and replied, “Your Majesty, His Royal Highness hasn’t arrived yet.”","WHAT?!","Empress Dugu’s instigation earlier already made Emperor Wu very displeased with Jun Linyuan’s arrogance, and he flared up when he heard Granny Gong’s answer.","“ Smack! ”","Emperor Wu smacked his chair and an armrest fell off.","Seeing this, Empress Dugu immediately held his arm and said softly, “Your Majesty, please don’t be angry. Do calm down. Rage is bad for you, and your health is the most important thing.”"]},{"number":1465,"title":"Chapter 1465 - Untitled","paragraphs":["Holding Empress Dugu’s hand, Emperor Wu said in a solemn voice, “Even you are concerned about my health, but that defiant son of mine... He wants to see me die from frustration, so that he can take the throne!”","That last bit was a very serious accusation!","Empress Dugu secretly rejoiced, but she feigned a terrified voice and said, “Your Majesty, please don’t be mad! I’m sure that’s not the crown prince’s intention!”","The more she tried to appease Emperor Wu, the angrier he became!","“Since he doesn’t want to go, then don’t!” Emperor Wu waved his hand in vexation.","Seeing that things were getting out of hand, Granny Gong ran to the empress dowager for help.","The old lady was already in her carriage and couldn’t be bothered to move around. However, she sat up in astonishment when she heard the news.","“Is the crown prince still not here?” The old lady’s face darkened.","All the officials were waiting outside Dingwu Gate, and they had all heard Emperor Wu’s opinion of his son, which was very bad for the teenager.","Granny Gong nodded without hesitation.","“That shouldn’t be the case.” The empress dowager frowned and murmured, “Junjun is the type of person who always keeps his promises. He won’t arrive early, but he won’t be late either. There has to be a reason for it.”","After that, she suddenly looked up and stared at Granny Gong. “Speak! What happened in the crown prince’s residence?!”","Granny Gong said, “Well...”","“Are you not going to tell me? Fine!” The empress dowager stared at Granny Gong and said, “Bring Bixi here!”","Bixi?","Granny Gong felt like fainting.","Bixi couldn’t come, because Jun Linyuan had killed her.","“What?” Seeing that Granny Gong wasn’t moving, the empress dowager looked displeased.","“Miss Bixi...” After some hesitation, Granny Gong finally told the old lady, “Miss Bixi is dead.”","WHAT?!","The empress dowager was astonished!","She stared at Granny Gong in disbelief. “How?! Did someone kill her?!”","Granny Gong said calmly, “It was His Royal Highness...”","The furious empress dowager immediately calmed down. “Was it Junjun?”","“Yes, Your Majesty.” Granny Gong nodded.","All anger disappeared from the old lady’s face, and she waved her hand. “I’m sure Junjun had his reasons. So be it. It’s no big deal.”","Granny Gong was speechless.","She was already used to the empress dowager’s behavior, so she wasn’t surprised by her reaction. The others around the old lady were even more used to it, and no one looked the least bit disturbed.","“So, are you here because something happened to the crown prince?” The empress dowager looked at Granny Gong.","Granny Gong immediately said, “His Royal Highness is late and hasn’t arrived yet, so His Majesty is displeased...”","“That’s it? I thought it was something much bigger. Come. Let’s have a look.”","With Granny Lan at her elbow, the empress dowager left her carriage and headed for Emperor Wu’s.","Meanwhile, Emperor Wu was throwing a tantrum at Jun Linyuan’s late arrival.","He smacked the table and bellowed, “If that defiant son doesn’t want to go, disqualify him! We’re leaving now!”","Empress Dugu secretly rejoiced. It seemed that the crown prince had fallen out of favor.","Seeing how furious the emperor was, all the officials shivered in fear and didn’t dare to move.","“Your Majesty!”","A cold voice rang out at that moment."]},{"number":1466,"title":"Chapter 1466","paragraphs":["Emperor Wu was wondering who was bold enough to intrude on him, when he saw that it was his mother.","“Mother, what are you doing here?” Emperor Wu quickly moved closer to hold her arm with an obsequious smile on his face.","Being a filial son, Emperor Wu had always been very obedient toward his mother.","The empress dowager glared at Emperor Wu. “I hear that you’re going to remove Junjun from the entourage?”","Emperor Wu cleared his throat.","The empress dowager glared at him. “It’s true! You really are going to do that!”","Empress Dugu interjected, “Your Majesty, that’s only because His Royal Highness is so...”","“Shut your mouth!” The old lady was furious, and she glowered at Empress Dugu. “I’m talking to my son. This isn’t your place to speak!”","Empress Dugu was speechless.","The empress dowager cast a stern look at Empress Dugu. “You just can’t wait to see the emperor hate the crown prince so that your own son can take his place, can you? I’m telling you: In your dreams!”","Empress Dugu felt so embarrassed at being scolded like that. She let her eyes fill with tears as she said in a pitiful voice, “Your Majesty, you’ve misunderstood me. I just don’t want to see His Majesty wronged...”","Emperor Wu held her hand and was touched by his dear Zitong.","The empress dowager glared at Empress Dugu. “Just shut up!”","Emperor Wu said, “Mother...”","The empress dowager lashed out at Emperor Wu. “Can’t you see by now what her plan is? Why is she crying? Have I wronged her? Junjun has no parents, he should be the one crying!”","Emperor Wu cleared his throat. “Mother, I’m still around...”","“When there’s a stepmother, the real father will forget about his son! You’re as bad as a stepfather now!”","Emperor Wu cleared his throat.","“Hmph!” The empress dowager snorted and sat down on the soft cushion.","Emperor Wu said, “Mother...”","The empress dowager said, “Not another word! I’m going to wait here, and I’m not leaving before Junjun arrives!”","Emperor Wu didn’t know what to say.","Empress Dugu was speechless.","She held Emperor Wu’s hand in frustration, humiliated by the old lady’s scolding.","Emperor Wu could only hold her hand without being able to offer any comforting words.","Around them, all the officials lowered their heads in silence.","The chief steward and Bai didn’t say a word either.","They all knew perfectly well that as long as the empress dowager was around, no one would threaten Jun Linyuan’s position.","While the situation was under control, over on the other end in the crown prince’s residence —","“Come with me.” Jun Linyuan took Feng Wu’s hand.","Feng Wu frowned. “I really don’t want to go.”","Jun Linyuan looked back at Feng Wu. “Are you sure?”","Feng Wu nodded repeatedly. “Yes, very.”","Jun Linyuan snorted. “Who gave you the right to stay here?”","Feng Wu was dumbfounded.","Jun Linyuan snorted. “You go where I go. Got it?”","Feng Wu was speechless.","Before Feng Wu realized what was going on, Jun Linyuan pulled her away, and she had to stumble after him.","Feng Wu tired to shake his hand off, but the crown prince only held her hand tighter.","On their way from the crown prince’s residence to Dingwu Gate —"]},{"number":1467,"title":"Chapter 1467","paragraphs":["A lot of people were positioned along the road just to report on Jun Linyuan’s whereabouts.","“There! His Royal Highness has left his residence.”","“His Royal Highness has passed Anding Street!”","“His Royal Highness has crossed Anhe Bridge.”","“His Royal Highness has...”","Soon, the news reached Dingwu Gate.","Meanwhile —","Everyone was silent, and no one made a sound.","Those who were qualified to come were anything but fools, and they all realized how tense the situation was.","“All hail His Royal Highness —”","A high-pitched voice at the gate announced Jun Linyuan’s arrival.","Despite the eunuch’s shrill voice, the others felt very relieved to hear it. They could finally breathe normally again.","Hearing that, the empress dowager rose to her feet and threw a dirty look at Emperor Wu. “I told you that Junjun would be here! Wasn’t I right?”","After that, she headed out.","Empress Dugu’s face turned livid.","Outside —","“Junjun —”","The empress dowager was elated to see Jun Linyuan. She was about to walk up to him with Granny Lan, when —","She looked up and saw Jun Linyuan holding Feng Wu’s hand.","Immediately, the empress dowager’s face turned livid.","“You —” The empress dowager glared at Feng Wu with cold eyes.","Feng Wu used all her might to throw off Jun Linyuan’s hand.","However, that didn’t appease the empress dowager. The look in her eyes only turned even more fierce!","Taking Jun Linyuan’s hand, she said, “Junjun, you’re finally here. Everyone’s waiting for you. What took you so long?”","Jun Linyuan gave Feng Wu an indifferent glance.","Feng Wu looked at him angrily and wouldn’t let him blame it on her.","“Ahem —”","Jun Linyuan coughed into his fist and asked, “Can we go now?”","“Yes, of course. You lot, help the crown prince to his carriage...”","The empress dowager was used to taking care of Jun Linyuan like this, but it meant much more to the officials.","Feng Wu was about to get into the carriage as well, when the empress dowager shot a warning glance at her.","Feng Wu sighed inwardly.","“Come to my carriage!” The old lady threw a dirty look at Feng Wu and gave the order.","Feng Wu was speechless.","Granny Gong wanted to follow them, but her stomach lurched when she saw the look the empress dowager gave her.","She gave Feng Wu a concerned look before she turned her searching look on Jun Linyuan.","Seeing that Jun Linyuan wouldn’t respond, Granny Gong could only heave a sigh and leave the young people to their own devices.","After a delay of nearly two hours, the procession finally started moving.","In the empress dowager’s carriage.","The old lady sat straight in her seat with a solemn look on her face.","She kept her unblinking gaze on Feng Wu.","Feng Wu lowered her head and stood silently in front of the empress dowager like a pitiful little girl.","The air felt so heavy.","Any other girl would have been frightened to tears by the atmosphere, but not Feng Wu...","She was too strong to be affected. However, she had to look frightened.","“Now you’re nervous?!”","The empress dowager was pleased when she saw how intimidated Feng Wu looked.","“Why was the crown prince late?!” She stared at Feng Wu."]},{"number":1468,"title":"Chapter 1468","paragraphs":["Feng Wu didn’t know what to say, because she had no idea why Jun Linyuan was late. However —","“His Royal Highness has his own way of doing things, and as... as his maid, I know nothing about it.” Feng Wu hesitated at calling herself a maid, but she was going to be Jun Linyuan’s maid for the next 18 days, so she had to force herself to say it.","The empress dowager snorted. “I knew it. How can you possibly know what the crown prince is thinking?!”","Feng Wu rolled her eyes inwardly. If you knew that, why bother asking in the first place?","The empress dowager was visibly less displeased after that, but suddenly, she seemed to recall something, and the look in her eyes turned very fierce!","“Feng Wu!” She glared at Feng Wu. “How dare you!”","She smacked the armrest.","Any other girl would have been frightened to tears, but not Feng Wu. She was far tougher than the old lady could imagine.","“Your Majesty, please don’t be angry!” Feng Wu made to kneel down.","“Clean her hands!” the empress dowager said angrily.","Maids approached Feng Wu with punishment rulers in their hands and ferocious expressions.","The look on Feng Wu’s face changed a little.","The empress dowager was surrounded by capable people, and two strong elderly maids pinned Feng Wu down and twisted her arms behind her back.","Seeing this, Granny Lan was concerned, so when the empress dowager wasn’t looking, she raised the curtain and shot Granny Gong a warning glance.","Granny Gong had been waiting outside the carriage, and she immediately realized that Feng Wu was in trouble.","That was bad.","Knowing how Jun Linyuan felt for Feng Wu, Granny Gong could only imagine how chaotic things would get if the empress dowager ended up punishing Feng Wu.","At that thought, Granny Gong immediately ran off to report to her young master.","“Clean her hands with the rulers!” The empress dowager’s face was livid, and her tone was very decisive.","She believed that Feng Wu had seduced the crown prince. Otherwise, her Junjun would never have arrived late.","Outside the carriage.","Emperor Wu had brought people of various clans with him this time; Northern Feng Mansion, the Zuo family, the Feng clan, the Dugu family, and Mu Manor were all included.","Of the royal family, the empress dowager, the empress, Concubine Oriole, the third and fifth princesses, and the third prince were coming along as well.","They had yet to recover from the shocking scene of Jun Linyuan arriving with Feng Wu’s hand in his. So, right now, they were all discussing it among themselves in their respective carriages.","Lady Northern Feng wasn’t happy about it, because she still didn’t think that Jun Linyuan would be a good husband for Feng Wu.","As for the Zuo family, Mrs Zuo’s eyes were opened so wide, and she wanted to throttle Feng Wu.","Because of Dugu Yamo, Mrs Dugu didn’t hate Feng Wu any less than Mrs Zuo did.","Lady Mu also disliked Feng Wu because of what happened to Mu Yaoyao.","The Feng clan.","Granny Gong had excluded the Feng clan from the list, but Empress Dugu had somehow managed to get their names added back.","Therefore, Feng Liu, Feng Sang and Lady Wang were also here.","There were other families and clans as well.","Mrs Zuo and Mrs Dugu were sitting in the same carriage at the moment.","Mrs Zuo frowned and asked Mrs Dugu, “Sister, did you see it?”","Mrs Dugu asked, “What?”","Mrs Zuo said, “His Royal Highness and Feng Wu are quite familiar with each other.”","Mrs Dugu smiled a little. “Sister, are you nervous? Well, Qingluan is the crown prince’s wife-to-be, so your reaction is only to be expected.”"]},{"number":1469,"title":"Chapter 1469","paragraphs":["Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","Holding Mrs Dugu’s hand, Mrs Zuo smiled wryly. “Sister, I’m not alone in this. Isn’t Yamo interested in that position as well?”","The entire imperial capital had heard how Dugu Yamo had tried to confess her love to Jun Linyuan, but ended up having her immortal flowers taken by Feng Wu. Because of that, Dugu Yamo had become the laughingstock of the whole city.","Mrs Dugu was furious when Mrs Zuo brought that up.","She asked, “Sister, what’s that supposed to mean?!”","Mrs Zuo immediately waved her hands. “Sister, please don’t be mad. I mean no disrespect. It’s just that everyone simply hates Feng Wu’s guts and they want to throttle her with their bare hands. Sister, don’t you feel that way as well?”","Mrs Dugu snorted.","Mrs Zuo tried to play nice. “Sister, how about we work together?”","Mrs Dugu narrowed her eyes and stared at Mrs Zuo without saying a word.","Mrs Zuo smiled. “Sister, don’t you want to get revenge for Yamo? I heard that Yamo was devastated and even tried to kill herself at home. What a pity.”","Dugu Yamo was Mrs Dugu’s favorite, and the girl’s tantrum had turned the household upside down. The mood in the manor was quite depressing and restless.","Dugu Yamo had tried to kill herself by smashing her head against a wall, but she failed, and there was now a big swollen lump on her forehead. It was quite a sorry sight.","At that thought, Mrs Dugu gritted her teeth.","“What are you proposing?” She stared at Mrs Zuo.","Mrs Zuo leaned closer and whispered something in Mrs Dugu’s ear.","Mrs Dugu looked a little relieved, but she still felt doubtful. “Are you sure?”","Mrs Zuo was very confident. “With both of us working on it, of course! If it doesn’t work, we can always ask the empress for help.”","The empress was from the Dugu family, and Mrs Dugu was her sister-in-law, so of course she would be on their side.","Moreover —","Mrs Zuo smiled a little. “Sister, haven’t you noticed? Her Majesty the empress dowager doesn’t like Feng Wu either.”","Mrs Dugu nodded and sighed. “That Feng Wu has really turned into everyone’s target. She’s going to have it very tough on this trip.”","Because it wasn’t just the two of them who wanted to get rid of Feng Wu.","“Everyone just hates her.” Mrs Dugu smiled.","Granny Gong ran at top speed to Jun Linyuan.","In fact, the crown prince had been agitated ever since the empress dowager took Feng Wu away. He couldn’t even clear his mind during his daily meditation.","“Your Royal Highness —” Feng alerted him from outside the carriage.","The crown prince didn’t reply.","After a pause, Feng went on. “Her Majesty doesn’t like Miss Wu. I’m afraid she’s going to face some very difficult times.”","Jun Linyuan snorted. “She’s so unruly. She needs the lesson!”","Feng was speechless. He thought, So be it. Your Royal Highness, I hope you won’t regret it later!","Granny Gong hastily arrived at that moment.","“Your Royal Highness, help! Her Royal Highness has taken out the medium Redness and is going to flog Miss Wu!” Granny Gong was worried sick.","The medium Redness?!","The large one could kill a person, while the medium one could destroy a person’s hands!","The stubborn Jun Linyuan suddenly got to his feet, almost breaking the ceiling of the carriage.","He raised the curtain and walked out without another word.","Feng rolled his eyes.","Despite his stubbornness, the teenager still had to go save his girl in the end."]},{"number":1470,"title":"Chapter 1470","paragraphs":["Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","Jun Linyuan’s long legs took him to the empress dowager’s carriage in no time.","“Stop!” he yelled furiously.","His arrival brought an unbelievable pressure down on everyone’s shoulders.","His bellows were like a thunderclap, and the entire procession stopped involuntarily.","The empress dowager almost had a heart attack. Her face went pale as she stared at Jun Linyuan in astonishment.","It took her a while to realize who it was, and only then did she pat her chest and let out a breath of relief. “You brat! You almost frightened me to death!”","Jun Linyuan’s gaze was on Feng Wu as soon as he walked in.","Right now, Feng Wu had been forced to her knees, and the angry and stubborn look in her eyes reminded him of a young beast.","Her hair and clothes were disheveled, and there were light finger marks on her face.","Jun Linyuan could imagine what had happened. Someone had tried to slap her, and she failed to dodge completely, hence the marks.","This girl...","It pained him to see the stubborn look in her eyes.","Without another word, Jun Linyuan walked up to her, bent down, and gave her his hand.","The crown prince had given Feng Wu his hand.","Everyone envied Feng Wu so much.","But —","To their disbelief, Feng Wu smacked his hand away!","She smacked him...","Someone actually dared do that to the crown prince?!","No one was more astonished than the empress dowager!","How dare that girl do such a thing to her Junjun? She wouldn’t stand for it!","Meanwhile —","Because the carriages had stopped, everyone turned their attention to this section.","Everyone here was sharp-eared, and they all heard the noise from the empress dowager’s carriage.","They were all surprised.","Mrs Zuo and Mrs Dugu were the most astonished of them all.","“Get her out of here and chop her head off!” the empress dowager yelled angrily.","Everyone outside heard that shout.","Mrs Zuo and Mrs Dugu’s carriage was the closest, so they both heard it.","They exchanged looks, and both rejoiced over Feng Wu’s predicament.","Luck was on their side. They didn’t even have to do anything, and the empress dowager already despised Feng Wu so much. She wanted Feng Wu dead!","Hence, the two ladies stopped talking and pricked their ears.","And they weren’t the only ones.","Lady Wang and the other members of the Feng clan were also in shock.","Feng Wu had offended the empress dowager, which was the worst news! The Feng clan was going to be incriminated! What should they do?","However, to their utter surprise, Jun Linyuan didn’t get angry at Feng Wu. Instead, he looked at her in resignation.","“Are you an idiot?!” Jun Linyuan jabbed Feng Wu’s forehead with one long finger before pulling her to her feet. He then tucked her under his arm and carried her away.","Feng Wu was dumbfounded!","“Hey! Jun Linyuan! Put me down! Put me down now!” Feng Wu hit Jun Linyuan with her fists.","But it simply didn’t make a difference."]},{"number":1471,"title":"Chapter 1471","paragraphs":["Right now, Feng Wu was so angry and frustrated that she wanted to pinch Jun Linyuan on his waist.","And that was what she did.","However, his muscles were simply too hard for Feng Wu to make an impact.","What a bummer!","Frustrated, Feng Wu bit down on Jun Linyuan’s arm.","Her teeth almost chipped!","It hurt a lot —","Tears filled her eyes.","Feng Wu kicked and scratched.","But Jun Linyuan still carried her away.","A lot of people had lifted their curtains to see what was going on, and they were all astonished!","That was especially the case for the empress dowager. Right now, her mind was in such a mess that she could only stare blankly into the air.","Until she collapsed in her seat.","“Your Majesty! Your Majesty!”","Granny Lan held the old lady’s hand and pressed her philtrum. She cried out anxiously, “Your Majesty! Wake up!”","The old lady slowly woke up.","Her eyes were still unfocused.","“Junjun... Junjun...” She was so shocked that she couldn’t form a coherent sentence.","“His Royal Highness has left. Your Majesty, please calm down. We can talk about it. Don’t get angry —” Granny Lan comforted her in a low voice.","“How... how can Junjun tolerate that girl?!!!” The empress dowager’s voice shook.","Granny Lan said, “Well...”","“He let that girl do all those unruly things!”","Granny Lan said, “Well...”","“Why?!” The old lady wouldn’t accept the fact and was furious. “After everything I’ve done to raise my baby, he let that annoying girl kick and punch him! Who the hell does she think she is, huh?! She’s nothing!”","Granny Lan tried to calm her down. “Your Majesty, young people have their own way of doing things, so how about we leave it to them to sort out?”","“No way!” The old lady waved her hand angrily. “That girl has such a seductive face, and it’s so obvious that Junjun is under her spell. That’s why he’s been indulging her! No, I can’t let that girl stay close to the crown prince anymore!”","Granny Lan didn’t know what to say. Somehow, she felt that little Feng Wu was the one getting ordered around here.","But she knew that the old lady hated Feng Wu at the moment, so she chose to remain silent.","The empress dowager fumed for the rest of the journey, and the entire procession was enveloped in an oppressive atmosphere.","That was, until they reached the outpost.","With the emperor in the convoy, everything had to be elaborate.","The outpost acted as a halfway residence for traveling officials, and wasn’t exactly a comfortable place to stay overnight. Since Emperor Wu was visiting, the place had been cleaned inside out and revamped.","Lord Mu was in charge of all the meals and accomodations.","While Emperor Wu and his family settled down in the outpost, the rest of his entourage set up tents in the area nearby.","The tents were set up around the outpost in perfect order.","Emperor Wu, the empress dowager, and Jun Linyuan each had a building of their own, but the same couldn’t be said for the rest of the convoy.","In Jun Linyuan’s carriage.","Feng Wu had been kicking and biting ever since Jun Linyuan carried her off in front of everyone.","She decided that had it not been for this guy, she would never have been threatened by the empress dowager and stared at like a circus monkey.","The more she thought about it, the angrier she became, and the more she wanted to bite Jun Linyuan."]},{"number":1472,"title":"Chapter 1472","paragraphs":["But Jun Linyuan’s muscles were too hard for her to bite, which only made Feng Wu angrier. She glared at him like an angry squirrel.","However —","Jun Linyuan only found the frustrated look on her face adorable, and he couldn’t help but pinch her little ear.","Feng Wu stared at Jun Linyuan in utter disbelief.","She was furious, and he actually pinched her ear!","And what was with that goofy smile on his face?","Feng Wu didn’t know what to do. “Jun Linyuan, what on earth do you want?!”","Instead of answering her, the crown prince threw her over his shoulder and walked out of the carriage.","“Hey! Jun Linyuan! Put me down, or I’m really going to be mad!” Feng Wu blushed.","Before, when Jun Linyuan carried her away, there hadn’t been many people around. But now, nearly everyone had gotten out of their carriages, and there were people everywhere. How could Jun Linyuan still do this?","God knew how embarrassing this was!","Moreover —","Looking up, Feng Wu saw Emperor Wu coming out of his carriage, accompanied by Empress Dugu and Concubine Oriole.","Emperor Wu saw Jun Linyuan, and his eyes widened in amazement.","What the heck?!","Emperor Wu stumbled and almost tripped.","“Your Majesty —” The chief steward immediately caught Emperor Wu by the arm and steadied him.","Emperor Wu drew in his breath.","Jun Linyuan!","The arrogant, unapproachable Jun Linyuan was doing such a thing! That just wasn’t something he was supposed to do!","“Am I seeing things?” Emperor Wu blinked and opened his eyes wider.","But he wasn’t mistaken. Jun Linyuan was indeed marching forward with Feng Wu over his shoulder.","“Stop!”","Emperor Wu stopped Jun Linyuan.","Right now, the atmosphere felt rather strange.","Jun Linyuan paused, turned around, and looked at Emperor Wu in bewilderment.","Emperor Wu was furious! That brat!","“What is this? Acting so inappropriately in broad daylight?!” Emperor Wu stared at Jun Linyuan. “Put her down now!”","However —","To Emperor Wu’s frustration, Jun Linyuan only gave him an indifferent glance before marching off with Feng Wu over his shoulder.","That was a direct order from Emperor Wu! An imperial edict!","But Jun Linyuan —","He openly disobeyed it!","Everyone stared at Jun Linyuan from behind before they glanced at Emperor Wu.","Emperor Wu could clearly sense his “imperial halo” dimming a little at that moment.","And Jun Linyuan’s prestige rose yet again!","“Your Majesty —” Empress Dugu saw it as well, so she tugged at Emperor Wu’s sleeve and whispered, “His Royal Highness may not realize the impact of his conduct, but this is going to severely challenge your authority, which was very hard to build up. His Royal Highness isn’t a child anymore. How can he still be so willful?”","“He’s not being willful! He’s deliberately weakening my authority!” Emperor Wu said resentfully.","Empress Dugu was delighted.","She was right. There was already a wedge between the father and son, and she had to make good use of the opportunity.","Hence, Empress Dugu started making her little speech as she walked alongside Emperor Wu, and only the two of them knew what she said.","In the empress dowager’s room.","“Argh...”","Pressing her fingers to her temples, the old lady rolled around in bed in pain."]},{"number":1473,"title":"Chapter 1473","paragraphs":["Granny Lan was worried sick.","She asked, “Your Majesty, how do you feel?”","It was already too painful for the empress dowager to speak, and she could only grunt in agony.","Granny Lan panicked and ran out of the room. While she sent the palace maids to fetch the imperial physicians, she herself went to report to Emperor Wu.","Empress Dugu was listing Jun Linyuan’s vices, when Emperor Wu heard the noise outside. He immediately frowned.","“Your Majesty, Your Majesty! Her Majesty the empress dowager is coming down with something, and she can’t even speak now!”","Granny Lan had served the empress dowager for many years and was a well-respected figure in the palace. That was why she could see the emperor right away.","Hearing this, Emperor Wu rose to his feet and threw a robe over his shoulders as he walked out.","“What’s going on? What’s wrong with the empress dowager?” Emperor Wu asked.","Granny Lan was so anxious that her face was pale. “Her Majesty hasn’t been feeling well since she got out of the carriage. She threw up once and went to bed without having any dinner. Right now, she’s in so much pain that she can’t even speak!”","Emperor Wu was a well-known filial son, and he was running as fast as he could now. He asked anxiously, “Where are the imperial physicians? Where are Master Chu and Master Bai?!”","“I’ve sent someone to fetch them. They should be here by now.” Granny Lan didn’t sound much calmer herself.","After all, this involved the empress dowager’s health, and It was too big a deal!","So, when Emperor Wu arrived, Master Chu and Master Bai were already there.","“Master Chu!” Emperor Wu walked in to see Master Chu opening his eyes as he finished checking the empress dowager’s pulse.","“How is Her Majesty?” Emperor Wu grabbed Master Chu by the collar.","Master Chu looked a little pale, but his voice was relatively calm.","“Your Majesty, Her Majesty’s brain disease is flaring up, which is affecting her entire body —”","“Get to the point!” Emperor Wu bellowed.","Master Chu said sympathetically, “Your Majesty, Her Majesty’s condition is very difficult to treat, and I don’t have much confidence in myself...”","“How’s that even possible?! Aren’t you the most skilled physician in the palace? How can you say that?!” Emperor Wu yelled angrily.","Master Chu said, “Your Majesty, we physicians aren’t omnipotent...”","Emperor Wu said, “I don’t care! Make sure Her Majesty is alright, or I’ll have your head on a plate!”","Master Chu almost broke down...","“But Your Majesty, there’s only a 10% success rate, and I’m worried that even if I cure her now, she may still suffer from residual symptoms...”","Emperor Wu snorted. “Like I said, I don’t care what method you use. I just want Her Majesty to be fine!”","Master Chu was almost driven mad.","The emperor ignored Master Chu and rushed inside to check on the empress dowager. Meanwhile, Master Chu almost pulled all his hair out.","“Master —”","Master Bai had remained silent so far, but he suddenly spoke gingerly.","Master Chu was too absorbed in his agony to notice.","“Master, there’s someone who might be able to help us...”","“Who?” Master Chu frowned.","“Miss Feng Wu,” Master Bai said solemnly. “Miss Feng Wu is a great doctor, and she cured the empress dowager the last time she had a brain condition. So, maybe she’ll know what to do this time.”","Master Chu frowned. “Are you sure?”","Master Bai patted his chest and promised, “Miss Feng Wu is definitely a better doctor than the both of us, and I’m sure she’ll know how to treat the empress dowager.”"]},{"number":1474,"title":"Chapter 1474","paragraphs":["“Master Chu, we’re running out of ideas here. Miss Feng Wu is our only hope.” Master Bai said anxiously. “Her Majesty won’t last much longer.”","Master Chu sighed. “In that case, go ahead.”","“Yes.” Master Bai dashed off after obtaining Master Chu’s permission.","The building which the crown prince was in was a restricted area. However, after Master Bai explained the empress dowager’s perilous situation, he was soon given permission to enter.","Inside, Feng Wu and Jun Linyuan were sitting opposite each other.","Feng Wu was in a fit of pique, and the crown prince looked equally angry. Neither of them were speaking to each other.","That was what Master Bai saw when he walked into the room.","To Master Bai’s astonishment, Feng Wu, the rumored little maid, was sitting opposite the crown prince like his equal. What was more, she was giving the crown prince attitude!","That was unbelievable!","Jun Linyuan stared at Master Bai.","Master Bai didn’t dare delay, and he immediately got to the point. “Her Majesty the empress dowager isn’t feeling well. Miss Wu, help!”","Jun Linyuan frowned.","He was never an affectionate person, but he still cared about the empress dowager.","“What happened?” Jun Linyuan asked, his face darkening.","Master Bai repeated the diagnosis, then concluded, “Her Majesty was probably upset by what happened earlier today, hence the relapse.”","Jun Linyuan didn’t know what to say.","“Miss Feng Wu, please go have a look at the empress dowager. Otherwise, Her Majesty may not be able to survive.”","Jun Linyuan glanced at Feng Wu.","Feng Wu didn’t want to, because the empress dowager hadn’t exactly been nice to her, and she wasn’t one to hesitate to get revenge.","However —","Beggars couldn’t be choosers, and Feng Wu was fully aware of that.","If she turned a blind eye to the empress dowager, and she really died, the consequences would be very severe.","God really liked to play tricks on her.","Rubbing her numb temples, Feng Wu rose to her feet and said in resignation, “I’ll go with you and have a look.”","Elated, Master Bai immediately led the way.","Feng Wu walked past Jun Linyuan without saying a word.","In the empress dowager’s building.","Emperor Wu narrowed his eyes as soon as he saw Feng Wu.","Feng Wu had left a good impression on Emperor Wu. However, Jun Linyuan’s ambiguous attitude toward Feng Wu made Emperor Wu involuntarily dislike her.","Seeing Feng Wu, Master Chu immediately said, “Miss Feng Wu’s skills are as good as mine. With her help, we’ll have a much better chance of curing Her Majesty.”","Emperor Wu stared at Feng Wu for a while and eventually nodded.","Master Chu was very relieved.","But —","To Master Chu’s surprise, while Emperor Wu gave his permission, the empress dowager didn’t!","“No! I won’t let that girl treat me! Get her out of here! Kick her out! I don’t want to see her! Go away!”","The empress dowager reacted very violently when she knew that Feng Wu was going to be her doctor.","Feng Wu frowned a little.","She didn’t like treating the empress dowager either. She was a supreme-level medicine refiner and was usually respected by everyone. But now, the old lady was so rude.","Feng Wu said coldly, “Your Majesty, you are indeed having a relapse. Not treating it won’t kill you, but it’ll do irreparable damage to your brain. It’s your decision.”"]},{"number":1475,"title":"Chapter 1475","paragraphs":["“How dare you curse me?! You defiant girl! Take her out and cut her head off!”","Feng Wu was speechless.","She turned around and shrugged at Emperor Wu. “It’s not that I don’t want to treat the empress dowager, but Her Majesty won’t allow me. Please don’t blame me when Her Majesty’s condition deteriorates.”","After that, she ignored the empress dowager, who was drained of all color from the pain, and turned to leave.","Emperor Wu was dumbfounded. He couldn’t imagine that someone could be as bold as his defiant son!","“Feng Wu!” Emperor Wu bellowed.","Feng Wu paused and looked at Emperor Wu in resignation. “Her Majesty is blessed, and her condition isn’t life-threatening for now. But it will get worse, and she’ll be in more and more pain.”","After a pause, Feng Wu added, “When that happens, her condition will be so severe that no medicine will work on her, and there’s nothing I will be able to do.”","Emperor Wu was dumbfounded, but he soon realized what she said. “Then why are you still leaving? Treat her now!”","Feng Wu shrugged. “Her Majesty won’t let me.”","Emperor Wu’s face darkened. “Treat her! That’s an order!”","With no other choice, Feng Wu went up to the empress dowager and said, “Your Majesty, I’m going to treat you...”","“Go away!!! I would rather die than have you treat me! Get out!” The empress dowager didn’t try to hide her resentment of Feng Wu.","Feng Wu looked at Emperor Wu in resignation. “The patient is out of control, which will hasten the deterioration. Her Majesty is only going to make herself worse.”","Emperor Wu was furious, but there was nothing he could do.","In the end, Feng Wu left.","It was a very difficult night for the empress dowager, and she almost passed out from the pain several times.","The second day —","Things only got worse.","The old lady couldn’t even get up. She kept making incoherent sounds, and one could tell from her pale face and trembling body that she was in extreme pain.","Emperor Wu kept giving Master Chu more pressure, but what could Master Chu do? He had to go to Feng Wu repeatedly.","Feng Wu came several times, but the empress dowager just wouldn’t let her...","It was the same thing all over again.","On the third morning, the empress dowager was practically unconscious. She was too dizzy to even open her eyes.","She really could die if they didn’t do anything.","Meanwhile, all the families of the officials had gathered around the empress dowager’s courtyard and were flustered.","It was as if the air had frozen.","“Is Her Majesty sick?”","“We’ve only been here for a short while, and Her Majesty is already sick. The winter hunt is going to be suspended.”","“That’s not the main consequence, but the possibility that Her Majesty may...”","“Have you heard? Feng Wu was invited inside.”","“What’s she doing there?”","“Isn’t she supposed to be a good doctor? I think she’s here to treat the empress dowager.”","“I’m going to laugh. She’s just a girl. A good doctor? Give me a break!”","–","When the ladies were together, they whispered among themselves, and Feng Wu was the main topic of conversation.","“Hey, isn’t it Lady Wang?”","Soon, they noticed that Feng Yanfeng’s wife was there as well.","Lady Wang didn’t have anywhere to hide and soon became the center of attention.","Mrs Zuo’s eyes flickered when she saw Lady Wang, and she smiled. “Lady Wang, Feng Wu is the fifth daughter of your clan, isn’t she?”"]},{"number":1476,"title":"Chapter 1476","paragraphs":["Chapter 1476: Untitled","What else could Lady Wang say? She could only smile bitterly and said, “She is.”","Immediately, all the ladies gave Lady Wang strange looks.","Mrs Zuo feigned an indifferent tone. “Lady Wang, I’ve been meaning to tell you something for a long time, but I’ve hesitated to do so.”","“Mrs Zuo, feel free to speak your mind.” Lady Wang forced herself to face the questioning looks.","“Isn’t your Feng Wu out of line?” Mrs Zuo frowned. “Is that how the Feng family raises their daughter?”","“Of course not!”","Before Lady Wang could reply, Feng Liu said loudly, “Mrs Zuo, Feng Wu is a vile and evil person by nature. My family’s teachings have nothing to do with it!”","Lady Wang added, “That girl went to Northern Border City five years ago and lived like a wild person out there. It’s not a surprise that she became so twisted.”","Mrs Zuo didn’t expect to hear such a reply.","She had thought that Lady Wang would be on Feng Wu’s side.","If that was the case...","That made things much easier!","Mrs Zuo smiled. “Lady Wang, to be honest, Feng Wu’s reputation isn’t exactly good at the moment.”","Lady Wang smiled bitterly. “Really?”","Mrs Zuo said, “That’s right. Everyone’s been saying that Feng Wu is the crown prince’s bed-warming maid, but she’s the daughter of the Feng family. How is she ever going to get married?”","Lady Wang smiled wryly. “That’s true. I’ve talked to her about it, but...”","She hesitated before she finished her sentence. This was such a good chance to slander Feng Wu that she didn’t want to waste it.","At that thought, Lady Wang smiled in resignation and said, “That girl wanted to be His Royal Highness’s maid, and nothing we said could stop her. What else could we do?”","Wow —","That shocked a lot of the ladies.","They thought that Feng Wu stayed with Jun Linyuan because he forced her to, but judging from Lady Wang’s tone, the crown prince hadn’t forced Feng Wu at all. She was the one who wouldn’t leave him alone!","“Really? Feng Wu offered to be His Royal Highness’s maid herself?” Mrs Dugu asked casually.","Lady Wang gave them a bitter smile. “I shouldn’t be saying this, but that girl is so willful and arrogant, and she’s constantly giving me headaches. She’s fatherless, and her mother is mentally ill. Her uncle and I have tried to keep her in line, but she’s just so impossible! Therefore, we can only let her do whatever she wants. There’s nothing we can do, even if we want to.”","Those words made the other ladies exchange amazed looks.","So, Feng Wu had really volunteered to be the crown prince’s little maid? She was so infatuated...","Immediately, the ladies that had liked Feng Wu before all frowned.","They all looked down on a girl without self-respect.","“I didn’t know Feng Wu was like that.”","“I used to think quite highly of her. As it turned out —”","“She was telling everyone that His Royal Highness forced her to stay with him, but —”","“Being in love with the crown prince isn’t all that bad, but only a despicable person would pretend to be all innocent!”","While the others expressed their disdain toward Feng Wu, Mrs Zuo and Mrs Dugu exchanged excited looks."]},{"number":1477,"title":"Chapter 1477","paragraphs":["That was a surprise. Lady Wang was actually on their side.","At that thought, they became much nicer to Lady Wang — so much so that other people might take them for real sisters.","While they were engaged in excited discussion, the empress dowager was getting worse.","She was barely conscious and was slipping into a coma.","Emperor Wu was so anxious that he didn’t stop pacing.","He suddenly turned around and stared at Master Chu, who had just come out of the room. “How’s Her Majesty doing? Speak!”","Master Chu furrowed his brow and was full of resignation. “Your Majesty, Miss Feng Wu predicted everything.”","“What?” Emperor Wu stared at Master Chu.","Master Chu immediately said, “Miss Feng Wu said a few days ago that Her Majesty’s condition would get worse, and so would the damage to her brain... Miss Feng Wu was correct about everything, and Her Majesty’s condition is very severe now! Your Majesty, Miss Feng Wu is the only one who can treat Her Majesty now. Otherwise, we may lose her!”","A hush fell over the room...","Emperor Wu stared at Master Chu in anger and frustration.","Master Chu stressed, “Your Majesty, Miss Feng Wu is our only hope now. No one else can save Her Majesty now!”","Emperor Wu bellowed, “Go get her, then!”","Master Chu nodded and quickly left.","However —","Master Chu arrived at Jun Linyuan’s building only to find that Feng Wu wasn’t there.","For the first time, he panicked.","He stared at Granny Gong and said anxiously, “What are we going to do now? His Majesty is waiting for her! How can she not be here now?!”","Her Majesty’s life was in danger!","Granny Gong gave it some thought and said, “Miss Feng Wu gave me a letter before she left and told me to give it to you when you came.”","Master Chu took the letter and quickly opened it.","One look and he was over the moon.","He dashed off with the letter.","Master Chu ran through the corridor like a gust of wind and rushed into the empress dowager’s building.","“Your Majesty, Her Majesty is going to be alright!” Master Chu sounded excited when he said, “Miss Feng Wu left us this treatment, and I’ve read it. If we follow these instructions, there’s a 70% chance of saving Her Majesty.”","“Where’s Feng Wu?” Emperor Wu was displeased.","The empress dowager’s life was on the line; where was she?","“Well... I heard that she’s away. As for where she went, I didn’t ask.” All of Master Chu’s attention was on Feng Wu’s letter.","“Her Majesty is seriously ill with her life hanging in the balance, and Feng Wu thinks she can go out just like that? Damn her!” Emperor Wu bellowed.","Master Chu raised the letter in his hand. “Your Majesty, Miss Feng Wu might think that this letter alone is enough to save Her Majesty, so...”","“The success rate will be more than 70% if she does it herself! She has no respect for Her Majesty or the royal family at all!”","She was as arrogant as Jun Linyuan!","The more Emperor Wu thought about it, the angrier he became. He then bellowed, “Bring Feng Yanfeng here right now!”","Hence, when Master Chu went to treat the empress dowager, Feng Yanfeng was brought in, and he looked completely confused.","“Your Majesty —” Feng Yanfeng bowed as soon as he saw Emperor Wu.","Meanwhile, all the people outside the building were murmuring among themselves as well.","“Why does His Majesty want to see Master Feng so suddenly?”","“Master Feng has always behaved himself. Did something happen?”","“Plus, it was the chief steward, His Majesty’s most capable servant, who went to fetch Master Feng...”"]},{"number":1478,"title":"Chapter 1478","paragraphs":["“Plus, it was the chief steward, His Majesty’s most capable servant, who went to fetch Master Feng...”","The mood felt rather heavy.","Master Zuo, Master Dugu, Lord Mu, and many other people were all confused.","They all wanted to know what on earth was happening inside.","In the building —","Feng Yanfeng had only just knelt down, when Emperor Wu raised a leg and kicked Feng Yanfeng in the chest.","Feng Yanfeng felt a stabbing pain in his chest. Before he knew it, he was flying backward.","He flew all the way out of the building.","Wow —","It happened so suddenly that everyone outside was astonished!","“What did Master Feng do to offend His Majesty?”","“Master Feng is the minister of the Ministry of Official Personnel. What unforgivable thing did he do to deserve such humiliation?”","“It seems that we’re going to have a new minister.”","Feng Yanfeng was the most baffled of them all!","It never occurred to him that His Majesty would be so angry and so merciless.","The moment Feng Yanfeng flew out of the building, Lady Wang ran over to his side, held his thigh, and burst into tears.","“Master, are you alright? Master, what happened? Master —”","Feng Yanfeng didn’t lose control. He brushed Lady Wang’s hand off and scrambled to his feet. He then walked up to Emperor Wu and knelt down. “Your Majesty, I don’t know what I did to deserve that punishment, but I hold no resentment. But Your Majesty, could you maybe tell me what I did wrong?”","“Hmph!”","Emperor Wu stood there with an expressionless face, his eyes as cold as ice.","“A member of your clan made a mistake, and as the head of the clan, you have to take the fall! I’m removing you from your office, starting from today. Do you have a problem with that?”","Emperor Wu didn’t say the exact words, but he dropped enough hints.","Feng Yanfeng got it after his initial shock, and asked, “Is it because of... Feng Wu?”","Emperor Wu didn’t answer that question and only waved his hands. “Get out!”","Once he had taken care of Feng Yanfeng, Emperor Wu crossed his hands behind his back and walked back inside.","But —","He might have left, but the impact was enough to make everyone wonder.","“Feng Wu! It’s all because of her!” Lady Wang finally realized what had happened and started yelling at Feng Yanfeng. “Master, did you just get dismissed because of Feng Wu?!”","Feng Yanfeng was still processing what had happened.","He had just lost his job, and it was because of... Feng Wu?","At that moment, Feng Yanfeng felt like throttling Feng Wu.","“Damn her! Damn that girl!” Feng Yanfeng almost passed out from rage.","People of the Zuo and Dugu families exchanged looks and revelled in his predicament.","“Sister, that’s so hilarious, hahaha —” Mrs Zuo held Mrs Dugu’s hand and laughed wholeheartedly. “Luck really is on our side. I didn’t expect Feng Yanfeng to be kicked out so easily.”","Mrs Dugu nodded.","“But why?” Mrs Zuo was confused. “What did Feng Yanfeng do to upset His Majesty so much? Or rather, what did Feng Wu do?”","Because of her relationship with the empress, Mrs Dugu had more information.","“I’ll tell only you.” Mrs Dugu told Mrs Zuo, “I heard that Feng Wu could have treated Her Majesty when she got sick, but Feng Wu went off to enjoy herself and abandoned Her Majesty.”"]},{"number":1479,"title":"Chapter 1479","paragraphs":["“What?!” Mrs Zuo couldn’t believe her ears. “How dare that Feng Wu?!”","Mrs Dugu smirked. “That girl thinks she has His Royal Highness’s favor, so she’s so full of herself now. She’s even bold enough to disrespect Her Majesty!”","Mrs Zuo clicked her tongue. “That Feng Wu is so arrogant. I bet His Majesty hates her so much now!”","Mrs Dugu nodded. “If Her Majesty can’t be treated, Feng Wu is going to get the blame. When that happens, no matter how His Royal Highness tries to protect her, she’s still going to die.”","The two ladies weren’t the only ones talking about it.","Everyone gathered together in twos and threes, worried about the empress dowager’s illness while feeling excited over the rumor about the Feng clan.","And all they talked about was —","If the empress dowager died, what kind of situation would Feng Wu be in?","Countless people couldn’t wait to see Feng Wu in trouble.","It just so happened that Feng Wu came back at that moment.","She was carrying a basket on her back, and it was filled with branches with dark green leaves that gave off a faint fragrance.","“Look! Feng Wu is back!”","“It really is her! How dare she come back now?!”","“She’s so going to die!”","Feng Liu had been waiting outside the outpost for Feng Wu. As soon as she saw her, she ran toward her at top speed.","“Feng Wu!”","Feng Liu’s eyes spat fire. She glared at Feng Wu, as if trying to burn Feng Wu to ash with the fury in her eyes.","Feng Wu frowned a little, glanced at her, and tried to walk around her.","However, Feng Liu wouldn’t let her leave.","“Feng Wu, you’re too ashamed to see me, aren’t you?! You can’t even meet my eyes!","“Feng Wu, do you know how outrageous you’ve been?!","“Feng Wu, I don’t care what happens to you, but why would you incriminate the entire Feng clan?!","“Feng Wu, what happened to my father is all your fault!”","–","Knowing that she couldn’t defeat Feng Wu, Feng Liu could only follow her as she complained.","But Feng Wu couldn’t even be bothered to look at her.","Until —","“Feng Wu!” A cold voice rang out behind them.","Feng Wu narrowed her eyes and turned around. It was indeed Feng Yiran.","“Come with me!” Feng Yiran led her away. “Father has been removed from his office because of you, and he’s been badly injured. Don’t you feel guilty at all?”","Feng Yanfeng?!","Feng Wu thought about her fence-sitting uncle.","She had no affection for that uncle, but Feng Yanfeng could still be a useful pawn in the future, so she knew that she should visit him.","“Lead the way,” Feng Wu said coldly.","The Feng clan was no longer one of the nine major families, and they weren’t ranked very high either. Therefore, their living quarters were quite far from the center.","Feng Yanfeng was sulking when Feng Wu arrived.","“Father, Feng Wu is here!” Feng Yiran led Feng Wu to Feng Yanfeng.","Feng Yanfeng felt a pang in his chest.","Feng Wu! She was the reason behind everything!","At that thought, Feng Yanfeng stared at Feng Wu in disbelief, and his gaze reminded her of icy blades."]},{"number":1480,"title":"Chapter 1480","paragraphs":["“How dare you come here!” Feng Yanfeng threw the bowl of medicine in his hand directly at Feng Wu’s face.","The thick liquid in the bowl arced through the air as it flew at Feng Wu.","Luckily, she reacted in time and immediately stepped aside to dodge the bowl and the liquid.","Thump!","The bowl broke into pieces on the floor with a crisp sound.","Feng Yanfeng was even more furious when he saw Feng Wu move away.","“How dare you! Feng Wu, how dare you!” Feng Yanfeng sprang up from his bed and asked, “Tell me! What on earth did you do?!”","Feng Wu frowned and looked confused. “What do you mean?”","“Quit pretending! Cough — ” Feng Yanfeng was shaking from head to toe. “If you haven’t done something to offend His Majesty, why would he blame it on me?! You’re the one who got me in trouble! Don’t you realize that?!”","Feng Wu was speechless.","Feng Yanfeng stared at Feng Wu. “Speak! What on earth did you do?”","Feng Wu shrugged and looked all innocent. “I didn’t do anything. As for why His Majesty is mad at you... How about you go ask him yourself?”","Just then, she heard light footsteps nearby.","Steward Feng quickly came in and whispered something in Feng Yanfeng’s ear before he backed away.","Feng Yanfeng was completely astounded by the news.","He looked at Feng Wu as if she was an idiot. “You... You!!!”","Feng Wu still looked very innocent. “What?”","Feng Yanfeng couldn’t stop trembling. When he pointed at Feng Wu, his finger trembled as well, which showed how astonished he was.","“You... You could have saved Her Majesty, but you didn’t! Feng Wu! You turned away from the empress dowager!”","Feng Yanfeng wanted to kill Feng Wu right there and then!","She would have been generously rewarded if she had saved the empress dowager, and the entire Feng clan could have risen because of it!","The crime for not helping the empress dowager was so severe that the entire Feng clan could be killed for it!","“You — how could you do that?!”","Feng Yanfeng was so agitated that he couldn’t form a coherent sentence, and he glared at Feng Wu. “We can overlook the generous reward, but we can’t possibly survive the punishment! Feng Wu, you’re taking the entire clan down with you!!!”","Feng Yanfeng’s eyes were bloodshot, and blue veins popped on his forehead. He was so agitated!","And when he said those words, he wasn’t the only one agitated.","“OMG!”","“Feng Wu has —”","“Feng Wu! How dare you!”","–","Lady Wang, Feng Yanfeng, Feng Sang, and Feng Liu all stood there in astonishment. Their heads went blank, and they all trembled violently.","Feng Wu left the empress dowager when the latter was severely ill. That was enough to have the entire Feng clan killed!","“Feng Wu, I’m going to kill you!”","“Feng Wu, how dare you!”","“Feng Wu, go to hell!”","–","Lady Wang trembled violently, and her heart raced. She rushed over to Feng Yanfeng and yelled, “Master, Master, our clan can’t keep this girl anymore! We won’t know how to teach her! Master, after what she did to you, do you want to see the same thing happen to our children?!”","“Pfft —”","Feng Yanfeng was so exasperated and shocked that he spat out a mouthful of blood!","Cough, cough —","After his coughing fit, Feng Yanfeng looked up, and his eyes were bloodshot red!"]},{"number":1481,"title":"Chapter 1481","paragraphs":["“Feng Wu, go to hell!”","His voice was so loud that it was like a thunderclap in the ears of the others.","Wow —","People were already talking about what was going on with the Feng clan, and they were even more curious now.","Lord Mu was in charge, and he quickly headed over.","Since Lord Mu was here, so were Master Zuo and Master Dugu.","All three were people Feng Yanfeng had tried to befriend recently, but he wasn’t happy to see them now.","Lord Mu couldn’t care less. He told Feng Yanfeng when he arrived, “Old Feng, let’s talk like civilized people. Shouting won’t solve anything.”","Master Zuo glanced at Feng Wu and smiled at Feng Yanfeng. “Feng Wu is only a kid now, and she needs more guidance. Don’t rush it.”","Feng Yanfeng almost choked on his own breath.","“That brat! She, she...” Feng Yanfeng almost couldn’t breathe. “The empress dowager’s life is hanging in the balance, but she went off to have fun! She’s trying to ruin our clan! I won’t have it!”","Feng Yanfeng struggled to his feet and grabbed Lord Mu’s hand. “My lord, you and the other officials are going to be my witnesses today! I’m going to make an announcement as the head of the Feng clan!”","Feng Yanfeng glared at Feng Wu and stressed each word: “From now on, Feng Wu isn’t a member of the Feng clan anymore!”","WHAT?!","That announcement was unexpected but predictable at the same time.","“Old Feng —” Lord Mu said calmly, “Let’s talk it over. I’m sure we can solve this. Removing her name from the clan is such a big deal that you have to be sure!”","Lady Wang and the others looked expectantly at Feng Yanfeng.","They had waited for this day for so long!","Both Master Zuo and Master Dugu tried to make Feng Yanfeng reconsider his decision.","However, Feng Yanfeng shook his head decisively. “No, I’ve given it enough thought already. Feng Wu has to be kicked out today!”","Master Zuo shook his head and sighed. He then shot a warning glance at Feng Wu. “Kiddo, what are you doing just standing there? Do you really want to get your name removed from the clan and become a lonely soul with no one to depend on? You should be pleading with your uncle right now!”","To have one’s name removed from their clan was such a big deal that everyone was convinced that Feng Wu would panic, but —","Feng Wu just stood there with the sunlight behind her.","The look on her face was very calm.","And she was completely unperturbed.","She smiled a little and asked quietly, “Are you going to remove my name from the clan?”","All eyes were on her.","Feng Wu smirked. “Do you think you can do that just because you want to?”","WHAT?!","Everyone’s stomachs lurched.","That was so arrogant!","“Feng Wu, I’m your uncle and the head of the clan. I have the right —”","“The head of the clan? For now. You don’t know what will happen in the future.” Feng Wu smirked.","“You —” Feng Yanfeng wanted to say something else, but Feng Wu waved him off.","“We’ll talk about it later; we’ll see who gets kicked out in the end.” Feng Wu sounded impatient. “I don’t have time for this. Wait until I’m not busy.”","She left after those words.","Just like that.","Everyone watched in disbelief as she walked away."]},{"number":1482,"title":"Chapter 1482","paragraphs":["That wasn’t what they were expecting!","It shouldn’t have played out like that —","“Take her down! Bring that brat to me!” Feng Yanfeng bellowed, feeling that his authority had been severely challenged.","However, no one moved.","Feng Yiran and Feng Liu weren’t Feng Wu’s match.","Master Zuo and the others would only play the happy onlookers and wouldn’t offer any help.","Feng Yanfeng didn’t know what to do; he was the only one who could handle Feng Wu now!","At that thought, he pounced at Feng Wu like a hungry wolf!","He decided that he would regain his lost dignity himself!","Crack!","Feng Yanfeng grabbed Feng Wu’s shoulder from behind!","However, he immediately felt a stabbing pain in his fingers, as if he had been hit by some invincible power!","Whoosh —","Feng Yanfeng involuntarily drew back his hand and stared at Feng Wu in astonishment!","“What are you wearing?!”","There was a line of needle marks on Feng Yanfeng’s palm!","Feng Wu narrowed her eyes.","She was wearing a simple vest, which Jun Linyuan had put on her when she was asleep. She wanted to take it off and throw it away, but Jun Linyuan wouldn’t let her no matter what.","Who would have thought that the soft vest would be so useful.","Feng Wu sneered at Feng Yanfeng and turned to leave.","“That brat!!!” Feeling utterly humiliated, Feng Yanfeng thought he was going to explode!","Lord Mu and the others felt embarrassed for Feng Yanfeng as well...","As the head of the Feng clan, he tried to remove Feng Wu from the clan, but humiliated himself instead...","Master Zuo was very disappointed in Feng Yanfeng as well.","Word of Feng Yanfeng trying to remove Feng Wu from the clan soon got out.","With so many people staying in the small outpost, they all gathered in small groups and the news spread very quickly.","“What? The Feng clan is going to kick Feng Wu out?! But why?”","“Why do you think? I heard that Master Feng was removed from his post because of Feng Wu.”","“Has she been kicked out already?”","“I don’t think so.”","“Why?”","“Don’t you see? His Royal Highness is behind Feng Wu. He takes her with him everywhere, which is why she’s so arrogant. Even if Master Feng wants to kick her out, he still has to consider the crown prince’s feelings.”","“That Feng Wu is so...”","Feng Wu went straight back to her building after she left the Feng clan.","She hadn’t gone out to stroll about, but to pick some herbs.","The empress dowager had been sick for so long that Feng Wu had to use a herb known as dragon wood fiber. However, it wasn’t a common herb and could be quite difficult to find.","Feng Wu left very early that morning, and with her pet’s help, she finally found one.","After washing the dragon wood fiber clean, Feng Wu deftly prepared it.","She was familiar with the process, so in less than an hour, the dragon wood fiber had been turned into a small pile of black powder.","She then poured the powder into a small porcelain vial.","The vial was the size of a pinky, and just big enough for the dragon wood fiber powder.","Feng Wu handed the vial to Granny Gong. “Take this to Master Chu.”","With how smart Granny Gong was, she immediately saw that it was a life-saving ingredient for the empress dowager.","Feng Wu said, “Boil three bowls of water until only one bowl is left, then pour the dragon wood fiber powder in. It can’t be more than the size of a fingernail, but don’t put in too little either.”"]},{"number":1483,"title":"Chapter 1483","paragraphs":["Granny Gong nodded, but she couldn’t help prodding Feng Wu. “Miss Wu, why don’t you take it to Her Majesty yourself?”","Feng Wu said coldly, “That’s not necessary. Granny Gong, just go ahead.”","The empress dowager had been so mean to Feng Wu, so she had no reason to go near the old lady. She wasn’t a masochist.","As for improving her image with the empress dowager, Feng Wu didn’t see any point in doing that.","Granny Gong smiled bitterly.","The empress dowager was indeed inclined to be hostile toward Feng Wu, and their relationship would only worsen if they saw each other now. It would be better that they stayed away from each other.","Granny Gong quickly headed back to the empress dowager with the dragon wood fiber powder.","Meanwhile, Master Chu was very anxious.","Sweat was rolling down his forehead.","He was facing a very critical situation.","He thought that there was a 70% chance of success, but once he cut the empress dowager open, that hope disappeared.","What should he do?","Looking at the cut he made in the empress dowager’s head, Master Chu felt a chill run down his spine, and his hands turned cold.","“Master Chu? Doctor?!”","Master Bai was Master Chu’s assistant, and he lost most hope when he saw the blood gushing out of the empress dowager’s forehead. When he noticed Master Chu’s pale face, Master Bai almost passed out.","Master Chu waved his hand and blinked hard.","He told himself not to panic and to calm down.","He had experienced quite a few critical moments in his life and had narrowly escaped death a few times, but he had survived them all, hadn’t he?","Wait! Feng Wu!","The idea struck Master Chu and he told Master Bai to fetch Feng Wu immediately!","Emperor Wu grabbed Master Bai as soon as he left the room.","“How did it go? How’s the empress dowager?”","Emperor Wu wasn’t the only one waiting outside. The entire royal family was there.","There were Empress Dugu, Concubine Oriole, the third and fifth princesses, and the princes.","Everyone looked anxiously at Master Bai.","Master Bai was almost in tears and said loudly, “Her Majesty is in critical condition right now, and her life is hanging in the balance. I have to find Miss Feng Wu now. She’s our only hope!”","Feng Wu was their only hope?","Empress Dugu had a complicated feeling in her heart.","If Feng Wu didn’t come and the empress dowager died, it would be the best news for her.","Just then, Granny Gong came into view.","“Miss Feng Wu —”","As soon as Master Bai spoke, Granny Gong shook her head and said, “Miss Wu isn’t here, but she had me bring the medicine.","“Here’s some dragon wood fiber powder, which is good for stopping the bleeding. To use it...”","After calmly repeating the instructions, Granny Gong handed over the bottle containing the powder.","Master Bai’s eyes lit up. He took the bottle with both hands and ran back inside without so much as a thank you.","Right now, everyone was concerned about the empress dowager.","But one or two individuals still wanted to stir up trouble.","“Is this dragon wood fiber powder freshly made?” Jun Wuxia, the third princess, stared at Granny Gong.","Granny Gong said, “Yes.”","Jun Wuxia asked, “Granny Gong, did you meet Feng Wu just then?”","Granny Gong said, “Yes.”","Jun Wuxia said, “So, she’s here in the outpost.”","Granny Gong said, “Yes.”","Jun Wuxia stared at Granny Gong with her cold eyes. “If that’s the case, why won’t Feng Wu come here and treat the empress dowager herself?”","Immediately, everyone gave Granny Gong strange looks.","That was right. Why?"]},{"number":1484,"title":"Chapter 1484","paragraphs":["The fifth princess said, “I heard that Her Majesty wouldn’t let Feng Wu treat her.”","Jun Wuxia waved her off. “Her Majesty can dislike Feng Wu as much as she wants, but Feng Wu has a duty to treat Her Majesty. Since she sent the dragon wood fiber powder, she has to know that Her Majesty is in critical condition. Why won’t she come here when Her Majesty’s life is hanging in the balance? What hidden agenda does Feng Wu have?!”","Empress Dugu had raised Jun Wuxia into a spoiled princess. She had always been willful and reckless, so why would she suddenly become so sensible and methodical?","Granny Gong kept her gaze on the princess and realized that someone had to be helping her out.","She looked from Jun Wuxia to a maid standing next to her.","The maid was called Yulian.","Yulian’s stomach lurched when she saw the look in Granny Gong’s eyes.","“Granny Gong, don’t you want to explain on Feng Wu’s behalf? If not, should we conclude that Feng Wu is disrespecting Her Majesty?” Jun Wuxia smiled at Granny Gong.","Having served in the imperial palace for so many years, Granny Gong was too experienced to be intimidated by Jun Wuxia.","She said calmly, “Miss Wu indeed knows how critical Her Majesty’s condition is. She knew that three days ago.”","Wow —","All eyes were on Granny Gong, and everyone was shocked by that bold statement.","Granny Gong went on. “Miss Wu also knew that Her Majesty would need the dragon wood fiber powder today, so she went out with a basket before sunrise this morning on her own and went into the mountains. She searched throughout the day until the moon rose, when she finally found a dragon wood fiber plant. She then brought it back and turned it into a powder.”","After a pause, Granny Gong added, “Miss Wu knows that Her Majesty doesn’t like her, so to avoid agitating Her Majesty and exacerbating her condition, Miss Wu gave up this great opportunity to show off her contribution.”","Looking around, Granny Gong said, “If you don’t believe me, just wait and see. If Master Chu can save Her Majesty with the dragon wood fiber powder, you’ll know I’m telling the truth and how sincere Miss Feng Wu is.”","That was an impressive speech. Not only did Granny Gong sabotage the trap Jun Wuxia had set, she also made Feng Wu out to be someone who wasn’t eager to claim credit.","Jun Wuxia clenched her fists angrily and glared at Granny Gong.","Granny Gong wasn’t intimidated at all and only smiled back at her.","The atmosphere felt rather strange.","Just then —","The closed door finally opened.","Master Chu and Master Bai came out, supporting each other.","“How did it go?” Emperor Wu was the first to react, and he grabbed Master Chu’s arm.","Master Chu looked like someone who had just escaped death. He breathed out slowly, and there was a faint smile on his face.","He said, “It was very dangerou at first, and we almost didn’t succeed. Luckily, Miss Feng Wu’s dragon wood fiber powder arrived in time. Otherwise, the consequence would have been unthinkable.”","Master Bai shook his head as well. “Her Majesty wouldn’t stop bleeding. Without the powder, she wouldn’t have made it.”","She would have died!","Everyone knew what Master Bai meant.","That was why they were so shocked!","“Is that dragon wood fiber powder so miraculous?” Emperor Wu cried out.","Master Chu said, “A medicine is the most valuable when it’s used correctly. Miss Feng Wu is a genius in this respect. I would never have thought about this medicine myself.”"]},{"number":1485,"title":"Chapter 1485","paragraphs":["Master Bai couldn’t stop praising Feng Wu either. “Miss Feng Wu’s medical skills are impeccable. With one look, she knows all the steps to be taken. She’s more than talented. She’s the greatest genius ever!”","Master Chu and Master Bai showered Feng Wu with compliments and wouldn’t stop talking, which annoyed many others.","Especially Jun Wuxia, who had gone pale with rage.","Seeing that the empress dowager was out of danger, Granny Gong left the crowd.","Emperor Wu was the one at a loss now.","Late that night.","Emperor Wu and Empress Dugu sat on the bed.","Seeing the big frown on Emperor Wu’s face, Empress Dugu held his hand.","Emperor Wu’s grip was forceful.","Empress Dugu caressed Emperor Wu’s face gently and said softly, “Your Majesty, are you worried about Her Majesty? Didn’t Master Chu say that Her Majesty is no longer in danger now? She’ll be fine once she wakes up tomorrow morning.”","Emperor Wu smiled bitterly. “I’m not worried about Her Majesty. I just don’t know...”","Empress Dugu asked, “Yes?”","Emperor Wu rubbed his forehead. He had been too impulsive today and had embarrassed himself.","With how smart Empress Dugu was, she immediately guessed what it was about, so she asked with a smile, “Your Majesty, is it about Feng Yanfeng?”","Emperor Wu heaved a long sigh and nodded.","He didn’t need to hide it from his Zitong.","Caressing Emperor Wu’s hand, Empress Dugu smiled. “Your Majesty, why don’t you give Feng Yanfeng his job back?”","Emperor Wu rubbed his forehead. “Won’t that make me look indecisive?”","Empress Dugu hesitated before asking, “Your Majesty, what do you have in mind?”","Emperor Wu asked, “How about I make Feng Wu a lord? What do you think?”","Deep down, Empress Dugu was displeased. “She’s already a princess... Does becoming a lord really suit her? Your Majesty, how about you give her something she can actually use?”","Emperor Wu asked, “Such as?”","To stop Feng Wu from getting another title, Empress Dugu became quite generous. “I heard that Feng Yanfeng tried to expel Feng Wu from the clan. Although he didn’t get to do it in the end, that still gives us a hint.”","“Where will Feng Wu live if she really is kicked out of her clan?” asked Emperor Wu.","“If I remember correctly, isn’t there a manor on Dongyuan Street? Your Majesty, how about you give the place to her?”","Empress Dugu was in fact very reluctant.","She had had her eye on that manor on Dongyuan Street for a while, and had wanted to give it to her nephew. Compared with promoting Feng Wu, however, the manor was nothing.","“The manor has been deserted for many years, and it used to be General Weiwu’s residence. I certainly can give it to her...”","In fact, although Feng Wu had indirectly saved the empress dowager, Emperor Wu still didn’t like Feng Wu very much.","That was because he deemed Feng Wu to be the same type of person as Jun Linyuan, who was aloof, arrogant, and had no consideration for other people.","The chief steward went to deliver the imperial edict himself.","Because Feng Wu was a member of the Feng clan, the imperial edict naturally was taken to the Feng family’s tent.","“Father, there’s an imperial edict for Feng Wu.” Feng Yiran immediately told Feng Yanfeng the news.","Feng Yanfeng struggled out of bed.","The chief steward just happened to walk in, and Feng Yanfeng saluted him.","As the general steward for the entire imperial palace, the chief steward was a respected figure. Wherever he went, people would try to fawn on him."]},{"number":1486,"title":"Chapter 1486","paragraphs":["Even Feng Yanfeng had to greet the chief steward with a bow.","The chief steward was a fair, chubby elderly man with a Buddha-like smile, which made him seem very approachable.","He smiled at Feng Yanfeng and said, “Master Feng, you’re too polite. Now, I have an imperial edict for Miss Feng Wu. Please bring her out here to hear it.”","Feng Yanfeng paled when he heard this.","Because of Feng Wu, he lost his job yesterday. He felt he had nothing left now.","That just showed how much His Majesty didn’t like Feng Wu!","And now, there was an imperial edict, and it was directed at Feng Wu alone. It didn’t take a genius to figure out how terrifying the imperial edict would be.","It couldn’t possibly be anything good.","At that thought, Feng Yanfeng finally summoned up his courage and smiled bitterly. “Sir, you’ve come a little too late. I’m terribly sorry...”","“Really?” The chief steward raised his eyebrows.","Feng Yanfeng said, “Starting from yesterday, Feng Wu has been expelled from the Feng clan. That is to say, after that, whatever she does has nothing to do with the clan.”","Lady Wang, Feng Yiran, and the others immediately chimed in, “That’s right!”","They decided that they were done paying for Feng Wu’s mistakes!","The chief steward frowned a little. “Do you mean it...”","Feng Yanfeng nodded repeatedly. “Yes! Yes, of course! Feng Wu has nothing to do with the Feng clan now, so any of her punishments or rewards will have nothing to do with our clan!”","“Well...” The chief steward heaved a long sigh. “Master Feng, are you sure? I hope you won’t regret it.”","Feng Yanfeng smiled bitterly. “Of course, I won’t. The decision was made yesterday.”","The chief steward nodded. “Even if that’s the case, because this is an imperial edict, the edict table has to sit here, and Miss Feng has to come out here as well.”","Feng Yanfeng had no problem with that.","Even if the imperial edict was about Feng Wu’s punishment, his family wasn’t going to be involved anymore.","Feng Wu was meditating, when she was disturbed by the noise outside.","Granny Gong told her about the imperial edict.","Feng Wu frowned a little. “Can’t he come here?”","Granny Gong smiled. “He can, according to regular practice. However, the chief steward insisted on having the edict table set there; I’m sure he has a reason for it.”","She then added, “The chief steward really likes His Royal Highness, so don’t worry. He won’t trick us. I’m sure he knows what he’s doing.”","Feng Wu shrugged. “Let’s go and have a look, then.”","Deep down, she already had a faint idea. After all, she had saved the empress dowager, so the emperor was bound to give her some reward, even if it was just for show.","Unfortunately, only a handful of people knew that she had saved the empress dowager, and that didn’t include Feng Yanfeng and his people.","In the Feng clan’s camp.","As soon as Feng Wu arrived, Feng Yanfeng’s family stared at her with eyes filled with hatred!","It was especially the case with Feng Liu, and she didn’t try to hide her hatred toward Feng Wu.","Feng Wu shrugged.","“Feng Wu! How dare you come here!” Feng Liu growled in Feng Wu’s ear.","Feng Wu asked casually, “Why wouldn’t I dare?”","Feng Liu asked, “Did you know that my father lost his job because of you?!”","Feng Wu smirked. “Why don’t you ask your father how he got that minister job in the first place?”","She had pulled some strings, and Feng Yanfeng still owed her 100,000 spiritual stones for it.","Feng Liu said, “Heh, are you suggesting it had something to do with you?”"]},{"number":1487,"title":"Chapter 1487","paragraphs":["Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","Feng Wu asked, “What if I told you that I was the one who got him that job?”","Feng Liu said, “Heh, that’s the funniest joke I’ve ever heard.”","Feng Wu shrugged. “Laugh all you want, then.”","She turned to look at Feng Yanfeng as she spoke. “Other people may not know, but Uncle, surely you should know better. Do you need me to take out that IOU?”","“You —” Furious, Feng Yanfeng went pale!","He didn’t expect the girl to be so difficult!","He then turned to the chief steward. “Since Feng Wu is already here, I believe we can hear the imperial edict now.”","Just get it over with and let Feng Wu be on her way, thought Feng Yanfeng angrily.","However, the chief steward reminded him in an unhurried tone, “Master Feng, did you say that Feng Wu’s name has been removed from your clan?”","“Yes!”","“No!”","Feng Yanfeng and Feng Wu gave different answers.","“Is she still a member of the clan or not?” the chief steward asked.","“No!” said Feng Yanfeng.","“Yes!” said Feng Wu.","Once again, Feng Yanfeng and Feng Wu didn’t agree with each other.","The chief steward rubbed his forehead. “An individual’s fate is connected to their clan. Who should I read this imperial edict to? The clan or Feng Wu? I can’t read it if you keep disagreeing with each other!”","“Read it to her! Read it to her!” Feng Yanfeng answered agitatedly. “Her name may still be listed in our clan, but she really can’t stay here anymore. Be it reward or punishment, Feng Wu can have it all.”","“Are you sure?” The chief steward narrowed his eyes.","“Yes! I’m positive!” Feng Yanfeng said excitedly. “The imperial edict belongs to Feng Wu herself. She can have all the rewards or punishments. We don’t want her good fortune, and we don’t want to be incriminated by her either!”","Lady Wang nodded. “That’s right! We don’t want her rewards or to be incriminated!”","The rest of them all nodded.","Meanwhile —","Because everyone was standing in front of the Feng clan’s tent, they soon attracted a lot of attention.","The Zuo, Dugu, Feng, and Xuan families, and many others, had gathered around as onlookers.","Lady Wang told Mrs Zuo and the others, “Please be our witnesses. Feng Wu has nothing to do with the Feng clan, and she will soon be removed from this clan. She’ll take full responsibility for her own mistakes, and we won’t take credit for her good fortune!”","“Nicely said, Lady Wang!”","“Master Feng was so miserable yesterday. If he’s incriminated again, he may lose his life.”","“This Feng Wu brings trouble to everyone around her.”","“The Feng family has made a wise decision.”","–","After much discussion, the chief steward finally started reading the imperial edict.","Feng Yanfeng was dumbfounded as soon as he heard the first sentence.","“In reward for her efforts in saving the empress dowager, Feng Wu will receive: a pair of jade ruyi ornaments, a golden room, a manor situated at No.2, Third Alley, Dongyuan Avenue, and...”","Feng Wu was rewarded for saving the empress dowager?!!!","Many people felt their heads spin when they heard it. They didn’t know what to think.","Didn’t the rumor yesterday say that Feng Wu didn’t go to treat the empress dowager, which was why Feng Yanfeng was fired?","It now seemed that —","That wasn’t the case.","Feng Yanfeng’s eyes almost popped out when he heard the manor address.","That manor was General Weiwu’s former residence. The location was wonderful, and the place was huge! It was the envy of many people!"]},{"number":1488,"title":"Chapter 1488","paragraphs":["Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","Even Master Zuo and Master Dugu were surprised, to say nothing of Feng Yanfeng!","It was especially the case with Master Dugu, who had had his eye on the manor for a long while, but Feng Wu somehow ended up taking it.","The chief steward still hadn’t finished reading the imperial edict.","The emperor bestowed a traveling tent on Feng Wu.","And a Ferghana horse.","And a divine bow.","And...","All of them were great honors and could be very useful when they arrived at the Senal Grassland!","They were all status symbols.","The Feng clan was surrounded by a lot of people, and everyone looked at Feng Wu in disbelief.","Before today, they had all been criticizing Feng Wu and found her annoying because she had lost His Majesty’s favor, but it had only taken Feng Wu a day to get her status back!","Feng Yanfeng was so distressed that he thought his eyes were going to fall out.","He looked at Feng Wu in disbelief before turning to the chief steward with an expectant look.","If His Majesty had rewarded Feng Wu so generously, did that mean that he could get his job back?","However, Feng Yanfeng waited and waited, but didn’t hear the words he was hoping for even when the chief steward finished reading the edict. He panicked.","“Sir —” Feng Yanfeng stopped the chief steward, who had rolled up the imperial edict and was ready to leave, and asked, “Is that all?”","“Not really.” Seeing the eager look in Feng Yanfeng’s eyes, the chief steward chuckled. “It’s just that... Since you yourself said that Feng Wu can have all the rewards and punishments to herself, there’s no need to read the part that was meant for you.”","“What?”","Feng Yanfeng paled and was dumbfounded.","For some reason, the chief steward unfolded a section of the imperial edict and let Feng Yanfeng took a peek before putting it away.","Feng Yanfeng was speechless.","He really was going to faint!","There was indeed a reward for him in the imperial edict. Although it wasn’t a ministerial position, it was good enough. It was a post as a second-ranked commanding officer at a border city. It was a job that would make a lot of people envious...","Feng Yanfeng thought he was going to lose his mind!","The chief steward even reminded Feng Yanfeng on his way out, “I’m going to put this second-ranked post for you on hold, Master Feng.”","Feng Yanfeng was still feeling dumbfounded even when the chief steward left.","A second-ranked official located in a border city? That position was second only to Northern Feng General!","The Junwu Empire valued martial virtues more than civil ones, so that job was almost as good as the minister of the Ministry of Official Personnel.","However —","He had just lost such a wonderful opportunity!","Feng Yanfeng had never regretted a decision so much.","The chief steward didn’t lower his voice when he said that, so everyone heard it. Right now, they were all giving Feng Yanfeng strange looks.","They could still hear Feng Yanfeng in their ears, declaring that Feng Wu had nothing to do with the Feng clan, and that she could have all the rewards and punishments to herself!","That was so frustrating.","Feng Wu couldn’t care less about Feng Yanfeng’s feelings, and she left after taking the imperial edict.","Feng Yanfeng wanted to say something to Feng Wu, but he hesitated.","The chief steward couldn’t be any more obvious with his hint. If Feng Yanfeng still wanted that job, Feng Wu was the key.","While Feng Yanfeng’s family was feeling distressed, Feng Wu felt very relieved.","Perhaps Feng Wu’s medicine was too potent, but the empress dowager had already woken up."]},{"number":1489,"title":"Chapter 1489","paragraphs":["Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","If it were up to Emperor Wu, he would send the empress dowager back already. After all, it would take at least another ten days for them to reach the Senal Grassland, and the empress dowager wouldn’t be able to handle the journey.","However, the empress dowager wouldn’t listen.","She insisted that she had to go to the Senal Grassland!","When the old lady acted out, there was nothing Emperor Wu could do.","With no other choice, Emperor Wu had to summon Feng Wu for a discussion.","Feng Wu frowned. “The best option right now is for Her Majesty to go back to the palace and get some rest. This is a very big deal.”","Emperor Wu rubbed his forehead. “That’s what I thought, but the empress dowager is bent on going to the grassland, and I can’t stop her.”","Feng Wu gave Emperor Wu a resigned look. Of course he could stop her. He just couldn’t bring himself to do so.","“If Her Majesty insists on going to the Senal Grassland, then we’ll have to worry about a lot of things for the next few days. There are so many aspects we’ll have to be cautious about, both in relation to her diet and her daily life,” Feng Wu said with a frown.","Emperor Wu gave a wave of his hand. “In that case, why don’t you look after Her Majesty yourself?”","Feng Wu looked at Emperor Wu in resignation. “Your Majesty, are you sure that Her Majesty won’t flare up when she sees me, and rip open all her stitches?”","Emperor Wu said, “Well...”","Feng Wu said, “But I’ll write down some dos and don’ts so that Granny Lan can pay more attention when she’s looking after Her Majesty. Along with my specially made pills, the wound will close up in three days. Everything should be fine then.”","“That’s great. Glad to hear that.” Emperor Wu was elated.","The empress dowager walked out from the inner room, supported by Granny Lan.","Right now, a white bandage was wrapped around the empress dowager’s head and she had a very pale face. However, she couldn’t look any more arrogant.","As soon as she came out and spotted Feng Wu, she frowned.","This time, she simply ignored Feng Wu and walked haughtily past her.","“Your Majesty!” The empress dowager greeted Emperor Wu.","Emperor Wu immediately went up to her. “Mother —”","“Master Chu was the one who had saved me from danger, wasn’t he?” The empress dowager greeted Master Chu in a benevolent manner.","Master Chu glanced at Feng Wu. He knew that Feng Wu was the only reason that the old lady was able to sit here safely. She would have been dead by now.","At that thought, Master Chu stepped out and said, “Your Majesty, actually, the chief doctor who helped you was —”","“Ahem —”","At that critical moment, Emperor Wu cleared his throat and cut Master Chu off.","Master Chu gave Emperor Wu a confused look.","Emperor Wu stared at him.","Master Chu immediately took the hint.","However, he did feel guilty for taking the credit.","Hence, Master Chu looked back at Feng Wu.","Feng Wu also nodded at Master Chu.","That was to say, she agreed as well.","Only then did Master Chu smile bitterly and said, “Actually, I did make a small contribution this time, but it was mostly thanks to Your Majesty’s own strength and God’s blessing.”","The empress dowager was happy to hear that, and she smiled. “I know I’m blessed, but your treatment was still necessary. I should thank you for that.”","She then glanced at Feng Wu before turning back to Master Chu. “I value you because unlike someone else, you don’t think that I can’t live without you.”","Everyone else around them fell silent.","They all lowered their heads and didn’t dare to look the empress dowager in the eye."]},{"number":1490,"title":"Chapter 1490","paragraphs":["As a matter of fact, the empress dowager really needed Feng Wu. Had it not been for her, the old lady would be in her grave now.","Lady Northern Feng was also there, and she ranted the most in her head. However —","Since His Majesty had spoken, there was nothing she could say.","The empress dowager threw a proud glance at Feng Wu and told Master Chu, “I also like you because you don’t try to take credit for other people’s work, and you’re not proud either, unlike someone. They act as if they call the shots around here when they didn’t do a thing. Heh —”","Master Chu looked embarrassed.","He wondered if the empress dowager had said that on purpose, because that description sounded just like him.","Master Chu felt like crying, because he was just an honest man.","“Your Majesty, we were only able to save you because —”","“Ahem —”","Several people cleared their throats.","Even Feng Wu shook her head at Master Chu.","Master Chu was speechless.","“Her Majesty’s wound has yet to close,” she reminded him in an indifferent tone.","She meant that if Her Majesty knew who her real lifesaver was, she might be so angry that her wound would burst open...","Master Chu understood that, so he had no choice but to take the credit.","The empress dowager glanced at Feng Wu and snorted. “What do you know about my wound? As if you were the one who treated me.”","Feng Wu cleared her throat again.","The empress dowager frowned. “Why are you coughing all the time? Are you sick? If you infect Junjun with your coughing, I’ll kill you!”","Feng Wu was speechless.","She wanted to explain, when the empress dowager waved her off. “That’s enough. I don’t want to listen to you, nor do I want to see your face. Go away now!”","The empress dowager was very blunt.","Empress Dugu, Jun Wuxia, and their lot were very happy to hear it, and they were thrilled to hear Feng Wu’s predicament.","The Northern Feng General, on the other hand, wanted to defend Feng Wu against the injustice.","Feng Wu was the one who had saved the empress dowager, but not only didn’t she get a thank you, she was scolded and taunted. How frustrating.","To Lady Northern Feng’s relief, after what the girl was put through, she remained unperturbed and level-headed. What a magnanimous young lady.","Feng Wu didn’t plan to stick around to be insulted, so she excused herself.","The winter hunt was supposed to be canceled, but since the empress dowager insisted on going, the journey resumed.","“We’re still going?”","All the clan heads and their families were confused; they couldn’t understand why the empress dowager still wanted to go to the Senal Grassland in her current condition.","Exactly what was so special about the place that the empress dowager just had to go there?","Granny Lan had asked the empress dowager that question before, but she wouldn’t tell even Granny Lan.","For the next part of the journey, Feng Wu still stayed with Jun Linyuan as his maid.","Jun Linyuan was a very fussy guy.","He was extremely picky about his food.","Ever since Feng Wu made the fish-flavored shredded pork with rice the other day, he had to eat what Feng Wu cooked for every single meal.","Luckily, Feng Wu was already a good cook, so she was able to cook Jun Linyuan different delicious dishes every time.","There were so many ingredients she could find in the mountains that she didn’t have to cook the same dish for nearly two weeks.","One night, they camped on the bank of Yuexi Lake.","As soon as they got out of their carriage, Jun Linyuan saw the lake, and he told Feng Wu that he wanted roast fish."]},{"number":1491,"title":"Chapter 1491","paragraphs":["“Roast fish?” Feng Wu stared at Jun Linyuan. “My dear crown prince, we’re out in the wilderness. Can you settle for something simpler?”","Feng Wu still had to cultivate and she was very busy.","But of course, Jun Linyuan wouldn’t let her go.","He gave Feng Wu a proud look, crossed his hands behind his back, and marched off.","What choice did Feng Wu have? She had to follow him in frustration.","Luckily, it was the 15th day already.","Feng Wu thought to herself, When the 18 days are over and this mission is completed, I won’t be his maid anymore.","The lake was filled with moon fish that would sell at a good price in the market since they were hard to catch and very rare.","But for Feng Wu and Jun Linyuan, catching moon fish was a piece of cake.","They didn’t even need any bait. Feng Wu just sat by the water and washed her hands. She then gathered her spiritual essence into a thread and lifted a fish out of the water by pulling the thread.","The moon fish was about half a meter long and a silver white color. In the moonlight, it almost looked translucent.","“Let’s go.” Feng Wu put a straw rope she had braided through the fish’s mouth, took Jun Linyuan’s hand, and tried to leave, because she wanted to get this over with as soon as possible.","She had obtained some insight while they were traveling today, and she was looking for an opportunity to sit down and think it over.","However, it was a beautiful night, and the crown prince obviously didn’t plan to let Feng Wu go that easily.","“Xuan Yi and Feng Xun will be here tonight,” Jun Linyuan said casually as he lay down on the snow-white rock and rested his head on his crossed hands.","“They weren’t with us before?” Feng Wu was surprised.","The crown prince glanced at Feng Wu before he turned his gaze to the sky in silence.","“That’s right.” Feng Wu rested her chin on her hands. “Xuan Yi aside, if Feng Xun were here, he would definitely have come find us. But he didn’t, not once.”","“Yes.” The crown prince nodded.","“If they’re going to be here tonight, one fish indeed won’t be enough. I remember that they can both eat a lot.”","Feng Wu caught a few more fish as she spoke.","With her storage space, she could simply throw the moon fish inside.","“By the way, we won’t see any moon fish again on our way to the Senal Grassland, will we?” This was Feng Wu’s first time going to the Senal Grassland, so she didn’t know the terrain well.","Jun Linyuan said casually, “A fish is probably worth a cow there.”","What?!","Feng Wu’s eyes lit up and she looked at Jun Linyuan in excitement. “Really? Are you sure?”","Jun Linyuan grunted.","“That’s so profitable! If that’s the case, we shouldn’t let these fish go to waste!”","One fish for a cow? Just imagine that! Feng Wu was getting excited just thinking about it.","“And a cow from the Senal Grassland is worth a low-grade spiritual stone in the mining area in the central plains.” Jun Linyuan made another striking statement.","Feng Wu: !!!","Although she had a spiritual stone lode, all the spiritual stones beneath the Fang manor, low- and top-grade alike, went toward the formation.","Feng Wu still had Chaoge, Qiuling, Uncle Qiu, and Xiaoqi to consider, and they all needed spiritual stones for their cultivation. So —","“These are all spiritual stones. No, I can’t just watch them slip away.”","Her beautiful master was in her ring space; she would never put the fish in there."]},{"number":1492,"title":"Chapter 1492","paragraphs":["But aside from that, she still had another storage ring which Jun Linyuan had given to her before, and it was where she could keep the fish.","Feng Wu crouched down and opened up the ring, and soon, moon fish started pouring into it.","One, two, three... 100, 1000... In the end, Feng Wu lost count of how many there were. In short, there were a lot.","Feng Wu exclaimed in surprise all of a sudden.","“What’s that?” Feng Wu snatched a moon fish out of the water and examined it curiously.","There was something different about this moon fish, which was covered in a faint glow. She could detect a subtle hint of spiritual essence on it.","Somehow, the fish struck her as odd, but she couldn’t exactly pinpoint why.","She was still trying to figure it out, when Jun Linyuan walked over and crouched down next to her.","His long, slender fingers reached over and took the chubby moon fish.","“Hm?”","The crown prince frowned a little.","“Do you know what’s with this fish?” Feng Wu looked curiously at Jun Linyuan.","“Yes.” He swiped his fingers across the scales of the fish and a streak of blue light floated up.","“Is that spiritual essence? This moon fish contains spiritual essence?” Feng Wu was confused.","“The moon fish doesn’t have it, but if they swallow something which contains spiritual essence, they’ll have it in them,” Jun Linyuan said.","“If they’ve ingested spiritual essence by mistake... Does that mean that there’s something filled with spiritual essence in the lake?” Feng Wu’s eyes lit up!","Jun Linyuan didn’t comment.","“Shall I go down there and have a look?” Feng Wu asked him.","Before she knew it, Feng Wu had started to get into this habit.","“Let someone else go,” Jun Linyuan said indifferently.","Was there anyone else around?","Feng Wu was still feeling bewildered, when two figures approached them.","“Boss Jun! We finally caught up with you! I was so worried!”","Feng Xun jumped at them and tried to hug Jun Linyuan, but of course, the crown prince wouldn’t let him.","Hence, Feng Xun turned to Feng Wu instead. “My dear sister —”","However, Jun Linyuan picked him up by the back of his collar before he could reach her.","“Waaaa! Boss Jun! Boss Jun! Let me down! Let me down!” Feng Xun kicked around in the air.","But —","Soon, Feng Wu heard the sound of something falling into the water.","Turning around, she saw that poor Feng Xun had just been thrown into the lake.","Feng Xun was about to go ashore, when Jun Linyuan stopped him.","He said, “Since you’re already there, dive deeper.”","Feng Xun was confused.","Feng Wu immediately explained to him about the moon fish.","Treasure hunting had always excited Feng Xun, so he dove in head first and quickly swam around in the lake.","Feng Wu was confident that Feng Xun would be able to find the source right away, but —","To her surprise, after coming back up for air three more times, Feng Xun still couldn’t find anything.","“Let me have a look.” Xuan Yi jumped in.","Feng Xun and Xuan Yi each covered half the lake after splitting it into quarters.","That way, they could do a grid search and would soon find their answer."]},{"number":1493,"title":"Chapter 1493","paragraphs":["As expected —","In less than 15 minutes, they heard from Xuan Yi.","He handed Feng Wu a broken stone when he came back up. “I think you know what this is.”","Feng Xun craned his neck. “Xuan Yi, are you kidding me? I found quite a few of these shabby stones on my side as well, but I didn’t think much of them.”","Xuan Yi didn’t reply and only watched Feng Wu quietly.","Taking the broken stone, it only took Feng Wu one look to realize what it was.","“This is a spiritual stone used in a formation. It’s just that it’s drained of spiritual essence, so it looks the same as any common stone.”","Feng Wu rose to her feet and studied the lake with a cold look in her eyes.","She didn’t expect to find a formation in the lake.","Judging from what was left of the spiritual stones, this was no ordinary formation.","“I’ll go have a look.”","Feng Wu jumped into the lake after saying those words.","She swam as nimbly as a fish in the lake, and before long, she arrived at the spot where Xuan Yi found the stone.","Grotesque stones and red coral of various shapes covered the bottom of the lake.","Feng Wu was very level-headed for her age. “We’ll search the area around this spot. We’re looking for some spiritual stones. I need a baseline spiritual stone to deduce the type of formation used here.”","Feng Xun and Xuan Yi were both influential young lords who usually didn’t take orders from anyone but Jun Linyuan.","But before they knew it, they had started to believe everything Feng Wu said.","With their help, Feng Wu soon discovered the pattern of the spiritual stones, and with that pattern, she was able to deduce the type of formation used.","“It’s a Level 5 formation. That’s incredible.” Feng Wu started looking for the core of the formation as she spoke.","Because she had found the general direction, the search wasn’t difficult at all.","Feng Wu was in the front with Feng Xun on her left and Xuan Yi on her right.","The three of them formed a triangle.","A few times, Feng Xun thought that they hit a dead end when there was nothing in front of them but a wall of red coral.","However, Feng Wu could somehow always lead them through it at an impossible angle.","No wonder this secret had been hidden under the lake for so many years; if one didn’t understand formations, they wouldn’t know where to look.","“We’re here.”","They were passing under the archway of a bridge when Feng Wu said that.","The scene they saw was quite impressive once they were on the other side of the archway.","They thought they had arrived in hell.","They were looking at a treasure ship.","After years at the bottom of the lake, the ship was very dilapidated.","There was some cargo on the ship, but there were more dead bodies.","Some lay face down, some on their backs, and some had been impaled on poles. It was a horrible scene.","“It’s a shipwreck!” Feng Xun was the first to rush toward it.","However —","“Stop!” Feng Wu stopped him.","Luckily, Feng Xun always listened to Feng Wu, so he stopped at her command.","He turned around and looked at Feng Wu in bewilderment.","Feng Wu said grumpily, “Did you think that shipwrecks wouldn’t have traps on them?”","She then threw a stone at the ship.","It hit the ship, and suddenly —","Squeak —","There was a terrifying sound.","Before Feng Xun realized what was going on, Feng Wu was already dragging him back."]},{"number":1494,"title":"Chapter 1494","paragraphs":["They had only just hidden behind a wall, when they heard the sound of shooting arrows!","The water should have hindered the arrows’ movements, but it seemed that these arrows were able to overcome that resistance, and the impact they made resembled an explosion. It was terrifying.","Whoosh —","They just kept coming!","Luckily, Feng Wu reacted in time. Otherwise, Feng Xun would have been injured, rushing out like that.","Still shaken from the lingering fear, he looked at Feng Wu and heaved a sigh of relief. “That was close. If you didn’t drag me away, I would have turned into a hedgehog by now.”","Feng Wu chuckled. “No, you won’t. You would just have a few painful injuries. Nevertheless, those are some very malicious arrows.”","They only boarded the shipwreck after it was all over.","“Hey, why are most of these dead people from the grassland?” Feng Xun examined the corpses curiously.","The flesh had rotted away years ago, but they could still see that the dead people were descendants of the grassland from the bones.","Xuan Yi said grumpily, “Grassland or not, it has nothing to do with us. Let’s go find the thing.”","Feng Xun agreed.","Compared with this discovery, they preferred the thrill of the treasure hunt.","“I think someone beat us to it and took everything valuable.” Feng Xun and Xuan Yi looked around and spoke in a sorry tone after they came back out.","“Is there nothing left?” Feng Wu frowned.","“No.” Feng Xun sounded resigned.","He had expected to find some treasure after they finally disabled the formation, but the ship had only turned out to be a shell.","Feng Wu scratched her head. “That shouldn’t be the case. Did someone get here before us?”","She wouldn’t believe it, so she went in to search herself.","Feng Xun followed her and discouraged her as she looked around.","“I told you already, there’s nothing left. But you won’t believe me and just have to look for yourself. You were so excited, but you’re going to be disappointed.”","The cabin was utterly empty, as though someone had taken absolutely everything.","While Feng Xun was sighing and moaning, Feng Wu was tapping on the walls with her fingers.","Feng Xun looked at Feng Wu in resignation.","He had told her that there was nothing here. Did she think she could find something by tapping?","But to Feng Xun’s surprise —","After three long and five short taps —","Crackle —","There was the sound of cracking wood.","Feng Xun’s eyes widened as he watched a medium-sized sealed box fall out of the wall.","“That —”","He stared at Feng Wu in bewilderment. “You — how did you find it?”","Feng Wu said innocently, “I just tapped randomly and it fell out.”","Feng Xun: !!!","It had obviously been hidden so well that the first group of people who got here hadn’t found this hidden treasure box.","“What’s inside?” Feng Xun was curious.","Feng Wu said, “We’ll have a look once we’re up on shore, since we have to leave now.”","Feng Xun was confused. “Why?”","Feng Wu said, “Because the self-destruct mode was activated after this box fell out. This treasure ship will explode in less than a minute.”"]},{"number":1495,"title":"Chapter 1495","paragraphs":["“What?” Hearing that, Feng Xun grabbed Feng Wu and dashed off. “Let’s go! This is a formidable treasure ship, and we don’t know how much of an impact the explosion will have. Just move as fast as you can!”","Feng Wu, Feng Xun, and Xuan Yi quickly left the bottom of the lake.","The three of them had just climbed out of the lake when —","Whoosh —","A formidable shockwave struck them from behind, and it was terrifying!","Waves shot up and exploded in the air!","Thump!","The impact threw the three of them onto the bank.","Luckily, Jun Linyuan had activated a protective skill before they hit the ground.","Feng Wu opened her eyes to find herself already in Jun Linyuan’s arms.","That terrifying shockwave had been extinguished by Jun Linyuan’s strike.","Feng Wu was speechless.","Even so, the water level was still rising quickly.","“Water is going to get up here soon. Let’s go.” Still carrying Feng Wu in his arms, Jun Linyuan ran back to the campsite.","Feng Xun and Xuan Yi followed him.","It was a long distance for normal people, but to Jun Linyuan, it was only a matter of a few leaps.","Jun Linyuan told Feng when they got back, “A flood is coming. Let’s move up the hill.”","Everyone was dumbfounded.","Why was there suddenly a flood?","No one would believe it if it had come from someone else, but since it was Jun Linyuan who said it, no one questioned it.","The carriages started moving again and were soon halfway up the hill.","Just then, the water from the lake arrived.","Everyone looked at Jun Linyuan in amazement.","That was so impressive! How incredible!","Jun Linyuan ignored them all. Instead, he carried Feng Wu back to their carriage.","Feng Wu was still holding the box she found at the bottom of the lake, and she only opened it happily when they got back to the carriage.","Feng Xun and Xuan Yi gathered around and watched curiously.","“What’s inside? I’m so curious,” Feng Xun said expectantly.","Feng Wu said, “It was so well-hidden. I think it’s some sort of top secret.”","The box was made from hard iron from the bottom of the ocean with a password consisting of formation codes. If one tried to pry it open by force, the box would destroy itself.","That was to say, no one would know what was inside.","Luckily —","Feng Wu knew formations, and less than a handful of people in the entire Junwu Empire were better at her in them.","With some deduction, she was able to solve the password in less than five minutes.","With a click —","The wondrous box opened.","The first item —","It was a messenger bottle.","Feng Xun didn’t open it right away, and only looked at Feng Wu.","Feng Wu was amused, and she chuckled. “It’s okay. There’s no trap. Just open it.”","Feng Xun only opened the bottle after hearing Feng Wu’s confirmation.","“Hey, what’s this?” Feng Xun took a light yellow parchment out of the bottle.","On it was an illustration of mountains and rivers with notes written in a foreign language.","“Hey, isn’t that the language of Senal? And isn’t that Sheep Grass Mountain?” Feng Xun cried out.","Feng Wu looked at him in confusion."]},{"number":1496,"title":"Chapter 1496","paragraphs":["Feng Xun couldn’t hold back his excitement. “That’s a treasure map, isn’t it?! Am I right?!”","Feng Xun showed it to Jun Linyuan as he spoke.","Jun Linyuan glanced at him and gave a slight nod.","That immediately settled Feng Xun’s mind, and he said excitedly, “So, that’s a real treasure map?!”","He looked at Jun Linyuan with twinkling eyes as he spoke.","Jun Linyuan nodded again. “And the treasure belongs to the royal family of Senal.”","“Holy crap!” Feng Xun was so excited that he almost jumped up.","The grassland was a region, and the Senal Grassland was the most wealthy of them all. If they could obtain the treasure of the royal family, that would be —","Even Feng Wu was thrilled, let alone Feng Xun. This would be so much more profitable than selling moon fish.","“And? Is there more?” Feng Xun asked anxiously.","Feng Wu took a second object out of the box.","It was a booklet. Technically, it was a notebook.","Feng Wu opened it and saw that it was the record of a solitary trip.","“This booklet belonged to someone called Molmo, who wrote all this.” After turning a few pages, Feng Wu saw that it was all written in the Senal language, which gave her a headache, so she gave the booklet back to Feng Xun.","“Molmo?” Feng Xun was utterly surprised. “I’ve heard that name before. If I remember correctly, he was the previous crown prince, and should have become the king!”","“Really?” Feng Wu raised an eyebrow. “Have we discovered some sort of secret of the royal family? That’s okay. We’ll have a closer look later.”","Putting the booklet aside, Feng Wu took out the third object.","It was a jade slip.","Feng Wu cried out softly when she injected her spiritual essence into the jade slip.","Immediately, all eyes were on her.","Feng Wu said, “It contains a cultivation technique known as Nirvana of Omen.”","Feng Xun was surprised. “Nirvana of Omen? Are you sure? Is it really Nirvana of Omen?!!!”","Feng Wu looked at Feng Xun in bewilderment. “Have you heard of this technique before?”","Feng Xun said, “Of course I have. That’s the most superior cultivation technique in the grassland, and only the royal family can access it. Moreover, it’s only for the most promising members.","“If I remember correctly, after this slip was lost, so was the cultivation technique.”","Feng Xun then smacked his own thigh. “Only those with the grassland bloodline can learn it, so it doesn’t mean much to us. But don’t worry. With it, we’ll be able to get a lot of things. Hahaha —”","Feng Xun was so excited that he prompted Feng Wu, “And? Is there more? Take it out, quickly.”","Feng Wu waved him off grumpily. “There’s also a dagger, and it looks a bit old.”","“Oh god! That has to be Molmo’s personal dagger! It has to be!","“Little Feng Wu! You’re awesome!” Feng Xun patted her arm in excitement. “You know what? The objects in the box may not seem like much, but if we make good use of them, we can turn the Senal Grassland upside down if we want! You’re our lucky star!”","Feng Xun patted Feng Wu on the back."]},{"number":1497,"title":"Chapter 1497","paragraphs":["He only realized that he had patted her too hard when Jun Linyuan threw a dirty look at him.","“Hahaha, Xiao Wu, are you alright?”","Seeing the way the girl stumbled under his patting, Feng Xun scratched his head, looking ashamed.","Feng Wu waved at him. “That’s alright. You guys enjoy your chat. I’m hungry. I’ll go roast you some fish.”","Those moon fish couldn’t go to waste.","They were at the best location halfway up the hill.","Feng Wu chose the best spot and had Feng Xun set up the grill for her.","Moon fish didn’t have a single scale and were very easy to clean.","After removing the entrails and rinsing the fish, Feng Wu made three cuts on each fish, used some ginger to get rid of the fishy smell, and seasoned them with a special concoction she made herself.","Meanwhile, she also stuffed the fish with spices that she had gathered during the trip.","Once everyone was given their tasks, Feng Xun started setting up the grill while Xuan Yi went to find some firewood.","Because they were out in the open, the other people were able to see everything they were doing.","Families like the Zuo family were especially shocked when they saw the way Feng Wu ordered Feng Xun and Xuan Yi around.","How was that even possible? What magic did Feng Wu have? Why did influential young lords like Feng Xun and Xuan Yi get along so well with her?","The harmonious scene stung many eyes and broke many hearts.","Seeing that the moon fish was properly seasoned, Feng Wu came out of the tent and took over the job.","“I’m starving —” Feng Xun patted his stomach and looked resentful.","Feng Wu patted his head the way one would pacify a puppy dog. “There, there. It’s almost done. Just another 15 minutes.”","“Alright. I’ll just sit here and wait.” Feng Xun sat down cross-legged and rested his chin on his hands. The way he blinked looked quite adorable.","That was how Feng Wu and Feng Xun interacted with each other on a daily basis, but to other people, that was the most incredible thing!","“Why is Young Lord Feng so obedient with Feng Wu?”","“And Young Lord Xuan as well.”","“Feng Wu is just a bed-warming maid. How does she do it?!”","–","The entourage this time was quite sizable, and there were high-ranking officials, first-ranked dames, princes and princesses of all sorts...","They were all arrogant people that used to look down on Feng Wu. But now, they suddenly realized that Feng Wu was so important to Feng Xun and Xuan Yi, which utterly confused them.","They were so overwhelmed with jealousy that they had no time to analyze it. All they knew were their jealous feelings!","Feng Wu didn’t know what the others were thinking, but even if she did, she wouldn’t care at all.","She mulled over her cultivation technique as she busied herself with roasting the fish.","She had mastered the three stances her beautiful master taught her, but she still didn’t know where she could find the fourth one.","Her master had disappeared so suddenly that she probably had to wait until he woke up to learn the fourth stance.","Feng Wu patted her own head in frustration.","She was only on the 6th mission of the 12 Trials of Love, and the 6th one had been extended... She couldn’t imagine how torturous the future ones would be.","As she skillfully coated the roast fish with sauce, she racked her brain and tried to predict what might happen next and what precautions she would have to take."]},{"number":1498,"title":"Chapter 1498","paragraphs":["Although she was absent-minded, the fish turned out excellent.","The empress dowager, Emperor Wu, and Jun Linyuan were the core of the convoy, so the three of them weren’t so far apart.","As soon as the fish was ready, the aroma filled the air. The empress dowager just happened to be downwind, so the intense scent drifted her way.","“That smells so nice!”","Feng Xun was so intrigued by the aroma that his mouth watered.","Feng Wu was already an excellent cook to begin with. The moon fish was naturally tasty, and Feng Wu had used a tiny formation to gather spiritual essence when she was cooking. As a result —","“Xiao Wu, Xiao Wu —” Feng Xun blinked at Feng Wu. His big sparkling eyes could melt one’s heart.","Feng Wu only gave him a grumpy look and rubbed his head. “Wait.”","“Alright...” Feng Xun looked as pitiful as a puppy dog.","Just then, he sensed a cold glance aimed at him!","A chill ran up his legs, and his back stiffened.","Turning his head involuntarily, he saw —","The crown prince was glaring at him with eyes so cold that they could freeze the air!","Ssss —","Feng Xun drew in his breath.","He detected jealousy... Boss Jun was jealous!","At that thought, Feng Xun immediately moved away.","Feng Wu had just torn off a palm-sized piece of fish and was handing it to Feng Xun when he moved away. He didn’t even get to his feet when he jumped back.","Feng Wu was surprised. “What?”","Looking around, Feng Xun saw that he was no longer being stared at. When he looked again, he saw that Boss Jun was no longer there.","“Haha, it’s nothing. I was mistaken.”","Feng Xun and Xuan Yi were travel-worn and weary from their long journey here. They didn’t even have time to rest on their way, let alone feed themselves.","By now, they were so hungry that they thought they were going to pass out.","“Aren’t you hungry? Take it.” Feng Wu wrapped a green lotus leaf around the roast fish and handed it to Feng Xun.","Feng Xun took it and breathed in deeply...","That aroma was insane!","Without thinking, he stuffed it into his mouth!","Wow —","It tasted even better than it smelled! It was maddening!","That was so delicious!","“Wow! That tastes great! Xiao Wu, you’re such an amazing cook!”","Feng Xun’s words were muffled with all the fish in his mouth, but one could tell what he wanted to say from his sparkling eyes!","Xuan Yi was also eating, but he wasn’t wolfing it down like Feng Xun. He was much more civilized.","He might eat like a refined man, but he wasn’t slower than Feng Xun by any means.","Feng Xun and Xuan Yi finished their portions in less than three seconds, and they involuntarily turned their heads toward Feng Wu.","She was still holding a moon fish about half a meter long.","“Xiao Wu —” Feng Xun cried out, and the next second, he jumped at Feng Wu.","Feng Wu said grumpily, “Don’t get too excited! I’ll give it to you!”","However, Feng Xun didn’t get it in the end, because Xuan Yi got there first.","“Damn it! Xuan Yi! How can you do that?! I didn’t know you were that type of person!”","Feng Xun was exasperated! That man was so mean!"]},{"number":1499,"title":"Chapter 1499","paragraphs":["Xuan Yi chuckled. “The devil takes the hindmost. Blame yourself for being too slow.”","“Give me back my roast fish!” Feng Xun stomped his foot in frustration.","Xuan Yi had gone through all the trouble to get it, so of course he wouldn’t give it back.","Feng Xun jumped at him in frustration!","But Xuan Yi knew Feng Xun too well to let him get what he wanted.","Before Feng Xun could get to him, Xuan Yi was already running away!","“Xuan the Second! Stop right there!” Feng Xun stomped his foot and ran after him as fast as he could!","Of course Xuan Yi wasn’t going to stop. Holding the fish, he dashed off, while Feng Xun chased after him at top speed.","There was only so much space in the campsite, and they weren’t exactly trying to keep their voices down, so they disturbed the others.","Right now, a lot of eyes were on them.","Most of the men were staying outside, while the women were in the tents. But if one looked closely, they could see that the door curtains had been lifted slightly...","The Zuo family.","Mrs Zuo and Mrs Dugu were still together. They were already sister-in-laws, and with their common enemy, the two of them were especially close at the moment.","They were still talking about how to deal with Feng Wu, when they smelled the incredible aroma. Before they knew it, they heard the hubbub outside.","“What’s that about?” Mrs Zuo asked curiously.","Mrs Zuo’s chamber maid was called Yufurong, and she had a mild temper and smiled all the time. She said merrily, “I’ll go have a look.”","She soon came back with a strange look on her face.","The two ladies darted curious looks at her, and Mrs Zuo frowned. “What’s that about?”","Yufurong stopped smiling and said quietly, “It’s Young Lord Feng and Young Lord Xuan.”","“Xuan Yi and Feng Xun? They usually behave themselves. Why are they making all that noise now? What’s going on?” Both ladies had their eyes on Xuan Yi and Feng Xun.","As a matter of fact, they weren’t the only ones. All families in the imperial capital with teenage daughters had their eyes on the two young lords.","Because they were the most ideal future husbands second only to Jun Linyuan!","Feng Xun and Xuan Yi were both promising enough to win the hearts of the mothers.","“Xuan Yi and Feng Xun? What happened? Are they having a row with someone?” Mrs Zuo asked with a frown.","Zuo Qingluan wasn’t her only daughter. There was also Zuo Qingyu.","Mrs Dugu also had three daughters.","Yufurong smiled wryly. “Young Lords Xuan and Feng are fighting each other.”","“What? Aren’t they good friends? They’re like brothers. Why would they break into a fight?”","Just then, they heard someone shouting outside.","“Xuan Yi! Stop right there! Do it, or I’m gonna kill you!” Feng Xun sounded as if he had lost his mind.","Xuan Yi was being very naughty. He stuffed the fish into his mouth as he ran.","Feng Xun couldn’t see it from behind, but when they reached a corner, he saw everything!","“Hey! Xuan Yi! How dare you eat it without my permission?! Put that fish down right now!”","Feng Xun had only tried such good roast fish once in his life, but someone else had stolen it before he could have another bite!","Xuan Yi looked over his shoulder with a resigned expression. “Is that all you can do? Shout at me?”"]},{"number":1500,"title":"Chapter 1500","paragraphs":["Feng Xun asked, “What else? Give me a hint.”","Xuan Yi didn’t have time for that. He took a large bite of the fish, chewed, and did it all over again.","The others were all astonished when they saw the way the two of them ran around.","The ladies were utterly surprised when Yufurong told them about it.","“What? Young Lord Feng and Young Lord Xuan are fighting over a roast fish?” Mrs Zuo couldn’t believe her ears.","But Yufurong nodded with a bitter smile. “That’s right; everyone heard it. Young Lord Feng is already running very fast, but he can’t catch up with Young Lord Xuan.”","Mrs Zuo looked shocked. “What’s going on? It’s as if the young lord has never tasted roast fish before.”","“But it does smell nice, and even my mouth is watering.” Mrs Dugu told the old maid next to her, “Go find out who made that fish and have them cook one for me. Quickly.”","Granny Ye was about to go, when Yufurong stopped her.","She smiled wryly. “Granny Ye, please don’t go. You won’t be able to get it.”","“What now?” Mrs Dugu was bewildered.","As the family of Empress Dugu, the Dugu family was one of the most influential families in the empire that everyone thought highly of. Why would anyone say no to such a family? Mrs Dugu smirked.","But —","“That fish was cooked by Miss Feng Wu herself.” Yufurong smiled bitterly.","Miss Feng Wu...","A hush fell over the crowd as soon as she said that name.","“She’s just all over the place!” Mrs Dugu snorted. She didn’t try to hide her disdain.","Mrs Zuo sounded discontent as well and said sarcastically, “What’s going on with the Feng clan? Why is that girl so good at seducing men?”","It was obvious that the two ladies were jealous, because they had daughters as well, and they could never get along well with Feng Xun and Xuan Yi.","While the two ladies were secretly tormented by their jealousy, the empress dowager —","Because she had insisted on going to the Senal Grassland, the empress dowager had to be on a strict diet imposed by Feng Wu.","The instructions were quite simple: the food had to be low in oil, salt, and sugar, and the empress dowager was already getting sick of it.","If she knew that Feng Wu had come up with that regime, she would probably hate her even more.","She was lying in bed and whining about her pain, when she smelled the aroma of food from outside.","It was such a unique smell that she didn’t think she had ever smelled it before.","One could only imagine how someone who was about to pass out from starvation would feel when they smelled the spicy aroma.","The old lady swallowed with difficulty. She was about to ask Granny Lan about it, when she heard footsteps outside.","“Your Majesty, Mrs Dugu and Mrs Zuo are here to see you. Do you feel well enough to see them?” Granny Lan asked.","Mrs Dugu and Mrs Zuo? Had they come with the food that was giving off that nice aroma?","The empress dowager was elated by that thought.","She sprang up from the bed and cried out, “Quickly! Invite them in!”","How thoughtful of them! the empress dowager thought to herself.","Invite them in? Mrs Dugu and Mrs Zuo exchanged surprised looks."]}]);
